bbat are not being defeated, they're being EATEN by New Sabbat.<br /> <br /> New Sabbat being 5,000 year old vampires possessing the corpses of the Neonates they let diablerize them.<br /> <br /> All under the control of the Antediluvians.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T14:47:19-07:00","id":1331660,"title":"","content":"One of the issues with the collapse of the Islamic State is accounting for all of its members and fighters. Too many have slipped through the cracks, remain terrorists, and will likely go on to create chaos and misery later.<br /> <br /> One of the issues with the collapse of the Traditional Sabbat is accounting for all of its members and fighters. Too many have slipped through the cracks, remain violent monsters, and will likely go on to create chaos and misery later. <br /> <br /> So what if the Sabbat has nominally lost Montreal - that doesn't mean any vampire residents in Montreal are safe from Sabbat attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T15:47:08-07:00","id":1331663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331660#post1331660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the issues with the collapse of the Islamic State is accounting for all of its members and fighters. Too many have slipped through the cracks, remain terrorists, and will likely go on to create chaos and misery later.<br /> <br /> One of the issues with the collapse of the Traditional Sabbat is accounting for all of its members and fighters. Too many have slipped through the cracks, remain violent monsters, and will likely go on to create chaos and misery later.<br /> <br /> So what if the Sabbat has nominally lost Montreal - that doesn't mean any vampire residents in Montreal are safe from Sabbat attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>you're missing the point,<br /> <br /> sabbat don't go to montreal for the Jyhad,<br /> they either go there to savor unlife, for self development or for pilgrimage<br /> <br /> the city was unique,<br /> it wasn't ruled by the Lasombra-Tzimisce hegemony,<br /> it wasn't in constant struggle,<br /> it wasn't under Mexico's influence,<br /> Cardinal strathcona, the one who took Montreal and re-build it, was a former Camarilla Ventrue Prince who embraced the sabbat ideology and kept it to heart to the final nights<br /> <br /> the biggest threat to the sabbat in montreal wasn't the camarilla, or the lupines or the hunters,<br /> it was their complacency, which the infernal didn't miss the chance to exploit<br /> <br /> montreal was the dream city of the sabbat,<br /> the only place they could go to and say &quot;we can do it after all&quot;<br /> <br /> now it's gone, and all their hopes with it<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T16:16:16-07:00","id":1331665,"title":"","content":"Sigh...I continue to mourn what V5 has done to my favorite aspect of Vampire the Masquerade. I don't know why the command decision was made to destroy and make an aspect of the game some people loved unplayable. I don't think I will ever understand that. Oh well, at least there's always the Golden Rule and previous editions. I just wish they hadn't so utterly destroyed the Sabbat in V5 for some reason.<br /> <br /> Mindless 1st edition nameless vampire the masquerade version of D&amp;D goblins for players to fight is two dimensional and bland. Revised made the Sabbat distinct and very deep. I enjoyed it greatly. Now...I don't even know how you make the Sabbat viable for play in V5 or if they ever will. Which is sad, as its effectively being told as a consumer and player of this game &quot;oh that thing you really liked to play? You can't in our new edition. Sorry!&quot;. I could write an essay on how deep and interesting the Sabbat of the Revised era was, but that won't change much. If your vampire game needed boogeymen there were a lot of other options besides a whole sect of vampires one could have chosen as an option. They didn't need to bring the Sabbat back to first edition IMO.<br /> <br /> Oh well :-(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T16:19:53-07:00","id":1331666,"title":"","content":"Oh..and also as someone who ran a Sabbat game in NYC for 10 years...the mention of Polonia and Sabbat claim for 9/11 (regardless if its true or not in the game world..it was unneeded) and basically making the Sabbat terrorists in V5 wasn't great either. I get the whole using the real world as basis for your modern urban fantasy game...but some things...i'd just rather not have in my game. I also have no desire to play &quot;Sabbat: the Terrorist&quot;<br /> <br /> Again all just personal taste though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T16:32:59-07:00","id":1331668,"title":"","content":"Montreal fell? Source?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T17:14:51-07:00","id":1331672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331665#post1331665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh...I continue to mourn what V5 has done to my favorite aspect of Vampire the Masquerade. I don't know why the command decision was made to destroy and make an aspect of the game some people loved unplayable. I don't think I will ever understand that. Oh well, at least there's always the Golden Rule and previous editions. I just wish they hadn't so utterly destroyed the Sabbat in V5 for some reason.<br /> <br /> Mindless 1st edition nameless vampire the masquerade version of D&amp;D goblins for players to fight is two dimensional and bland. Revised made the Sabbat distinct and very deep. I enjoyed it greatly. Now...I don't even know how you make the Sabbat viable for play in V5 or if they ever will. Which is sad, as its effectively being told as a consumer and player of this game &quot;oh that thing you really liked to play? You can't in our new edition. Sorry!&quot;. I could write an essay on how deep and interesting the Sabbat of the Revised era was, but that won't change much. If your vampire game needed boogeymen there were a lot of other options besides a whole sect of vampires one could have chosen as an option. They didn't need to bring the Sabbat back to first edition IMO.<br /> <br /> Oh well :-(</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the answer was in the interview.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're from Montreal. We love Montreal. When we were asked where we wanted to our vampire game, we decided to do Montreal.&quot;<br /> <br /> So the game is about the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Sabbat fighting for Montreal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331668#post1331668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Montreal fell? Source?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>The interview in the OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331666#post1331666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh..and also as someone who ran a Sabbat game in NYC for 10 years...the mention of Polonia and Sabbat claim for 9/11 (regardless if its true or not in the game world..it was unneeded) and basically making the Sabbat terrorists in V5 wasn't great either. I get the whole using the real world as basis for your modern urban fantasy game...but some things...i'd just rather not have in my game. I also have no desire to play &quot;Sabbat: the Terrorist&quot;<br /> <br /> Again all just personal taste though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> I'm going to state that I don't understand the incorporation of 9/11 as a Sabbat rallying cry either. Not only is it tasteless (even if they weren't responsible), it's nonsensical. The Sabbat <i>are</i> a bunch of religiously-motivated terrorists but they're not part of some greater terrorist hobby club. I don't see why an involvement in a real life massacre of the innocent would impress anyone and I'd rather not hear any arguments why it would either.<br /> <br /> It was my least favorite part of V5 and don't know why it was carried over from V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-19-2019, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T18:09:21-07:00","id":1331678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331668#post1331668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Montreal fell? Source?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So....are all the random boardgames and card games and slot machines etc.coming out all going to be canon? Because thats a whole bunch of little first run companies that could fold in the next 12 months that the IP has been farmed out to.....its going to be hell keeping track of canon for anyone wanting to touch this property.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T18:11:31-07:00","id":1331679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331678#post1331678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So....are all the random boardgames and card games and slot machines etc.coming out all going to be canon? Because thats a whole bunch of little first run companies that could fold in the next 12 months that the IP has been farmed out to.....its going to be hell keeping track of canon for anyone wanting to touch this property.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are in fact planning on making this a franchise akin to STAR WARS with a focus on incorporating material and keeping it consistent.<br /> <br /> Any ideas must go through approval at Disney, err Paradox.<br /> <br /> I'm really glad of that as it shows a loyalty to the brand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T19:21:29-07:00","id":1331690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331679#post1331679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, they are in fact planning on making this a franchise akin to STAR WARS with a focus on incorporating material and keeping it consistent.<br /> <br /> Any ideas must go through approval at Disney, err Paradox.<br /> <br /> I'm really glad of that as it shows a loyalty to the brand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a disaster in the making but I guess we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T19:46:28-07:00","id":1331692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331690#post1331690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a disaster in the making but I guess we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines being canon was the best idea they ever had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T19:55:11-07:00","id":1331694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331692#post1331692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bloodlines being canon was the best idea they ever had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what that has to do with anything but agree to disagree. It was a nice introduction to VtM but having someone go from newly embraced to city wrecking powerhouse over the course of a few nights is probably not the way to go outside of videogames. I guess using some of the NPCs in tabletop was a good way of luring in folks who had only played the video games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T20:01:24-07:00","id":1331696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331694#post1331694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Not sure what that has to do with anything</b> but agree to disagree. It was a nice introduction to VtM but having someone go from newly embraced to city wrecking powerhouse over the course of a few nights is probably not the way to go outside of videogames. I guess using some of the NPCs in tabletop was a good way of luring in folks who had only played the video games.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a great way to bring in new fans.<br /> <br /> It also reaches new audiences.<br /> <br /> Keeping it tabletop alone is needlessly confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T21:31:57-07:00","id":1331707,"title":"","content":"My point was, and is, the fall of Mexico City and Montreal does not mean the loss of all of the Sabbat - even if they exist in smaller numbers over all, pacts may still roam around doing Sabbat things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T23:32:00-07:00","id":1331729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331653#post1331653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what next? the technos are back to being evil fascists who only want to clone your family and kill the original?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wish Technocracy would become inhumane bastards from the first edition again.<br /> If that's really the case, I'll dance with joy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24623-dreamwalker","name":"Dreamwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T01:17:18-07:00","id":1331737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331707#post1331707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was, and is, the fall of Mexico City and Montreal does not mean the loss of all of the Sabbat - even if they exist in smaller numbers over all, pacts may still roam around doing Sabbat things.</div> </div> </div> </div>which isn't much, compared to the old sabbat, and compared to the new camarilla,<br /> alot of the sect's substance was removed,<br /> people have been asking for more depth for the sect, not for less<br /> <br /> going from the Vatican to roaming jyhadists is a huge downgrade even by 1st ed standards,<br /> then saying &quot;oh, but don't worry, they're still veery scaaary, I swear&quot; isn't much of a consolation, quite the opposite<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreamwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331729#post1331729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish Technocracy would become inhumane bastards from the first edition again.<br /> If that's really the case, I'll dance with joy.</div> </div> </div> </div>even if, on top of going back to being villains, they get downgraded from huge world spanning/extra dimensional spanning organization to street gangs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T03:36:15-07:00","id":1331745,"title":"","content":"As I am about to run a new game set in Montreal around the Nights of Prophecy scenario and aftermath (That I hope to run for a few years at least) this just makes it easier for me to accept that the V5 cannon isn't something I will be touching. Saves me a lot of cash to be fair... I will just stick with V20. I think that the plot of V5 has some interesting ideas, but they all seem like such sudden and vast changes to happen to vampire society in a relatively short amount of time. Not a fan. <br /> <br /> For me the Second Inquisition will remain a rumor, the Sabbat will remain in mexico, Montreal will remain as it is and the Jyhad will continue, waiting for the Gehenna that will never truly come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12180-jeevesosiris","name":"Jeevesosiris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T05:23:44-07:00","id":1331757,"title":"","content":"It's natural that some cities have changed with a new edition of the game. Just alter the setting to fit your game. Simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T06:55:13-07:00","id":1331767,"title":"","content":"I don't know...I can see a Sabbat game in 5e being very compelling. You are one of the survivors of the sect, whether you are a conscientious objector to the Gehenna War, or you are a survivor of said war, one who wasn't devoured by the elder monstrosities. Your goal is to survive in this new world, try to carve territory in cities where you once ruled, and fight off incursions from the Camarilla and Anarchs. Oh, and while you're at it...those Sabbat elder monstrosities are looking for you, too...they don't like their good little soldiers ignoring their calls.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'd play in something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T09:15:42-07:00","id":1331782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331757#post1331757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's natural that some cities have changed with a new edition of the game. Just alter the setting to fit your game. Simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evolve? Most certainly. We can see that in OPP's V5 Chicago by Night. But the original is still recognizable. I may not like how everything ended up but I can see the logical progress and understand how it got there.<br /> <br /> The rest of V5 lacks that transition and in the case like this it is needlessly jarring and offputting. Spell plague all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T09:54:16-07:00","id":1331789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331782#post1331782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evolve? Most certainly. We can see that in OPP's V5 Chicago by Night. But the original is still recognizable. I may not like how everything ended up but I can see the logical progress and understand how it got there.<br /> <br /> The rest of V5 lacks that transition and in the case like this it is needlessly jarring and offputting. Spell plague all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we've actually seen enough of the new setting to comment on that actually.<br /> <br /> There's been four supplements total and one canonical web series.<br /> <br /> Two of which were received very well.<br /> <br /> The main book also won the Origins Award for Best RPG and Fan Favorite. I feel this is closer to D&amp;D 5E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:09:37-07:00","id":1331791,"title":"","content":"Disagree with the D&amp;D 5e comparison. With D&amp;D 5e I can open the Players Handbook and play any core concept from the previous editions of Dungeons and Dragons. Core book V5, I can not run a Sabbat game. And yes, Sabbat was a core option in both the Revised Core Book and V20. Imagine if you loved playing an elf ranger in D&amp;D. Then the new edition came out, and they said &quot;oh ya elf rangers? We might get to that eventually but they are all basically dead and not even remotely what you are familiar with.&quot; That is pretty much how anyone whose favorite aspect of Vampire the Masquerade was Sabbat feels with V5. <br /> <br /> Can you golden rule it? Absolutely! Do I think V5 is an abomination worthy of an edition war? Nah, to each their own. It's not my cup of tea, and that is ok. But I feel like this James Cameron quote sums up my thoughts on this pretty well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u201cI think there\u2019s a tricky balance when you\u2019re doing a sequel, between making it fresh, surprising the audience, but not surprising them with such a swerve that they feel that it\u2019s not honoring the first film. You\u2019ve got to play to expectations, you\u2019ve got to play against expectations. And I always think that it\u2019s about answering a question that you didn\u2019t know to ask. But when they see it, it seems obvious.\u201d</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:20:03-07:00","id":1331794,"title":"","content":"I think the closest example I can think of is the fact that the Sabbat is a bit like the Galactic Empire in the Star Wars Expanded Universe. A lot of writers felt the need to start humanizing the Galactic Empire with characters like Grand Admiral Thrawn, Admiral Pellaeon, and other &quot;heroic&quot; Imperials. They even had the Galactic Empire make a peace treaty with the New Republic and become the co-stars of the Legacy comics that were the Grand Finale of the Old Expanded Universe.<br /> <br /> This was something I feel was a serious misstep and missed the point of the characterization. I had a similar feeling about the Technocracy Revised books, which continually and repeatedly tried to paint the Technocracy in the best light possible. Something I was uncomfortable with then and now realize was because, &quot;Wait, these guys are genocidal fascists. WHY are we trying to put a smiley face on them?&quot; I had a similar moment in Warhammer 40K fandom when I realized some people were sincere Emperor fanboys.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat has continually lost a huge amount of its edge as more of its details have been exposed to the public. They also have been reduced from being a terrifying and mysterious force to just stealing from the Anarch's stick (FREEEEEDOM) and stealing from the Camarilla (manipulative alien elders). Seeing them get broken up into new sects I think is a good thing for people who want to have deeper concepts.<br /> <br /> We know from CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS interview that the spiritual side of the Sabbat survives in the Church of Caine and they're going to have all of the Sabbat's ritae, secret rituals, and bizarre activities. We know the Anarchs are now going to have all of the violent freedom and pack-like war on the Camarilla. The Lasombra are now available as a Camarilla sect. We're also getting rules for the Tzimisce. I have no doubt a smaller version of the Sword of Caine will survive as well. But the Sabbat as they were envisioned, the Boogeymen of Kindred SocietyTM are coming back and that's not a bad thing.<br /> <br /> The Old Sabbat has broken up and the individual pieces are stronger for it as well as regaining some edge. No more failed wannabe Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:30:09-07:00","id":1331800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331782#post1331782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evolve? Most certainly. We can see that in OPP's V5 Chicago by Night. But the original is still recognizable. I may not like how everything ended up but I can see the logical progress and understand how it got there.<br /> <br /> The rest of V5 lacks that transition and in the case like this it is needlessly jarring and offputting. Spell plague all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given there's only been one sourcebook outside of the initial three releases, it seems premature to make judgements, at least until you see the board and video games being released set in the cities about which you're concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:32:28-07:00","id":1331802,"title":"","content":"Ya that is kinda my point hehe. You view those things as good. I do not see any of those as good things. I see them as drastic changes to the thing I really liked; which resulted in it not even remotely looking like the thing I enjoyed. <br /> <br /> Yes, in V5 they moved the Sabbat closer to 1st ed. I also don't like 1st ed sabbat. My cup of tea is Revised era/v20 Sabbat. As the editions progressed it expanded the Sabbat, it didn't take anything away. IMO that is how you should do it. Explore a concept, give it more depth. To me I do not like the choice in V5 was made to undo all that has come before and make them boogeymen vampires.<br /> <br /> I have Baali and Infernalists for that. That Sabbat used to be a deep interesting complex aspect of the game. Now, its not so much. Again to each your their own! You love the Anarch aspect of the game and think they got the shaft in Revised etc by the Sabbat. I just think, I feel the same way about V5 and would rather have said maybe we could have just had both rather sacrifice one to benefit the other.<br /> <br /> But like I said, its all just personal preference anyways, and I always have my v20/revised collection!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:47:08-07:00","id":1331805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331802#post1331802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya that is kinda my point hehe. You view those things as good. I do not see any of those as good things. I see them as drastic changes to the thing I really liked; which resulted in it not even remotely looking like the thing I enjoyed.<br /> <br /> Yes, in V5 they moved the Sabbat closer to 1st ed. I also don't like 1st ed sabbat. My cup of tea is Revised era/v20 Sabbat. As the editions progressed it expanded the Sabbat, it didn't take anything away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is where we strongly disagree. The Sabbat was continually taking away things from the Anarchs and Camarilla both. The Sabbat forced itself into their conflict and meant that the Anarchs couldn't be the number one enemy of the Ivory Tower that they were set up to be. The War of the Ages became deemphasized for Sect vs. Sect conflict. It also meant the conflict internally between the Prince and Neonates was dramatically undercut. The Sabbat were always throwing themselves into the storylines that it became very hard to run the other games as they thematically undermined a lot of the rest of the game as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why care about Humanity? Paths of Enlightenment show it's not important!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We're the only ones who care about Noddism and the Antediluvians!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sabbat just was everywhere and other parts of the game suffered for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IMO that is how you should do it. Explore a concept, give it more depth. To me I do not like the choice in V5 was made to undo all that has come before and make them boogeymen vampires. </div> </div> </div>For me, I feel like the Sabbat was great but they were just too big of a presence. If you want a game that focuses on:<br /> <br /> * Anarchs<br /> * Humanity<br /> * The evils of the Camarilla<br /> * Social interaction<br /> <br /> They just kind of pushed their way in and took up too much of the narrative space. I'm hoping the Sabbat will continue to exist but I hope in a dramatically reduced role--maybe like a 1/10th of its previous size.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat Remnant. People should be able to play the Classic Sabbat but as a faction rather than an all-consuming setting element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have Baali and Infernalists for that. That Sabbat used to be a deep interesting complex aspect of the game. Now, its not so much. Again to each your their own! You love the Anarch aspect of the game and think they got the shaft in Revised etc by the Sabbat. I just think, I feel the same way about V5 and would rather have said maybe we could have just had both rather sacrifice one to benefit the other.<br /> <br /> But like I said, its all just personal preference anyways, and I always have my v20/revised collection! </div> </div> </div>I'm of the mind that Modiphus will probably include more Sabbat information. The Sabbat is still around in Chicago by Night 5E. They weren't exterminated as some people believed them to be. The Lasombra still have half of their clan staying with them.<br /> <br /> We're really mostly dealing with rumors here.<br /> <br /> It could well be the Sabbat as know them will be fine with the Eldritch Abomination Sabbat (I'm calling them &quot;The Brood&quot; in my game after a certain group in V:TR) just as an enemy they're fighting.<br /> <br /> We just have speculation now and some lost cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:58:02-07:00","id":1331808,"title":"","content":"Ya...I also strongly disagree with half of Clan Lasombra joining the Camarilla. Again, based sorely on previous editions. But this would be a long in depth discussion. Which is not something text is great for! Its also just my opinion. <br /> <br /> It really boils down to this. We kinda just like different aspects of the game, and thats totally cool! I just wish my option of what I enjoyed was viable in a new edition of the game. As it is right now? Its not, and there is nothing on the foreseeable future that shows that is changing any time soon. Whats presented so far? Thats not the Sabbat. Its something else entirely. Which again is totally fine if thats your cup of tea, but its not mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T11:04:54-07:00","id":1331810,"title":"","content":"Eh, I love internet discussion but up to you if you're feeling to it. I want V5 to bring new things to the table, change, and awesome concepts but I also want people to be able to play their former characters.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% set against the old ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331808#post1331808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya...I also strongly disagree with half of Clan Lasombra joining the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, the Lasombra Clan Books constantly emphasize the only reason that they sided with Gratiano and the Sabbat was that he proved his superiority by killing the Lasombra Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> If the Lasombra Antediluvian was always alive and never died then, by their own Path of Night, they owe him their loyalty.<br /> <br /> Because the Lasombra are just this side of Sith Lords.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra do not side with the weak and if the Sabbat cannot back up their claims of superiority then they get nothing from the Keepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T11:08:05-07:00","id":1331812,"title":"","content":"There is also the mercenary, and basic survival, quality to the decisions. Things are going South with the Sabbat - the Lasombra have no loyalty, and so try something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T11:24:33-07:00","id":1331816,"title":"","content":"Alright, so couple of things. In Second Edition, if you look at Gratiano's Write-up in Children of the Inquisition He succeeded, the Lasombra Antediluvian died. Even by revised when they started to walk that back...it was he still dead. He gotten eaten by the Abyss when he died in his hubris attempt to take it over. The Abyss is absolutely a problem. Even in Gehenna, its not entirely the Lasombra Anti that returns. Its a lovecraftian Abyssal thing. <br /> <br /> Secondly the Path of Night is about bowing before no one. So I am not seeing how they owe their loyalty to the clan founder in that path. The level 2 sin on that path is &quot;Accepting the Superiority of another.&quot; Unless you are talking the Path of Allied Night, but core Night doesn't support that. Even by revised, paths of enlightenment in the sabbat are not common. Again just going by the books here.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra would also never bow and submit themselves to the Ventrue who are the leaders of the Camarilla. They aren't beggars and that is their entire clan's biggest rivalry dating back to the first city.. If they were going to abandon the Sabbat as failures into the Camarilla, they would have done it in 17th century when the sect was on the brink of collapse by the canon. The lasombra aren't a clan that's going to go from being on top and the leaders of a sect, to crawl to their 500 year old enemy, beg for acceptance and start at the bottom. They kinda aren't big on just giving up power like that. It just doesn't make much sense to me. The Sabbat has been on the ropes more times in the 500 years in the canon then this one time. The Lasombra, don't leave it and accept defeat (kinda the whole reason they told the camarilla off at the convention of thorns). They change it from within and mold it to their desires and needs as a clan. See all the Sabbat Civil Wars. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla already had the Lasombra Antitribu. If they wanted to expand them a bit...sure. That would have been fine. Half the Clan? Nah as written in revised etc, the Keepers made their choice centuries ago and been pretty clear they are stubborn clan. However, thats also just an option in V5 Chicago book. I am basing my opinions (and again they are just opinions) solely on the revised material. I looked at one and then looked at the other and went &quot;huh that doesn't make much sense to me&quot;, but if it does for you? Cool! But as someone who really liked the Sabbat it just was just another feeling of &quot;oh...come on&quot;. I hope that whoever and whenever a Sabbat book is published they can try to fix some of it. But I doubt that will happen. <br /> <br /> Again, which is fine. Its not for me, and that an ok thing. I can still tell all the sabbat stories I want in my previous editions. I just wish I could in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:25:19-07:00","id":1331828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331800#post1331800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given there's only been one sourcebook outside of the initial three releases, it seems premature to make judgements, at least until you see the board and video games being released set in the cities about which you're concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>A valid point and why I intend to continue supporting OPP's published works in V5 financially if not Mophidius given respective track records of the companies work in V5. Chicago by Night is a much better product then both V5 core and the camarilla/anarch books.<br /> <br /> But given that we only have had 3 releases besides the core rulebook, that is all the evidence we have as consumers to base our purchasing power on, and express our concerns about a setting and product we are deeply passionate about. <br /> <br /> Montreal by Night may come out a few years down the line, but if until then the canon has been changed to suit a board game of all things people may lose interest or hold off on purchases and use dollars elsewhere. I'm not asking for V5 and its product line to align to my personal vision of what vampire should be(though it would be nice) I'm asking for an acknowledgement of past lore and canon and when it is updated that those updates are explained and not hand waved as &quot;it's just better this way&quot;. If people didn't like the metaplot requiem would have been far more popular. <br /> <br /> Update, evolve and change as needed to fit the new vision, just give us the why and how it changed from what it was, and maybe acknowledging why it was enjoyed in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:26:21-07:00","id":1331830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331816#post1331816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so couple of things. In Second Edition, if you look at Gratiano's Write-up in Children of the Inquisition He succeeded, the Lasombra Antediluvian died. Even by revised when they started to walk that back...it was he still dead. He gotten eaten by the Abyss when he died in his hubris attempt to take it over. The Abyss is absolutely a problem. Even in Gehenna, its not entirely the Lasombra Anti that returns. Its a lovecraftian Abyssal thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one interpretation of events but as we see with the Lasombra Trilogy (starring Lucita), Gratiano never diablerized the Lasombra Antediluvian in the first place. This is as of Revised and the Lasombra Antediluvian is alive in the traditional sense. He's not a remnant of an Antediluvian like Cappadochias but an actual Antediluvian antediluvian.<br /> <br /> It may be inhuman but it wasn't &quot;smacked down.&quot; Any more than the fact Haqim now appears as a tidal wave of blood instead of a person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Night is about bowing before no one. So I am not seeing how they owe their loyalty to the clan founder in that path. The level 2 sin on that path is &quot;Accepting the Superiority of another.&quot; Unless you are talking the Path of Allied Night, but core Night doesn't support that. Even by revised, paths of enlightenment in the sabbat are not common. Again just going by the books here. </div> </div> </div>The Lasombra are all about strength and power. The Amis Noctis are built around the concept of rewarding those who have proven themselves. As stated, their entire claim to fame in the Sabbat is that they destroyed their Antediluvian. If that's not the case, then they have to reevaluate their role in the sect as well as its benefits.<br /> Mind you, I think there's more practical reasons for joining the Camarilla. The Lasombra have always had a large unspoken number of Ancilla and smarter than your average shovelhead types who have wanted to accumulate mortal power and influence--things they can't do as long as the Sword of Caine is looming over their heads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra would also never bow and submit themselves to the Ventrue who are the leaders of the Camarilla. They aren't beggars and that is their entire clan's biggest rivalry dating back to the first city. </div> </div> </div>Over in the Ventrue Revised book, they point out the Lasombra and Ventrue didn't have anty rivalry whatsoever until the Anarch Revolt. They try to pretend that but the two of them got along just fine in Rome. The idea there's an eternal emnity between the two Clans is silly as the Ventrue hated the Brujah and then hated the Tzimisce but the Lasombra thing is a product of the Anarch revolt.<br /> <br /> Next, now is the best time ever for the Lasombra to join because the Ventrue are crippled with the death of their Founder and so many lost to the Beckoning. They no longer have their soldiers in the Gangrel or Brujah while the Tremere Pyramid has been decapitated of its headstone. They have the chance to conquer the Camarilla from within and there's a very good argument that any Anarch PCs should support Camarilla membership for the Lasombra just because they'll tear the place up from the inside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they were going to abandon the Sabbat as failures into the Camarilla, they would have done it in 17th century when the sect was on the brink of collapse by the canon. The lasombra aren't a clan that's going to go from being on top and the leaders of a sect, to crawl to their 500 year old enemy, beg for acceptance and start at the bottom. They kinda aren't big on just giving up power like that. It just doesn't make much sense to me. The Sabbat has been on the ropes more times in the 500 years in the canon then this one time. The Lasombra, don't leave it and accept defeat (kinda the whole reason they told the camarilla off at the convention of thorns). They change it from within and mold it to their desires and needs as a clan. See all the Sabbat Civil Wars. </div> </div> </div>I should note that it's almost certainly the 50% of the Lasombra who have the most to gain from defection to the Camarilla that are probably the ones defecting. It's probably not the Cardinals, Gehenna Crusaders, and Pricius who are defecting. Its almost certainly those who see a chance for advancement and power in a new sect that has lost a staggering amount of its former leadership. The Lasombra is full of Keepers who have been denied Resources, Influences, Fame, Allies, and Contacts because the Sword of Caine disdains mortal influence.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, by contrast, exalts in it. It's a chance for Luis Santiago or Maria the Ancilla to become incredibly wealthy when they were previously forced to do nothing but ritae and hanging with their pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla already had the Lasombra Antitribu. If they wanted to expand them a bit...sure. That would have been fine. Half the Clan? Nah as written in revised etc, the Keepers made their choice centuries ago and been pretty clear they are stubborn clan. </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to also note the Lasombra have always been bitterly disappointed with the Sabbat. The Lasombra control of the sect has never been as firm or as welcome as they have claimed it has been. The four Sabbat Civil Wars can basically be summarized as, &quot;The antitribu hate the Lasombra for being assholes that think they should lead.&quot; Each one of the Civil Wars has forced the Lasombra to continue to give ground in leadership positions and recognition with another one happening just before the events of V5.<br /> <br /> After the Gehenna Crusade disaster, the Second Inquistion, and the discovery of the Ante being alive--I can see why some decide to go with greener pastures. At the end, the Lasombra have no loyalty to anyone but themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, which is fine. Its not for me, and that an ok thing. I can still tell all the sabbat stories I want in my previous editions. I just wish I could in V5. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate you taking the time to discuss the issue with me. You raise some very good points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:33:20-07:00","id":1331832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331828#post1331828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A valid point and why I intend to continue supporting OPP's published works in V5 financially if not Mophidius given respective track records of the companies work in V5. Chicago by Night is a much better product then both V5 core and the camarilla/anarch books.<br /> <br /> But given that we only have had 3 releases besides the core rulebook, that is all the evidence we have as consumers to base our purchasing power on, and express our concerns about a setting and product we are deeply passionate about.<br /> <br /> Montreal by Night may come out a few years down the line, but if until then the canon has been changed to suit a board game of all things people may lose interest or hold off on purchases and use dollars elsewhere. I'm not asking for V5 and its product line to align to my personal vision of what vampire should be(though it would be nice) I'm asking for an acknowledgement of past lore and canon and when it is updated that those updates are explained and not hand waved as &quot;it's just better this way&quot;. If people didn't like the metaplot requiem would have been far more popular.<br /> <br /> Update, evolve and change as needed to fit the new vision, just give us the why and how it changed from what it was, and maybe acknowledging why it was enjoyed in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's an unusual amount of disdain here for the medium that Montreal by Night's update is receiving its position. &quot;A board game&quot; is a weird thing to have an issue with when our hobby, tabletop games are descended from board gaming with Warhammer 40K having been something that has successfully had the two work side by side for decades. One of the things that Paradox Interactive has expressed the desire to do is move the franchise out of just tabletop roleplaying games into other mediums. Board games are as popular as ever, we have card games, video games (alas the mobile game had to be taken down because of--well, it's developer), and hopefully TV shows as well as movies.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the fact that Montreal by Night is being altered by...people from Montreal...has a bit of importance here.<br /> <br /> They chose to make it there because it's their home city, same for the people doing Bloodlines 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:45:34-07:00","id":1331833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331789#post1331789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we've actually seen enough of the new setting to comment on that actually.<br /> <br /> There's been four supplements total and one canonical web series.<br /> <br /> Two of which were received very well.<br /> <br /> The main book also won the Origins Award for Best RPG and Fan Favorite. I feel this is closer to D&amp;D 5E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a 50% success rate is a successful margin, nor does Paradox given the shake up. I'm trying not to hate on V5, I'd just prefer it doesn't compound on past mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:47:48-07:00","id":1331834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331833#post1331833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think a 50% success rate is a successful margin, nor does Paradox given the shake up. I'm trying not to hate on V5, I'd just prefer it doesn't compound on past mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you define mistakes.<br /> <br /> Especially as, again, it won two Origins awards and has been extremely successful. My issues are with presentation, others issues are with the content itself.<br /> <br /> What do you see as mistakes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-20-2019, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:50:20-07:00","id":1331835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331832#post1331832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like there's an unusual amount of disdain here for the medium that Montreal by Night's update is receiving its position. &amp;quot;A board game&amp;quot; is a weird thing to have an issue with when our hobby, tabletop games are descended from board gaming with Warhammer 40K having been something that has successfully had the two work side by side for decades. One of the things that Paradox Interactive has expressed the desire to do is move the franchise out of just tabletop roleplaying games into other mediums. Board games are as popular as ever, we have card games, video games (alas the mobile game had to be taken down because of--well, it's developer), and hopefully TV shows as well as movies.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the fact that Montreal by Night is being altered by...people from Montreal...has a bit of importance here.<br /> <br /> They chose to make it there because it's their home city, same for the people doing Bloodlines 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair points. I play 40k and enjoy board games. And if the board game was in it's own little pocket universe where it didn't affect canon lore I wouldn't take issue. If it was in an another city that didn't have a by night book, no problem.<br /> <br /> I'd just prefer not to have established well received canon changed for the basis of a board game which may or may not sell at all without some rationale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:52:49-07:00","id":1331836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331835#post1331835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair points. I play 40k and enjoy board games. And if the board game was in it's own little pocket universe where it didn't affect canon lore I wouldn't take issue. If it was in an another city that didn't have a by night book, no problem.<br /> <br /> I'd just prefer not to have established well received canon changed for the basis of a board game which may or may not sell at all without some rationale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, it's not exactly Monopoly here.<br /> <br /> The board game seems to be a narrative heavy miniatures chronicle with a predefined story. From what I'm reading, it's actually more like a Chronicle that just so happens to have Pregens and miniatures. Which is a very different Beast than something that doesn't have a story but just a background.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:03:40-07:00","id":1331839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is one interpretation of events but as we see with the Lasombra Trilogy (starring Lucita), Gratiano never diablerized the Lasombra Antediluvian in the first place. This is as of Revised and the Lasombra Antediluvian is alive in the traditional sense. He's not a remnant of an Antediluvian like Cappadochias but an actual Antediluvian antediluvian.<br /> <br /> It may be inhuman but it wasn't &quot;smacked down.&quot; Any more than the fact Haqim now appears as a tidal wave of blood instead of a person. </div> </div> </div>Oh this is certainly just an interpretation, they never come out and say &quot;Oh its 100% just the Lasombra Antediluvian&quot; they leave it a mystery. I simply just prefer the &quot;Nah the 3rd gens are full of hubris and can get themselves killed because of it. &quot; instead of &quot;lol they just always win&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lasombra are all about strength and power. The Amis Noctis are built around the concept of rewarding those who have proven themselves. As stated, their entire claim to fame in the Sabbat is that they destroyed their Antediluvian. If that's not the case, then they have to reevaluate their role in the sect as well as its benefits.<br /> Mind you, I think there's more practical reasons for joining the Camarilla. The Lasombra have always had a large unspoken number of Ancilla and smarter than your average shovelhead types who have wanted to accumulate mortal power and influence--things they can't do as long as the Sword of Caine is looming over their heads. </div> </div> </div>The friends of the night are also a very small portion of the clan. Gratiano destroyed their power base and structure making them little more then an old boys club. If you wanted just the friends of the night to defect to the camarilla? Sure, I could see that argument. However, that certainly is not half the clan. More realistically its 20-30 lasombra. As for accumulating mortal power and influence in the sabbat? They absolutely can and have. In the Sabbat you have the Order of St. Blaise that does just that. Among the Lasombra you have the Kings and Queens of Shadow. I think one of the often missed aspects of the sabbat genre is the sabbat isn't just one thing. Its a confederation of factions and ideals. Each vying for what they believe the sabbat should be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Over in the Ventrue Revised book, they point out the Lasombra and Ventrue didn't have anty rivalry whatsoever until the Anarch Revolt. They try to pretend that but the two of them got along just fine in Rome. The idea there's an eternal emnity between the two Clans is silly as the Ventrue hated the Brujah and then hated the Tzimisce but the Lasombra thing is a product of the Anarch revolt.<br /> <br /> Next, now is the best time ever for the Lasombra to join because the Ventrue are crippled with the death of their Founder and so many lost to the Beckoning. They no longer have their soldiers in the Gangrel or Brujah while the Tremere Pyramid has been decapitated of its headstone. They have the chance to conquer the Camarilla from within and there's a very good argument that any Anarch PCs should support Camarilla membership for the Lasombra just because they'll tear the place up from the inside. </div> </div> </div>Ya...thats kinda unreliable narrator though. There are more instances in more books about the lasombra ventrue rivalry then there are to oppose it. I still don't buy the Lasombra bending knee. If they were coming in as conquerors? Maybe. But they aren't. They are coming in bottom of the totem pole, begging to be saved, offering themselves up on a plater to the 500 year old enemy. I'm sorry, it just doesnt make much sense to me and seems like a wild left turn for the clan, or a means to make the lasombra playable in V5 when you aren't planning on doing Sabbat any time soon. So one had to find a way to make it fit. Still feels like a square peg round hole situation to me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should note that it's almost certainly the 50% of the Lasombra who have the most to gain from defection to the Camarilla that are probably the ones defecting. It's probably not the Cardinals, Gehenna Crusaders, and Pricius who are defecting. Its almost certainly those who see a chance for advancement and power in a new sect that has lost a staggering amount of its former leadership. The Lasombra is full of Keepers who have been denied Resources, Influences, Fame, Allies, and Contacts because the Sword of Caine disdains mortal influence.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla, by contrast, exalts in it. It's a chance for Luis Santiago or Maria the Ancilla to become incredibly wealthy when they were previously forced to do nothing but ritae and hanging with their pack. </div> </div> </div>Right but again, it also doesn't. The propaganda line is a disdain for mortals and masquerade. The reality is they need mortals and a masquerade just like everyone else. Again, see the order of st blaise as an example. also what chances for advancement? You are talking about a sect based on the concept of age, centuries spent gathering power and influence, and rarely giving it up. Hence the Anarchs problem with them. The Lasombra are not going to advance any time soon or gain any key positions of authority in the Camarilla. They start at the bottom, with no centuries built power base, no allies just old enemies and rivals and hope someone throws them a bone one day? Thats not the clan Lasombra I know. But again, just based off one's own interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's important to also note the Lasombra have always been bitterly disappointed with the Sabbat. The Lasombra control of the sect has never been as firm or as welcome as they have claimed it has been. The four Sabbat Civil Wars can basically be summarized as, &quot;The antitribu hate the Lasombra for being assholes that think they should lead.&quot; Each one of the Civil Wars has forced the Lasombra to continue to give ground in leadership positions and recognition with another one happening just before the events of V5.<br /> <br /> After the Gehenna Crusade disaster, the Second Inquistion, and the discovery of the Ante being alive--I can see why some decide to go with greener pastures. At the end, the Lasombra have no loyalty to anyone but themselves. </div> </div> </div>I mean by the Guide to the Sabbat the Lasombra make up 1/4 of the entire sect. Thats a large number, rivaled only by the Tzimisce (who I suspect will also be leaving the sabbat in V5). The Lasombra are Darwinist. They support the civil wars of the sabbat because they believe it makes it stronger. Iron Sharpens Iron. Look at the end result of the Civil Wars in 1998. The sect was never a great threat to the Camarilla. Then out of no where they took the entire east coast in a crusade..because no one expected it. If anything that embodies lasombra ideology and proves their beliefs right. Again Id argue if the Lasombra faith was so weak to cause the clan to break and join their 500 year long enemy..they would have done that a long time ago. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate you taking the time to discuss the issue with me. You raise some very good points. </div> </div> </div>Right back at you! I could go on forever on this, pull up books, give page numbers, and quotes. But over text its often difficult to convey what you really mean and I also not looking for any sort of debate lol. Because again, it all boils down to personal preference. What you like about V5 Sabbat isn't wrong. Its perfectly fine. I think we are looking at the same coin but two different sides. My point is your option is viable in V5, and sadly mine isn't. Using just the books as are of course and ignoring Golden Rule and all that. But ya, good discussion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:06:50-07:00","id":1331841,"title":"","content":"Well if you don't wish to discuss further, I understand. I appreciate you taking the time to discuss what you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:10:04-07:00","id":1331842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331834#post1331834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on how you define mistakes.<br /> <br /> Especially as, again, it won two Origins awards and has been extremely successful. My issues are with presentation, others issues are with the content itself.<br /> <br /> What do you see as mistakes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Origin awards have much effect on sales and success. I hadn't heard of them until I saw that they won on these forums. No one in my gaming groups knows about them. And the 2017 winner for best RPG was a game called &quot;No thank you, Evil!&quot; By Monte Cook. I haven't seen that in any stores or recommended by anyone I know.<br /> <br /> As for what I view as the mistakes, it as follows.<br /> <br /> 1. Lack of explanation for lore changes. (Theo Bell shooting Hardestadt, the Beckoning, a bunch of mortals killing the tremere council of 7(why would all 7 paranoid bastards ever be in one physical location?)etc. The list goes on. Sure you can give explanations for your table or golden rule, but then why put it in at all? They had enough pages for unused concept art from a defunct MMO production and larper photos but not enough to put in what matters.<br /> <br /> 2. If we wanted to play requiem, we would have played and bough requiem. The push to make the Camarilla Invictus lite, the anarchs the carthians, the sabbat split into the 7 and the cult of belial and clan tremere split between Ordo Dracula and circle of the crone was kind of offputting. <br /> Shake the setting up sure, give it new ideas, great. Don't copy paste from Requiem.<br /> <br /> 3. Trying to go back to some perfect 1st edition glory days when revised and V20 where the most successful and widely played.<br /> <br /> 4. Layout - Zomg the core book is horribly designed and hiring Ericcson was a huge mistake, one I'm glad was rectified. He was intensely passionate but passion is not enough to make a successful product. <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall this is all water on the bridge. V5 CbN is well written and designed. I will continue to support V5. I'd just like to see it bypass mistakes, and trying to tie all product lines as canon without the support network leads me to think they are trying to do what DC has done and rush forward to one universe without playing the groundwork that marvel was willing to put in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:13:01-07:00","id":1331844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well if you don't wish to discuss further, I understand. I appreciate you taking the time to discuss what you did. </div> </div> </div>Oh its not that, I just think we will agree to disagree on it. Minus the Sabbat becoming Terrorists. We can both agree that wasn't needed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T17:42:41-07:00","id":1331891,"title":"","content":"I think the big problem with the Sabbat in revised was, and why they change it now, that it eventually was just big pile of cool ideas the writers had, mushed together into one thing, but if you started thinking about it to much, it didn't make a whole lot of sense. It almost feels like the writers just got the directive at some point \u201chave an idea about monstrous vampires? vampiric religions? Conspiracies? Just put it in the Sabbat...<br /> <br /> For example it always made more sense to me, that the Lasombra as a Clan would belong to the Camarilla. Especially compered with some of the Camarilla Clans the Lasombra seemed way more fitting there. In a more extreme sense, it never made much sense to me that any \u201cClan\u201d would belong to the Sabbat, that Sabbat should all regard themselves as antitribu. After all, they are Cains progeny and don't stand in awe of some antediluvian. The Sabbat should be pack politics where the Camarilla is Clan politics.<br /> <br /> I love the Sabbat because I love the ideas collected within the sect. I hate it because it makes no sense for them all to be in the same sect. What VtM needed from the get go, was more factions or sects to accommodate all those ideas.( As requiem did)<br /> But I also agree that to just crowbar it now, to late. If you say you develop VtM make it VtM and don't try to make Requiem with serial numbers filed of instead.<br /> <br /> But the one thing I very much like about V5(setting wise) is the emphasis again on Camarilla, not nice people, and certainly not the heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","user":"nobby","date":". 08-21-2019, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T18:59:57-07:00","id":1331898,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of what people think of the upcoming CULTS OF THE BLOOD GOD will depend on how much they reveal the Church of Caine. I think they may well be a more player-friendly version of the Sabbat rather than the Lancea Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Agata Starek seems to be the most Sabbat-esque non-Sabbat ever and might be meant to show why so many defected to the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T09:58:11-07:00","id":1331975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331800#post1331800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given there's only been one sourcebook outside of the initial three releases, it seems premature to make judgements, at least until you see the board and video games being released set in the cities about which you're concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well not really, Sabbat was fully playable in the first year of the 2nd edition (The Sabbat Player's guide was relased in 1992, same year of the corebook), in the first year of the Revised and in the first year of V20.<br /> That we have to wait, and that after one year we still have no news about the sabbat, and probably will have no further until 2020, it's a clear proof that Sabbat, which was once one of the core elements of the setting, is not core anymore. Which is pretty bad for Sabbat fan.<br /> <br /> Especially because it totally came out of the Blue.<br /> <br /> Last time we saw them the Sabbat just won the Crusade, conquered all of the East Coast, was pressing in the south and was sieging San Diego. The main problem the Sabbat had was the mounting civil war and the defection of the Assamite from the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> Now we have no civil war (the entire main plot-line of the Sabbat in revised just vanished, we just have hint that maybe De Polonia might had the upper hand, but we really knows nothing about something that was this central in the setting) and the Sabbat was just basically magically teleported (basically on the moon, since we know nothing about what it's happening there and we have very little info about the middle east in modern nights) and basically we know nothing until further notice.<br /> <br /> It's really a Spell-Plague like solution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-21-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:05:01-07:00","id":1331979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331805#post1331805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is where we strongly disagree. The Sabbat was continually taking away things from the Anarchs and Camarilla both. The Sabbat forced itself into their conflict and meant that the Anarchs couldn't be the number one enemy of the Ivory Tower that they were set up to be. The War of the Ages became deemphasized for Sect vs. Sect conflict. It also meant the conflict internally between the Prince and Neonates was dramatically undercut. The Sabbat were always throwing themselves into the storylines that it became very hard to run the other games as they thematically undermined a lot of the rest of the game as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why care about Humanity? Paths of Enlightenment show it's not important!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We're the only ones who care about Noddism and the Antediluvians!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sabbat just was everywhere and other parts of the game suffered for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For me, I feel like the Sabbat was great but they were just too big of a presence. If you want a game that focuses on:<br /> <br /> * Anarchs<br /> * Humanity<br /> * The evils of the Camarilla<br /> * Social interaction<br /> <br /> They just kind of pushed their way in and took up too much of the narrative space. I'm hoping the Sabbat will continue to exist but I hope in a dramatically reduced role--maybe like a 1/10th of its previous size.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat Remnant. People should be able to play the Classic Sabbat but as a faction rather than an all-consuming setting element.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm of the mind that Modiphus will probably include more Sabbat information. The Sabbat is still around in Chicago by Night 5E. They weren't exterminated as some people believed them to be. The Lasombra still have half of their clan staying with them.<br /> <br /> We're really mostly dealing with rumors here.<br /> <br /> It could well be the Sabbat as know them will be fine with the Eldritch Abomination Sabbat (I'm calling them &quot;The Brood&quot; in my game after a certain group in V:TR) just as an enemy they're fighting.<br /> <br /> We just have speculation now and some lost cities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ehm... Anarch vs Camarilla was core buisness only in first edition, which means from 1991 to mid 1992. From 1992 to 2018 the core buisness was the sect war.<br /> <br /> Yeah I'm happy that now you are happy because you niche content has become main content, but most players of vampires never gave a fuck about Anarch vs Camarilla. Most players of Vampires joined when the main thing was Camarilla vs Sabbat. <br /> <br /> <br /> So it's not like the Sabbat had hijacked the setting. The Sabbat was THE (or at least one of the THE) setting. The setting that stood 26 years out of 27 years of pubblication.<br /> <br /> Basically the Core thematics have become a niche, and the niche has become the core thematic. Sure if you are 1ed fan it's nice, but most vampire's fan are not 1ed fan : they are 2nd ed fan, Revised fun, V20 fan, and not because reasons, just because Vampire was Camarilla/Sabbat centric for the 95% of it's time.<br /> <br /> You are happy that the 5% got his spot back. Too bad for the remaining 95%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-21-2019, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:28:25-07:00","id":1331982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331832#post1331832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's an unusual amount of disdain here for the medium that Montreal by Night's update is receiving its position. &quot;A board game&quot; is a weird thing to have an issue with when our hobby, tabletop games are descended from board gaming with Warhammer 40K having been something that has successfully had the two work side by side for decades. One of the things that Paradox Interactive has expressed the desire to do is move the franchise out of just tabletop roleplaying games into other mediums. Board games are as popular as ever, we have card games, video games (alas the mobile game had to be taken down because of--well, it's developer), and hopefully TV shows as well as movies.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the fact that Montreal by Night is being altered by...people from Montreal...has a bit of importance here.<br /> <br /> They chose to make it there because it's their home city, same for the people doing Bloodlines 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A couple of points:<br /> I do like me some boardgames. But I have a limited amount of time and money. I do fully expect a game line of primarily pen-and-paper RPGs to keep their metaplot-relevant updates to, well, pen-and-paper books. I don't want to have to hunt down the various Expanded Universe products, as cool as they ,might be (I used to be a VTES player among other things), to hunt down the things that are, or are not, declared canon by whoever holds final sway over that (Paradox, maybe?). Keeping up with the metaplot got bad enough when it was only RPG books and fiction books, now I have to parse other stuff too.<br /> I consider myself a semi-dedicated player/ST to vampire. I did bounce off V5 hard, but in general, I try to keep up. A relative newcomer will have ever more issues navigating the plot mire.<br /> <br /> Them being from Montreal will ensue that Montreal in game seems real to Montreal in our reality, which is a very good thing indeed. I do recall the travesty that was Dark Ages' &quot;history&quot; and &quot;lore&quot;, especially in Eastern Europe. However, Montreal By Night does not take place in our reality, it takes place in VTM's reality. So ensuring continuity with that (aka not making the Sabbat an afterthought) comes before ensuring that Habitat 67 or Gay Village are located where they should be.<br /> <br /> That aside, Montreal By Night is my favourite Sabbat book, and I will mourn the loss of the Dark Christianity aspect of the Sabbat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:32:49-07:00","id":1331983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331975#post1331975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time we saw them the Sabbat just won the Crusade, conquered all of the East Coast, was pressing in the south and was sieging San Diego. The main problem the Sabbat had was the mounting civil war and the defection of the Assamite from the Black Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a different definition of &quot;won&quot; than I do since the Sabbat lost their capital and stronghold in North America. The loss of New York was greater than all the gains of conquering the East Coast. V20 also had the Sabbat lose Washington D.C. in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. It's also established the Sabbat have been pushed back by Jan Pieterszoon over the course of the past ten to fifteen years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now we have no civil war (the entire main plot-line of the Sabbat in revised just vanished, we just have hint that maybe De Polonia might had the upper hand, but we really knows nothing about something that was this central in the setting) and the Sabbat was just basically magically teleported (basically on the moon, since we know nothing about what it's happening there and we have very little info about the middle east in modern nights) and basically we know nothing until further notice.<br /> <br /> It's really a Spell-Plague like solution. </div> </div> </div>No, the Gehenna Wars are detailed in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. They have been going on since the War on Terror at the end of Revised for a decade. The Sabbat Civil War plot didn't vanish, it just happened before the new edition's events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:37:41-07:00","id":1331984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331979#post1331979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehm... Anarch vs Camarilla was core buisness only in first edition, which means from 1991 to mid 1992. From 1992 to 2018 the core buisness was the sect war.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also a major focus of Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah I'm happy that now you are happy because you niche content has become main content, but most players of vampires never gave a fuck about Anarch vs Camarilla. Most players of Vampires joined when the main thing was Camarilla vs Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you speak for all of us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's not like the Sabbat had hijacked the setting. The Sabbat was THE (or at least one of the THE) setting. The setting that stood 26 years out of 27 years of pubblication. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat were the focus of:<br /> <br /> 1. The Clan Novels<br /> 2. Their books<br /> <br /> The Giovanni Chronicles, Transylvania Chronicles (which included the Sabbat as an option but were focused on the Anarch Revolt as a whole), and Gehenna books had nothing to do with the Sabbat. There was also the Kuei-Jin invasion that received an entire year of development.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat don't actually occupy that much space in the game even if they had more than arguably their fair share.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically the Core thematics have become a niche, and the niche has become the core thematic. Sure if you are 1ed fan it's nice, but most vampire's fan are not 1ed fan : they are 2nd ed fan, Revised fun, V20 fan, and not because reasons, just because Vampire was Camarilla/Sabbat centric for the 95% of it's time.<br /> <br /> You are happy that the 5% got his spot back. Too bad for the remaining 95%. </div> </div> </div>So, your basic argument is that the Anarchs were unimportant because of writer fiat and we should suck it up but now that the Sabbat are less important by writer fiat, that's terrible.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/049/787/No-Country-for-Old-Men_Tommy-Lee-Jones_Josh-Brolin_Javier-Bardem_9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:53:18-07:00","id":1331986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331982#post1331982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of points:<br /> I do like me some boardgames. But I have a limited amount of time and money. I do fully expect a game line of primarily pen-and-paper RPGs to keep their metaplot-relevant updates to, well, pen-and-paper books. I don't want to have to hunt down the various Expanded Universe products, as cool as they ,might be (I used to be a VTES player among other things), to hunt down the things that are, or are not, declared canon by whoever holds final sway over that (Paradox, maybe?). Keeping up with the metaplot got bad enough when it was only RPG books and fiction books, now I have to parse other stuff too.<br /> I consider myself a semi-dedicated player/ST to vampire. I did bounce off V5 hard, but in general, I try to keep up. A relative newcomer will have ever more issues navigating the plot mire.<br /> <br /> Them being from Montreal will ensue that Montreal in game seems real to Montreal in our reality, which is a very good thing indeed. I do recall the travesty that was Dark Ages' &quot;history&quot; and &quot;lore&quot;, especially in Eastern Europe. However, Montreal By Night does not take place in our reality, it takes place in VTM's reality. So ensuring continuity with that (aka not making the Sabbat an afterthought) comes before ensuring that Habitat 67 or Gay Village are located where they should be.<br /> <br /> That aside, Montreal By Night is my favourite Sabbat book, and I will mourn the loss of the Dark Christianity aspect of the Sabbat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely valid issues. One of the things that depresses me is the fact that it's just not financially viable right now for me to take a trip with the family down to Disneyworld in order to visit Galaxy's Edge. I'm also having trouble keeping up with all the new products for the Star Wars franchise's new canon. I think that in the new age of social media, though, that it's much easier to get the stories and information about things like the plotline of CHAPTERS than it would be in 2004, though.<br /> <br /> I'm also of the mind that CHAPTERS seems to have been made by people who love Montreal by Night and will incorporate all of that lore into the setting. The Sabbat have suffered badly in the city but that doesn't mean their loss of control isn't a valid story of itself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:55:56-07:00","id":1331987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331979#post1331979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehm... Anarch vs Camarilla was core buisness only in first edition, which means from 1991 to mid 1992. From 1992 to 2018 the core buisness was the sect war.<br /> <br /> Yeah I'm happy that now you are happy because you niche content has become main content, but most players of vampires never gave a fuck about Anarch vs Camarilla. Most players of Vampires joined when the main thing was Camarilla vs Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it's not like the Sabbat had hijacked the setting. The Sabbat was THE (or at least one of the THE) setting. The setting that stood 26 years out of 27 years of pubblication.<br /> <br /> Basically the Core thematics have become a niche, and the niche has become the core thematic. Sure if you are 1ed fan it's nice, but most vampire's fan are not 1ed fan : they are 2nd ed fan, Revised fun, V20 fan, and not because reasons, just because Vampire was Camarilla/Sabbat centric for the 95% of it's time.<br /> <br /> You are happy that the 5% got his spot back. Too bad for the remaining 95%.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most players joined because of the Sabbat? Really? Do you have data to back up that assertion?<br /> <br /> I've been playing Vampire since 1991, and not once...not even ONCE...did I play in a Sabbat game. The ST's I gamed with used the Sabbat like V5 uses them...as a group of Vampiric boogeymen. Despite your assertions, they were not THE default of the setting.<br /> <br /> Your baseless hyperbole aside, we can see that the developers are looking at releasing books and stories that deal with two of the three major sects (Camarilla and Anarch), which has always been the focus of the gameline whenever a new edition was released (1st, 2nd, and revised...V20 was almost all inclusive).<br /> <br /> Give it time...the V5 developers will release more info. I'm sure they don't want to saturate the market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24575,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","user":"Raunalyn","date":". 08-21-2019, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:06:04-07:00","id":1331988,"title":"","content":"I should also note I think that the Sabbat <i><b>should</b></i> have a Player Option.<br /> <br /> The Brood (what I call the Gehenna War Sabbat) can be the Threat Null of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Classic Sabbat can be a minor sect carrying on business like it's 1999.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been playing Vampire since 1991, and not once...not even ONCE...did I play in a Sabbat game. The ST's I gamed with used the Sabbat like V5 uses them...as a group of Vampiric boogeymen. Despite your assertions, they were not THE default of the setting. </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines only gained them as a playable option via Fan Mods.<br /> <br /> I think Anarchs and Cammies will also be the focus of Bloodlines 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:34:55-07:00","id":1331991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331984#post1331984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was also a major focus of Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which until some years ago it wasn't even canon and it's not a pubblication and it was developed by Troika's Brian Mitsoda and not by White Wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm glad you speak for all of us. </div> </div> </div>Since you assume that generally speaking people were interested in Anarchs, yeah, why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat were the focus of: </div> </div> </div>1. The Clan Novels<br /> 2. Their books [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> From 1992, book about the Sabbat or where the Sabbat is a consistent part of the content<br /> Caine's Chosen<br /> Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat<br /> The Players Guide to the Sabbat<br /> Clanbook: Tzimisce<br /> Clanbook: Lasombra<br /> Clanbook: Lasombra Revised<br /> Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised<br /> Montreal by Night<br /> Mexico City by Night<br /> <br /> <br /> And so on<br /> <br /> Anarch entries since 1992...<br /> <br /> Anarch Cockbook<br /> Los Angeles By Night<br /> Guide to the Anarchs<br /> <br /> Even in mixed entries like<br /> <br /> <br /> Midnight Siege (all about sect wars, nothing about the Anarchs<br /> <br /> <br /> Sins of the Blood (half of the book is about Paths)<br /> <br /> Guide to the Camarilla (Constant theme all over the book)<br /> <br /> New York By Night (Most of the book is about the aftermath of the battle with the Sabbat)<br /> <br /> Archon and Templars, (half of the book is about the Templars)<br /> <br /> Children of the Nights, (Sabbat characters? 21 out of 60. Anarchs? Maybe a couple?)<br /> <br /> World of Darkness 1ed and 2nd ed (Just saying, in World of Darkness 2nd we have 209 references about the Sabbat, and only 76 about the anarchs)<br /> <br /> Counsel of Primogen (62 Sabbat references, against 32 for the Anarchs)<br /> <br /> Washington City by Night (Sabbat is the main problem of Vitel and the war with the Sabbat is one of the main theme of the Book, while the Anarch are pretty much nobody.<br /> <br /> Kindred Most Wanted, out of 13 characters 4 are Sabbat (Angelo, Petaniqua, Dylan Bruce, Valerius Maior), 1 is Anarch (Germaine)<br /> <br /> And so on and so on and so on...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Giovanni Chronicles,Transylvania Chronicles (which included the Sabbat as an option but were focused on the Anarch Revolt as a whole), </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should check again. Especially Son of the Dragon and the Dragon Ascendant. Where do you think Goratrix thing happened?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gehenna books had nothing to do with the Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like Gehenna has always been so secondary for the Sabbat!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was also the Kuei-Jin invasion that received an entire year of development. </div> </div> </div>Eh yeah, 36 page in Night of the Prophecy, no shit!The other entries are KoTE supplements San Francisco by night doesn't even have an anarch character, and yet it has a Sabbat Pack<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, your basic argument is that the Anarchs were unimportant because of writer fiat and we should suck it up but now that the Sabbat are less important by writer fiat, that's terrible.<br /> </div> </div> </div>No my argument is that the Sabbat has been a core theme for 26 years and the anarchs for 1. So in the economy of the setting and in its identity the Sabbat is way more important than the Anarch ever were. So it's much a greater loss to lose the Sabbat than to lose the Anarch, since the anarch are not (or at least they weren't until V5) a core trait of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:39:00-07:00","id":1331992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331991#post1331991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No my argument is that the Sabbat has been a core theme for 26 years and the anarchs for 1. So in the economy of the setting and in its identity the Sabbat is way more important than the Anarch ever were. So it's much a greater loss to lose the Sabbat than to lose the Anarch, since the anarch are not (or at least they weren't until V5) a core trait of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the Camarilla and Anarchs were included in the *core* books in 1st edition, 2nd edition, and revised, but not the Sabbat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:42:30-07:00","id":1331993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331987#post1331987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most players joined because of the Sabbat? Really? Do you have data to back up that assertion?<br /> <br /> I've been playing Vampire since 1991, and not once...not even ONCE...did I play in a Sabbat game. The ST's I gamed with used the Sabbat like V5 uses them...as a group of Vampiric boogeymen. Despite your assertions, they were not THE default of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good for you table! Which by the way is not the entire world. The anarchs were side-lines as soon as 1992 and the big success (even in market terms) of the game-line came with 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your baseless hyperbole aside, we can see that the developers are looking at releasing books and stories that deal with two of the three major sects (Camarilla and Anarch), which has always been the focus of the gameline whenever a new edition was released (1st, 2nd, and revised...V20 was almost all inclusive).<br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> Emh, no. In 2nd edition they already so much ancillary that you had the Player Guide to the Sabbat in the same year of the corebook (1992), while you had to wait for the Anarch Cockbook (1993) .<br /> They were so ancillary that in Revised they were a footnote at the end of the Guide to the Camarilla, while the Sabbat had a full guide in less than a year from the Corebook , while Guide to the Anarchs was published in 2002, years and years later.<br /> <br /> They were so ancillary that the Sabbat had 2 City Books since 2nd edition, the Camarilla 3, and the Anarchs...1. And none in Revised era.<br /> <br /> So ancillary that the Anarch got only 1 real supplement about them in Revised (Guides to the Anarchs) while the Sabbat had many and was a main focus in the mixed ones.<br /> <br /> So ancillary that out of 60 characters in Children of the Night one third is Sabbat, and maybe a couple are anarchs.<br /> <br /> So ancillary that this is the final judgment of Justin Achilli about the Anarchs<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MERE ANARCHY?<br /> So much for the Camarilla and Sabbat \u2014 now for the<br /> anarchs. Hitherto, the anarchs achieved little\u2026 which, for<br /> them, was sort of the point of being an anarch. Having overthrown<br /> a prince or two to establish the Anarch Free State,<br /> they didn\u2019t want to establish a new order. Coteries and lone<br /> vampires did whatever the hell they wanted, only uniting to<br /> resist attempts to force them into one sect or another. Their<br /> primitive council in Los Angeles had no power and most<br /> members didn\u2019t show up for meetings.<br /> In 2000, the West Coast anarchs learned that freedom<br /> requires more than a leather jacket, a nose ring and a Motley<br /> Cr\u00fce haircut. The \u201cNew Anarch Movement\u201d is dead \u2014 along<br /> with many of the anarchs themselves </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-21-2019, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:47:25-07:00","id":1331994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331993#post1331993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good for you table! Which by the way is not the entire world. The anarchs were side-lines as soon as 1992 and the big success of the game-line came with 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Data? Your table is not my table, nor is it the entire world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331993#post1331993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emh, no. In 2nd edition they already so much ancillary that you had the Player Guide to the Sabbat in the same year of the corebook (1992), while you had to wait for the Anarch Cockbook (1993) .<br /> They were so ancillary that in Revised they were a footnote at the end of the Guide to the Camarilla, while the Sabbat had a full guide in less than a year from the Corebook , while Guide to the Anarchs was published in 2002, years and years later.<br /> <br /> They were so ancillary that the Sabbat had 2 City Book since 2nd edition, the Camarilla 3, and the Anarchs...1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the Sabbat were always excluded from the core books and the anarchs weren't, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24575,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","user":"Raunalyn","date":". 08-21-2019, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T11:51:39-07:00","id":1331995,"title":"","content":"Look, it seems as if maybe I might be sounding a little antagonistic; that is not intentional. I tend to reply to hyperbole in this way, and message boards are notoriously bad with depicting tone.<br /> <br /> My point is that we don't know what's going to come for the Sabbat...we are only 4 books into this particular line. I'm sure the developers have something planned for the Sabbat (also why I think that the Player's Guide will include clans that are normally associated with the Sabbat). All I am saying is give it time before you start with the hatred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:07:02-07:00","id":1331997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331995#post1331995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, it seems as if maybe I might be sounding a little antagonistic; that is not intentional. I tend to reply to hyperbole in this way, and message boards are notoriously bad with depicting tone.<br /> <br /> My point is that we don't know what's going to come for the Sabbat...we are only 4 books into this particular line. I'm sure the developers have something planned for the Sabbat (also why I think that the Player's Guide will include clans that are normally associated with the Sabbat). All I am saying is give it time before you start with the hatred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seriously irritated they cancelled the Sabbat book to replace it with the Second Inquisition book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:09:05-07:00","id":1331999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331997#post1331997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm seriously irritated they cancelled the Sabbat book to replace it with the Second Inquisition book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering if it required some serious re-writes like the Camarilla book did. Maybe there was some subject matter that needed to be revised to avoid controversy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:28:50-07:00","id":1332005,"title":"","content":"Another thought is that they want to do the Sabbat RIGHT!<br /> <br /> Let's look at the state of things for the other 2 sects. Both have significant changes (The Cammies now have the Banu Haquim, they've kicked out the Brujah, and they've started accepting the Lasombra and have become even more of a Good ol' Vamps club that requires elite invitation to; the anarchs now include the Brujah and the Ministry and have taken most of the territory that has been abandoned by the Sabbat and Cammies who went to the Middle East). So, it is safe to theorize that the Sabbat are also going to be changed in some way.<br /> <br /> My speculation? Those Sabbat who weren't turned into six-packs by their elders will return and immediately start shoring up their defenses to fight against the things that are going to be coming out of the Gehenna wars. We're talking old, terrible horrors that the Sabbat clans have been fighting for the past 20 years...I don't think that the Middle East will be able to contain them for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:52:08-07:00","id":1332009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331999#post1331999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm wondering if it required some serious re-writes like the Camarilla book did. Maybe there was some subject matter that needed to be revised to avoid controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldnt want my book about religious fanatics, mass murderers, doomsday cultists, fanatical crusaders, (from a human perspective) immoral detached deviants, etc to be controversial in any way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:05:35-07:00","id":1332016,"title":"","content":"it'd be nice if the devs would at least tell us what they're planning for the sabbat, good or bad,<br /> so we can stop holding our breaths and decide if we should be hype or just forget about the sabbat<br /> <br /> you know, I'd actually be fine with 1st ed sabbat at this point,<br /> IF it's really 1st ed sabbat,<br /> cause right now, it doesn't even feel like 1st ed sabbat,<br /> cause, at least 1st ed sabbat had the lasombra/Tzimisce overlords, they had territories that others would consider as no-go zones etc,<br /> now they just feel like roaming murderhobos,<br /> maybe they're closer to Requiem's Belial's Brood (or was it VII?), but certainly not sabbat<br /> <br /> just tell us pls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T16:42:27-07:00","id":1332040,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted a 4th Sabbat Civil War. This allows a more localized Sabbat, one city might have the old hierarchy with an Archbishop, bishops, etc. Another might have a nomadic pack, that rejects the old Sabbat order. and another might have a small, hidden coven masquerading as Anarchs or Camarilla and secretly meeting to conduct their rites, etc. I think the occultation of the Sabbat is an excellent development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24582-ruthven","name":"Ruthven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T18:53:56-07:00","id":1332052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1332009#post1332009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldnt want my book about religious fanatics, mass murderers, doomsday cultists, fanatical crusaders, (from a human perspective) immoral detached deviants, etc to be controversial in any way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, that the Sabbat book was home to several pages about how the<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_dress\" target=\"_blank\"> dress is gold, </a>and that is just unforgivable. Unforgivable! <br /> <br /> Joking aside, I doubt there is anyway to do a Sabbat book that will not be controversial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T19:13:37-07:00","id":1332054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1332052#post1332052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look, that the Sabbat book was home to several pages about how the<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_dress\" target=\"_blank\"> dress is gold, </a>and that is just unforgivable. Unforgivable!<br /> <br /> Joking aside, I doubt there is anyway to do a Sabbat book that will not be controversial.</div> </div> </div> </div>People threw a fit over the implication the Brujah have Neo-Nazis in them.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Sabbat cannonically have those <i>actual</i> Nazis working for it and I mean original characters too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T06:42:34-07:00","id":1332116,"title":"","content":"From the moment Montreal By Night first saw print, the Sabbat\u2019s appeal, to me, was the fantasy of these creatures trying to forge a genuinely posthuman society for themselves - even with all the hypocrisies that come with it, like the clashes between the generations within the sect. At least these people weren\u2019t going to waste their immortality by hating themselves for what they are. For reasons having to do with being a closeted twentysomething (I\u2019m out and fortysomething now) from a strict religious background, the Sabbat\u2019s core fantasy of striving to accept your real self, finding a community where you belong anyway, and then maybe becoming something more spoke to me in a way that Anarchs Versus Cammie Princes couldn\u2019t. <br /> <br /> Without getting into the accuracy of claims about player demographic estimates, I\u2019m definitely on the side of players who found the game world interesting because of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-22-2019, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T08:52:55-07:00","id":1332136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1332116#post1332116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the moment Montreal By Night first saw print, the Sabbat\u2019s appeal, to me, was the fantasy of these creatures trying to forge a genuinely posthuman society for themselves - even with all the hypocrisies that come with it, like the clashes between the generations within the sect. At least these people weren\u2019t going to waste their immortality by hating themselves for what they are. For reasons having to do with being a closeted twentysomething (I\u2019m out and fortysomething now) from a strict religious background, the Sabbat\u2019s core fantasy of striving to accept your real self, finding a community where you belong anyway, and then maybe becoming something more spoke to me in a way that Anarchs Versus Cammie Princes couldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Without getting into the accuracy of claims about player demographic estimates, I\u2019m definitely on the side of players who found the game world interesting because of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you found a part of the game that appealed to you. It sounds a bit like why I've found the Anarchs so appealing that they don't submit to the people who stand above them but resist. That you don't have to conform to society but will be able to have each other's backs no matter what. For me, the Sabbat have been a source of many fascinating stories as well. I'm a religious and mystical person in life with a great love of archaeology as well as history. So the Noddism and religious bent of the Sabbat have always had a certain lure to me.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I've always also felt the Sabbat was best used as a cautionary tale too. They exist to show what happens when you abandon the pretence of being anything than a hateful monster who kills people because why not. They have an important role in the game but that's to demonstrate &quot;But for the Grace of Caine go I.&quot;<br /> <br /> You need the Sabbat to demonstrate the Blood Eagle done to a single mother and nailing someone to a tree &quot;just because.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T09:24:36-07:00","id":1332137,"title":"","content":"Hello Onyxpath Forum!<br /> It\u2019s Thomas from Flyos Games, the board game company developing Vampire the Masquerade CHAPTERS.<br /> <br /> After reading your comments, I think I\u2019ll add my input as well.<br /> Not to discuss the Sabbat timeline (Since we have a NDA) but to provide more details about the Chapters project.<br /> <br /> Vampire the Masquerade CHAPTERS is a narrative board game, taking place in Montreal.<br /> The starting idea of the project was that <b>it is hard, complicated to play VTM as much as we want</b>. We\u2019ve been playing for 18 years and friends still cancel, snow keep falling every winter (especially in Montreal), and adults are busy/exhausted with life.<br /> <br /> We wanted to buy a box where everything was inside, ready to use: a storyteller (we tried, it\u2019s hard to fit), different character archetypes, a well-written and credible story where choices impact the events, and the possibility to play alone or with friends.<br /> Unfortunately, that game does not exist\u2026 yet.<br /> <br /> So, we decided to use our board game experience (Kiwetin and Until Daylight) and our undying passion for Vampire the Masquerade to create the best project we ever worked on. It would be a bridge between board game and RPG, an introduction for some, something easy to play for new players and hard to master for passionate fans.<br /> <br /> <b>Why Montreal? </b><br /> Because we live in it and things have changed in 20 years in Montreal.<br /> The city has never been so full of joy, arts, happy humans, construction and corruption.<br /> WoD, the world and kindred organization have changed as well, and humans are more determined than ever before to find scapegoats.<br /> Sabbat never hide their glory, it makes sense that in the context of the second inquisition, the Sabbat was the first to fall.<br /> <br /> <b>We won\u2019t divulge anything</b> about the story, the plot, or things that may happen in the game.<br /> However, we can say that we are doing our utmost best to create the best game, story and campaign possible.<br /> <br /> <b>What we can do is talk about our commitment,</b> the team of illustrators, writers, translators, scenarists, miniatures sculptor, graphic designers and game designers, we have gathered.<br /> No compromise on the quality, no shortcut.<br /> <a href=\"https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/277025/vampire-masquerade-chapters\" target=\"_blank\">https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/...erade-chapters</a><br /> <br /> <b>What we can promise you is that we are relentless.</b><br /> Matthew Dawkins is a Lore consultant and is taking an active role in the development of the project.<br /> We are meeting players at the GenCon, listening to their ideas, concerns and taking notes.<br /> We are inviting VTM players to our HQ to test the prototype, give their insight and feedback<br /> <br /> <b>What we can do is include you:</b><br /> We posted a first post in Onyx Path forum 8 minutes after our press release (April 4th 2019, at 00:08am) asking for anyone willing to participate, give their feedback and help us create the best RPG in a box to come to the Facebook group to help us. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302440-vampire-the-masquerade-chapters-announced\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ters-announced</a><br /> <br /> <b>What we offer you is a place at the table</b> to give your input, help us understand how you play, what you like, what in your opinion should we add and would make Vampire the Masquerade Chapters the best RPG in a box possible:<br /> <br /> Come help us: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/VampiretheMasqueradeCHAPTERS/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/Vamp...eradeCHAPTERS/</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24826-thomas","name":"thomas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T10:24:53-07:00","id":1332146,"title":"","content":"Thanks for showing up and sharing that info!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T10:27:39-07:00","id":1332149,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Thanks for posting Thomas. Looking forward to how it turns out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T16:32:21-07:00","id":1377600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331794#post1331794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the closest example I can think of is the fact that the Sabbat is a bit like the Galactic Empire in the Star Wars Expanded Universe. A lot of writers felt the need to start humanizing the Galactic Empire with characters like Grand Admiral Thrawn, Admiral Pellaeon, and other &quot;heroic&quot; Imperials. They even had the Galactic Empire make a peace treaty with the New Republic and become the co-stars of the Legacy comics that were the Grand Finale of the Old Expanded Universe.<br /> <br /> This was something I feel was a serious misstep and missed the point of the characterization. I had a similar feeling about the Technocracy Revised books, which continually and repeatedly tried to paint the Technocracy in the best light possible. Something I was uncomfortable with then and now realize was because, &quot;Wait, these guys are genocidal fascists. WHY are we trying to put a smiley face on them?&quot; I had a similar moment in Warhammer 40K fandom when I realized some people were sincere Emperor fanboys.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat has continually lost a huge amount of its edge as more of its details have been exposed to the public. They also have been reduced from being a terrifying and mysterious force to just stealing from the Anarch's stick (FREEEEEDOM) and stealing from the Camarilla (manipulative alien elders). Seeing them get broken up into new sects I think is a good thing for people who want to have deeper concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've read across other of your posts across the forum on the theme of Sabbat and some other elements of the game, I have an impression that, with all due respect, you are tilting at windmills here. I really don't understand the need to dehumanize Galactic Empire, WH40K either side, traitors or loyalists, Sabbat of 2ed/Revised either if you are playing the game. It feels like, as some of us have noticed, the main problem of V5 is that too much is being dragged from the mindsets and opinions of out-of-characters.<br /> <br /> Technocracy are genocidal fascists. Imperium of Man is comprised of genocidal fascists. Galactic Empire are genocidal fascists. Ehm, in regards to respective settings, who isn't? I am not going to start a holy war of out-of-game beliefs here. People like to explore extreme things - personalities, emotions, ideologies, themes, views, derangements. The very thing which is the biggest attraction of Vampire games, to me, and I believe I am not alone in this, is the deviance, the alternative, the exploration of extremities of human condition and emotion. How you can do it when you judge a darker part of the setting as unconditionally bad? what about the others then, are Camarilla or Anarchs attitudes towards mortals in any way of human perception and understanding, valid? When you're embraced, you are an abomination of natural order, a thing which has to literally and figuratively feed off other people to sustain itself. How come one of that kind is worse than the other, from the human-centered pov? The human of WoD which is not quite darker than the real one, does not distinguish a camarilla monster from sabbat monster, they are equally mostrous to us. Why do we delve into that viewpoint at all, or, even worse, make it a Final Instance of what is good or bad concerning the setting?<br /> Let's not play the game at all then, or try out the Hunter and find yourself as another monster this time bereft of any 'supernatural' excuse - becoming Dexter/Punisher of WoD was solely your choice and there is no greater power or fate to blame.<br /> <br /> Going back to the concepts of mentioned factions across various settings, I believe to be fair is to dig deeper into what it means for someone to be a serious, genuine 'Emperor fanboy'. I would say that the rule of thumb across any mature roleplay is that immersing yourself that deep into in-game factions and characters should not be accepted as a valid MO. If we are talking about the factions across settings though, why would we call Imperium genocidal fascists in terms of said setting? To a human in WH40k, I'd argue, both Chaos and Imperium present too almost equally bad options but the rest are even worse (I'd argue that probably Tau' way is the 'nominally' best, but again, that's from my viewpoint of 2k human raised in the spirit of rationality, tolerance and human-centric attitude). Humanity itself is such a multi-faceted concept that I don't want to write a novel here about it, just raise a rhetorical quesiton of why we are taking one specific approach to it as a centerpoint of the whole setting? Saying Galactic Emire, Sabbat etc. are just evil, with all due respect, as one-dimensional a statement as one can do especially in regards to such a complex setting as WoD. Why wouldn't authors try to humanize them? Why should they necessarily dehumanize them? Why should we stay on the 'brighter' side without looking at - and through the eyes of - the darker one? Do we have so few examples of deumanizing one side and humanizing the other in real world history? The characters on both sides are humans after all. Even mutated Chaos cultists or the most robzombiesque Sabbat are or were humans and still carry that seed in themselves however vehemently they deny it. Are humans unconditionally good? I believe there's an answer in the question itself. Should we try to explore all sides of what it means to be a Human in the games and, what is the point of this discussion, allow authors to explore all sides of it in game books even though the eyes of the Other, including the Monster? definitely. The only question I would raise in that regard is that with how much class and delicacy you do it? (some parts of V5 did it completely abandoning finesse and delicacy for cheap edginess, you know what I'm talking about, and it was one huge fail).<br /> It was always a core underlying theme, a meta, if you will, of the whole WoD, not just the Vampire - &quot;only becoming a Monster allows one to understand what it means and what it takes to be a Human&quot;.<br /> <br /> People join various services and structures with questionable reputations not because they are evil, or want to. History knows countless atrocities committed by people believing they do the right thing to benefit other people not just themselves. Order of Reason was created to save humanity, and Technocracy's purpose is still that, at least a declarative one. Imperium protects humankind with whatever means it finds necessary, most of the time failing horribly. Not a fan or adept of SW but I believe Galactic Empire is not about 24/7 human sacrifices - for some reason some people believe in advantages and dismiss the disagvantages, of authoritarian regimes, they did in the past, they do now, why it shouldn't happen in future? Me, a descendant of communists, always questioned my predecessors' beliefs but always wondered what took it for them to keep going? To persevere in the face of brutal, horrible Soviet reality? They did not do bad things themselves but they surely realized of what kind of regime they were part of. How they coped with it? What made them strive and hope for the best and raise their kids and grandkids to be intelligent, delicate humans in the face of the worst of their reality? What it takes to carry noblebright in your heart when it's grimdark surrounding you? How that noblebright gets warped after decades of surviving said reality? I found my answers to these questions and to be honest, darker aspects of WoD, among many other things, only helped me in that quest.<br /> <br /> Now, going more specific, not sure why the Sabbat are mischaracterized since the deviation from 1ed depiction of boogeymen. Just recently, Justin Achilli posted in his twitter a picture displaying the main three factions in the game as a three legged chair - Anarchs as Peasants, Camarilla as Aristocracy, Sabbat as Clergy. I think of it as the most valid simplification on the sects' identities. Getting Sabbat out of the Clergy spot into something between all three was a bad choice imo which happened in Revised. Across all sects, Sabbat was at the forefront of going 'other way', of abstaining from playing mortals and with mortals instead trying to evolve, transcend, and explore the 'new' world deeper instead of focusing on the material. The setting itself ecouraged it - being a supernatural thing that can kill any bully in the street or manipulate any banker into giving a credit card number, but being killed by a mere touch of sunlight kind of forces you into a certain predisposition. Shifts your perspective, to put it mildly. The Sabbat was a way to ponder on the nature of vampirism much more thoroughly and deeply than other sects, in my opinion, and it was dark enough to play it properly - primarily through trauma. The PTSD theme, to me, is vital to understanding what Sabbat is and how it should be played and characterized. What happens when a whole sect is an embodiment of the circle of violence and abuse? How do individuals cope with it? At what point one breaks, and if breaks at all? How much of personal will and drive is needed to try and turn things around you into another direction when you and your closest ones are small parts of one military/religious machine? Moving most of the Sabbat from exploring Paths in 2ed to being 70% just around Humanity 4 at permanent was definitely a poor choice, imo. That's what made them 'darker Camarilla' and 'more violent Anarchs' and tore out the huge chunk of their appeal. Combine it with Lasombra' Godfather caricature and shovelheads' Rob Zombie movies and you see why it's a bad choice when you aimed at playing a spiritual pillar of vampiric world.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote, I genuinely despised some of Russian and other EE players mocking V5 for retconning the worst things which came out since it's start and the whole &quot;HAHA they dont have balls HAHA&quot; imageboard-y bullshit. Here, I am trying to find that golden middle between &quot;going too far&quot; and &quot;not going at all&quot;. With the latter, which I believe you propse, we can simply throw out one of the three pillars of VtM out of the window turning the remaining Sabbat crusaders into Diablo 3 minibosses.<br /> <br /> Going with Gehenna war being simply a feast for Ancients is not good either - quoting Achilli again, of course there are huge chances you and your coterie/pack are manipulated by terrifying methuselahs somewhere out there; there are still some chances you can be lucky by breaking or avoiding their strings and taking the fight to your puppetmaster(s). Without that romantic tiny chance, the setting, the metaplot turns into something predictable, cynical and dull (just as planned all along). What if Gehenna crusade succeeds and the Sabbat are not possessed but make a triumphant return? What if they return not as infernalists but as scholars and prophets (still monsters by human POV, mind you), toughened but enlightened through trauma by the worst of both human and vampiric worlds and striving to elevate Cainites and oppose Ancients in some new unexpected ways? Just a thought, but I'd be very disappointed if they go full braindead Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Maybe that gap between 1ed mysterious threat and revised' freak circus is what made you consider Sabbat due a redesign in v5. Probably we agree on that. It's just me that found the most interesting themes in the sect in the 2ed and in the Montreal by Night specifically. For me, this book was the turning point and my interest of VtM and WoD overall went from casually scrolling through rulebooks to zealously (hah) devising believable backgrounds and stories, drawing NPC portraits and reading through tomes in order to create my own chronicles full of secrets to uncover. It was also my first Sabbat book and everything Revised I read after felt like a huge step backwards, although I realized that the authors decided, for reasons unknown, to make Mexico/NY a mainstream Sabbat, and Montreal - a rare deviation, an anomaly in the lost boys' club. The purge of Path of Harmony followers is an epitome of that stupid turn. Sad, and if you ask me, unnecessary, but maybe that clears up things how I and some other players viewed the sect and what it should have been.<br /> <br /> Another thread on this forum, BJD Metaplot diary, had your post on the Montreal chapter and one part of it actually made me compose this wall of text. You mentioned that Lucita is looking for friends and camaraderie in the Sabbat, and good luck to her with that. Ironically, the Montreal book explores this part of Sabbat identity better than any other. The packs are disciplined, organized and driven. Just a couple of examples:<br /> <br /> Two Lasombra love each other to the point of one violating his beliefs and risking his own status to protect and vouch for the other despite her weakness and obsession with her mortal relative.<br /> Gargoyle Loyalist is enthralled by a bishop and can't control herself because of the feelings; out of sheer camaraderie he, follower of path of power, violates it's tenets in order to go out of his way and help the 'weak' to join another pack and find company; things are worsened because the bishop is Ultra and the pack he sends Gargoyle to is of Loyalists, so he's strengthening his political rival but ultimately believes it's all for the good of the sect, falling behind on his own Path. His packmates, Black Hand members, know of this sacrifice and respect him all the more because of it.<br /> Another cainite sent to kill said bishop joins his pack instead after a night of the duel with that bishop during which he made the assasin question his beliefs through conversation mixed with combat; a secret is that the bishop has no vinculum bonds over the assasin - after that duel he follows the bishop out of genuine respect.<br /> A former archbishop repents and abandones his infernalist ways trying to save his childe and the city while realising it's almost impossible in the face of mistrust, outright hostility and the other supernatural forces at play. Still he perseveres while constantly tempted to turn back to his hellish powers and reclaim everything he lost with brute force.<br /> A pack takes in an accidentally embraced cainite who proved his worth in combat, even if it goes against Sabbat tradition and he's not True Sabbat - they value his tenacity and personal strength and he is ready to die for his new family.<br /> <br /> From human POV, all of them are unapologetic murderous monsters with their hands in blood up to elbows who see themselves far above humans while refusing (to varying degree) to recognize how close their passions and emotions are to human ones. Some do, most don't, but the smartest of them realize they are mere pawns in the game with their souls at stake and that it's their Paths and spiritual evolution which can only save them; there is no going back to Humanity - only those around you are the only solace and light in the pitch blackness which is Montreal's supernatural world, and even they hide their own secrets some of which are darker than others. Again, the rest of them wallows in spiritual rot at the heart of the city, oblivious to corruption surrounding them. Political chess, scholarly rivalry, personal vendettas form the web which entangles them while the city is quickly going to hell. The sheer challenge of untying that web and saving what is worth - and defining what even is worth - saving is what appeals to me in the Sabbat since said book. Not sure why humanizing vampires of Sabbat, basically transitioning Humanity dilemmas and relations with mortals to vampire-only community in such a way is worse than portraying them as mindless boogeymen, or worse than humanizing Camarilla elders or Anarch gangsters. Quoting yourself, Humanity in WoD is just another, 6th kind of monstrous species and I totally agree with it.<br /> The city has it's own Litany of Blood, a ritual you mentioned Beckett at in BJD; you see a 'typical Sabbat thing'. I see a holy - for participants - ritual honoring the huge effort, loss and dedication of those who put their unlives for their common cause; a tradition of honoring your dead has a trace throughout human history and appeals to the better parts of human nature. What other Vampire sect or society unironically and diligently preserves the memory of it's fallen members for centuries? Or, while we are at it, what other vampire society has so many members willingly putting themselves on the line for some higher purpose? Sabbat was designed to explore human themes uncovered by Anarch-Prince dichotomy under angles untried before, and it's kind of sad it's all got obscured for you, among others, by shallow savagery of Revised shovelheads.<br /> Adding a theme of Bigger Scarier Than Thou in the face of self-obsessed Nietzschean vampires makes the whole story believable; Metathiax and his pawns were that in MbN, Methuselahs, Ancients and occasional possessed kindred or even other cainites could fit that role in V5. Not to mention the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> The book has enough examples of things Lucita is looking for which are almot non-existant in other parts of vampiric society, for many reasons not only Vaulderie, but of course, without reading it, the only book which pays Sabbat due in revised is probably Caine's Chosen. Perhaps she should be trying to become a Seraph instead of regent<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Black Hand also breaks the commonly expressed narrative of spiritual, sophisticated Sabbat automatically becoming Camarilla-like - Camarialla never had it's own CIA/GRU and vampiric warfare should not always resemble '30 days of night' nonsense - new Sabbat should be probably fighting more like Bourne or Alejandro from Sicario.<br /> <br /> Now, with an attempt to wrap it all up, golden rule and agree to disagree still stand, however I felt the need to oppose things you mentioned as taken for granted or seen as part of mainstream direction the authors wanted to go all along - I never found VtM and WoD overall to be a didactic setting telling us what's certainly bad and what's certainly good and play to 'correct the world' but offering an opportunity truly unique to roleplaying industry to see, discuss, play and decide for ourselves, raising the toughest questions and looking for answers in ourselves and in others. Sabbat, and especially MbN, was one of the things really good for that purpose.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your time if reading this, and again, no offense intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 03-31-2020, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T18:13:23-07:00","id":1377615,"title":"","content":"I don't know how locations are being handled in the game, but I hope that bolt hole Beckett got crammed into, in BJD, makes an appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T21:43:24-07:00","id":1377649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331834#post1331834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on how you define mistakes.<br /> <br /> Especially as, again, it won two Origins awards and has been extremely successful. My issues are with presentation, others issues are with the content itself.<br /> <br /> What do you see as mistakes?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it has a large enough advertising budget to buy an award..that is literally all any award ever shows.<br /> <br /> It focuses on the most boring things about VtM (Anarch temper tantrums, seriously Anarchs have never been interesting, will never be interesting and now they are stealing parts of the Sabbat stick...and ruining them). The interesting thing was the philosophical war at the heart of the Sabbat Vs Camirilla war, the fundamentally different way of keeping the beast chained, the Camirilla enforcement of Path of Humanity, for a homogeneous ideological outlook.vs the Sabbats multiple paths connected via Vaulderie and Ritae approach, V5 has forgotten: their are no good vampires, everyone is irredeemably evil, their are no heroes, only monsters, and now the system, at a base level cannot support that conflict, is ramming the Anarchs down everyone's throats, and has castrated the elders as viable threats...I have a hard time believing the Devs liked or had played previous editions, know they have, but I am left wondering why, when V5 pours so much hatred and scorn on what made the previous editions good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-01-2020, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T00:00:31-07:00","id":1377672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377649#post1377649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it has a large enough advertising budget to buy an award..that is literally all any award ever shows.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just silly.<br /> <br /> People love V5, especially thanks to all the free advertising and not so free advertising on Twitch. It's selling like hotcakes and people vote them in. It had a lot of controversies and people can justifiably critique it all they want but it's hugely popular. People who pretend otherwise are in denial. Detractors need to get over their claim its unpopular that flies in the face of every bit of evidence. It doesn't mean you can't criticize it but that its a financial and critical failure is just bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It focuses on the most boring things about VtM (Anarch temper tantrums, seriously Anarchs have never been interesting, will never be interesting and now they are stealing parts of the Sabbat stick...and ruining them). The interesting thing was the philosophical war at the heart of the Sabbat Vs Camirilla war, the fundamentally different way of keeping the beast chained, the Camirilla enforcement of Path of Humanity, for a homogeneous ideological outlook.vs the Sabbats multiple paths connected via Vaulderie and Ritae approach, V5 has forgotten: their are no good vampires, everyone is irredeemably evil, their are no heroes, only monsters, and now the system, at a base level cannot support that conflict, is ramming the Anarchs down everyone's throats, and has castrated the elders as viable threats...I have a hard time believing the Devs liked or had played previous editions, know they have, but I am left wondering why, when V5 pours so much hatred and scorn on what made the previous editions good. </div> </div> </div>Unsurprisingly, I believe the Sabbat have never been and never could be as interesting as the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T02:32:37-07:00","id":1377693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377672#post1377672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just silly.<br /> <br /> People love V5, especially thanks to all the free advertising and not so free advertising on Twitch. It's selling like hotcakes and people vote them in. It had a lot of controversies and people can justifiably critique it all they want but it's hugely popular. People who pretend otherwise are in denial. Detractors need to get over their claim its unpopular that flies in the face of every bit of evidence. It doesn't mean you can't criticize it but that its a financial and critical failure is just bullshit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, I believe the Sabbat have never been and never could be as interesting as the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never made a claim about sales afaik, it is selling, I made a claim about awards, to whit they are all corrupt, never seen one I trusted.<br /> <br /> What do people like about the Anarchs btw? I genuinely don't get them, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:23:27-07:00","id":1377711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377672#post1377672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unsurprisingly, I believe the Sabbat have never been and never could be as interesting as the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I tried to do my best to explain why it is. I believe both to be crucial parts of the Vampire identity and covered my favorite part. I'd like to know why that part is or should be used as a cautionary tale only and justified why it should not. Talking about the game's direction and the canon not the homebrew here - I always liked the main line no matter how many things I'd changed in it; it's always interesting to see the continuation of that same plot and the living world envisioned by it's creators and professionals. I suppose you feel the same way towards VtM but looks like we are not into a discussion here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:29:51-07:00","id":1377712,"title":"","content":"I like the Sabbat and the Anarchs. I think they both represent different aspects of the vampiric condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:45:08-07:00","id":1377714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377693#post1377693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never made a claim about sales afaik, it is selling, I made a claim about awards, to whit they are all corrupt, never seen one I trusted.<br /> <br /> What do people like about the Anarchs btw? I genuinely don't get them, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarch have their appeal. It's a rebellion against both kinds of establishment, it's a way to forge the third way, it's a sect closest to humanity even if they exemplify and accentuate both best and worst about the modern world; it's a chance to take a deeper look at the nature of any political movement, of fiery ideologies of any (yes of ANY) kind and take it up to eleven with the help of the supernatural surroundings. It's also undisputably the best way to explore the generational conflict and see how centuries of experience fare against adaptability and closeness to mortals, being attuned to the rapid evolution of society in modern nights arguably more than any other group of supernaturals.<br /> In a way, it's opposite of what I've described as the core theme of the Sabbat. It's members believe themselves, to varying degrees of honesty, to be far from humans, not necessarily superior, just detached and shedding away their mortal skin, sometimes literally, and the consience of the human while in fact the things which hold the sect together are unjustifiably human at core. <br /> Anarchs take 180 on it and believe themselves to still be humans, or close to humans, while refusing to realise they are humans no more and their closeness to them is going to disappear in a century, or even earlier. It's a fiery denial of the inevitable that has it's own, tragic and romantic, appeal. &quot;The night is young&quot;, after all.<br /> <br /> These are my points of view in regards to Anarchs whom I alway found second most interesting after Sword of Caine, the Ivory Tower being the least. Mainly because it was one huge default and a status quo, their goals and values the pettiest. Now, the V5 Camarilla is what it should be, imo - I like their take on it and the fact that they now stand for something. Being honest about the protection of the elders and Methuselahs makes them much more credible now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T05:08:17-07:00","id":1377717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377714#post1377714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anarch have their appeal. It's a rebellion against both kinds of establishment, it's a way to forge the third way, it's a sect closest to humanity even if they exemplify and accentuate both best and worst about the modern world; it's a chance to take a deeper look at the nature of any political movement, of fiery ideologies of any (yes of ANY) kind and take it up to eleven with the help of the supernatural surroundings. It's also undisputably the best way to explore the generational conflict and see how centuries of experience fare against adaptability and closeness to mortals, being attuned to the rapid evolution of society in modern nights arguably more than any other group of supernaturals.<br /> In a way, it's opposite of what I've described as the core theme of the Sabbat. It's members believe themselves, to varying degrees of honesty, to be far from humans, not necessarily superior, just detached and shedding away their mortal skin, sometimes literally, and the consience of the human while in fact the things which hold the sect together are unjustifiably human at core. <br /> Anarchs take 180 on it and believe themselves to still be humans, or close to humans, while refusing to realise they are humans no more and their closeness to them is going to disappear in a century, or even earlier. It's a fiery denial of the inevitable that has it's own, tragic and romantic, appeal. &amp;quot;The night is young&amp;quot;, after all.<br /> <br /> These are my points of view in regards to Anarchs whom I alway found second most interesting after Sword of Caine, the Ivory Tower being the least. Mainly because it was one huge default and a status quo, their goals and values the pettiest. Now, the V5 Camarilla is what it should be, imo - I like their take on it and the fact that they now stand for something. Being honest about the protection of the elders and Methuselahs makes them much more credible now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I don't like those themes about them, but at least I can see why some one else could. As I said previously, the two sides of the same coin that is the Sabbat Vs Cam war interests me way more than the Anarchs do (if the Anarchs actually earned that title, by being a highly structured paramilitary group of permanent revolution, that purged those that don't tow the line and generally acted like historic anarchists, maybe I would like them more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T07:40:50-07:00","id":1377730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377717#post1377717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I don't like those themes about them, but at least I can see why some one else could. As I said previously, the two sides of the same coin that is the Sabbat Vs Cam war interests me way more than the Anarchs do (if the Anarchs actually earned that title, by being a highly structured paramilitary group of permanent revolution, that purged those that don't tow the line and generally acted like historic anarchists, maybe I would like them more)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that Camarilla-Sabbat conflict was paramount in 2ed/Revised/V20, have no problem with it, although I would it to go deeper than just decapitating Ventrue merchants (and Gehenna war actually providing such a chance but we have no clue how exactly it is going); but I see why they decided to shift back to V1 themes. Probably they want to go full circle once again, this time without the eschatological 2004 vibe. If that's the case and the sects are three again, each with it's distinctive feel and theme, doing their own things, I am totally in. If they make Sabbat V1 again, I'm out.<br /> <br /> The Anarch thing being as far from Bat'ko Makhno or Durutti as possible is of no surprise in modern nights. Look at their 'counterparts' in moder world. Constant infighting, bickering, competitions in ideological purity, moral committee trials in forums and threads, tribalism, and most of all, complete lack of personal integrity or collective accountability. <br /> The fact that finally the VtM Anarchs somehow, miraculously handled the last two issues is the main reason they skyrocketed from 'those local leather clowns' into 'seize the means of vitae production'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T08:33:44-07:00","id":1377739,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> what are Bat\u2019ko Makhno and Durutti?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:14:40-07:00","id":1377749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377739#post1377739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> what are Bat\u2019ko Makhno and Durutti?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably the most famous propenents of practical militant anarchism. In real world history, of course. &quot;Bat'ko&quot; in Ukranian means 'Dad'. It was his alias during the 1919-1921 Civil war across post-tzarist Russia and it's former colonies. His actual name was Nestor. Buenaventura Durruti was the same but in Spain in 1930s.<br /> That's very simplified explanation, of course. There are numerous websites dedicated to the life and ideas these people fought for.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:14:40-07:00","id":1377750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377739#post1377739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> what are Bat\u2019ko Makhno and Durutti?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably the most famous propenents of practical militant anarchism. In real world history, of course. &quot;Bat'ko&quot; in Ukranian means 'Dad'. It was his alias during the 1919-1921 Civil war across post-tzarist Russia and it's former colonies. His actual name was Nestor. Buenaventura Durruti was the same but in Spain in 1930s.<br /> That's very simplified explanation, of course. There are numerous websites dedicated to the life and ideas these people fought for.<br /> <br /> sorry for the duplicate, my web is messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-01-2020, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:21:40-07:00","id":1377752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377730#post1377730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree that Camarilla-Sabbat conflict was paramount in 2ed/Revised/V20, have no problem with it, although I would it to go deeper than just decapitating Ventrue merchants (and Gehenna war actually providing such a chance but we have no clue how exactly it is going); but I see why they decided to shift back to V1 themes. Probably they want to go full circle once again, this time without the eschatological 2004 vibe. If that's the case and the sects are three again, each with it's distinctive feel and theme, doing their own things, I am totally in. If they make Sabbat V1 again, I'm out.<br /> <br /> The Anarch thing being as far from Bat'ko Makhno or Durutti as possible is of no surprise in modern nights. Look at their 'counterparts' in moder world. Constant infighting, bickering, competitions in ideological purity, moral committee trials in forums and threads, tribalism, and most of all, complete lack of personal integrity or collective accountability. <br /> The fact that finally the VtM Anarchs somehow, miraculously handled the last two issues is the main reason they skyrocketed from 'those local leather clowns' into 'seize the means of vitae production'.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they moved to permanent revolution mode, where are the gulags? The mass collateral damage terror campaigns? Death marches? That is how militia Anarchs have worked from the Paris commune on. Except they didn't seize the means of production, the Cam and Sabbat where so busy headbutting the stupidity stone, while wearing the idiot glasses and gargling the foolish gin, that the Anarchs won by default","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-01-2020, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T10:19:29-07:00","id":1377762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377752#post1377752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they moved to permanent revolution mode, where are the gulags? The mass collateral damage terror campaigns? Death marches? That is how militia Anarchs have worked from the Paris commune on. Except they didn't seize the means of production, the Cam and Sabbat where so busy headbutting the stupidity stone, while wearing the idiot glasses and gargling the foolish gin, that the Anarchs won by default</div> </div> </div> </div>permanent revolution did not involve the gulags 'cause the permanent one never happened, but I digress. terror campaigns and other stuff you mentioned are not what you will have in V5.Not sure if it's a bad thing, though. The V5 is yet to cover the worse of modern nights, it just started with Cults book.<br /> <br /> By seizing the means, I mean House Carna, I mean Theo Bell. I mean many not-Setites and most of Brujah and Gangrel going there (tbh I wonder what took these two so long?). So many of cainites of numerous clans and most probably various generations don't just hop aboard the happy rebel train, holding hands and kumbaya through the end times, Gehenna war, Beckoning and Second Inquisition. Therefore I consider Anarchs a legitimate success (with a small dose of plot armor from the authors) solely for making it through all of the mentioned ordeals.<br /> <br /> Stupidity stone made me laugh, thank you. It definitely puts Camarilla into their position of drooling old idiots who, should the fire hit the fan, bunker down and play 'we are highly concerned' card. They did not deserve such a downgrade, if you ask me, after being a dominant power of the vampiric world for several centuries. In that, I agree with you.<br /> However, Sabbat finally doing what they were designed for, is fine by me. I don't see any stupidity here. Depends on how much of the sect really moves to MENA and from what I read across the web, it's most of the sect, 70-80%. So it's only natural the quickest to fill the resulting gap in Western cities would be the most attuned to mortal world and shifting political landscape while Camarilla closes their doors and hides in their mansions.<br /> <br /> The only thing which really concerns me is the V5 so far being centered around Western cities and communities but I guess it's just a start. Also, one could says that in other parts of the world, Camarilla vs Sabbat competition still continues in this or that way and the places where the Anarchs are now dominiant are limited to NA/EU domains. If any book covered this topic pls point me to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T11:41:09-07:00","id":1377769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> thanks. That answers my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:00:30-07:00","id":1377773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377711#post1377711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I tried to do my best to explain why it is. I believe both to be crucial parts of the Vampire identity and covered my favorite part. I'd like to know why that part is or should be used as a cautionary tale only and justified why it should not. Talking about the game's direction and the canon not the homebrew here - I always liked the main line no matter how many things I'd changed in it; it's always interesting to see the continuation of that same plot and the living world envisioned by it's creators and professionals. I suppose you feel the same way towards VtM but looks like we are not into a discussion here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that I *LIKE* the Sabbat and think they have a very valuable role in the setting. I'm just saying they don't have shit on the Anarchs and it's nice they're finally getting the attention they deserve.<br /> <br /> I could go into length about what I like about the Sabbat and why I think V5 isn't fair to them but usually when I do, people start dumping on the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> You can like 90% of V5 without agreeing with everything. The Sabbat have an important role as the inhuman irredeemable vampires that threaten the vampire status quo. The Satanic and mysterious undead wholly given to the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T12:09:22-07:00","id":1377776,"title":"","content":"<b>The Anarchs vs. Camarilla appeal</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, people try to attribute the Camarilla and Sabbat and Anarchs to real world philosophical groups and speaking as an academic that's....dumb. The vampire is a creature that requires at least 1000 to 10,000 humans for every single one of them and they exist as a parasite among them. They exist as an elite nobility (or predator) among the masses no matter what they are and they will never have numbers larger than a mid-sized high school in any city in the world. There's never going to be more than 200 vampires in a city as large as New York City which means that existing political models are RIDICULOUS to apply to them.<br /> <br /> Instead, the best model for the Anarchs vs. Camarilla are the fictional and very entertaining cyberpunk models as well as organized crime. Anarchs exist as competing organized gangs against the stiff and decaying institutions of the Camarilla mafia. In the end, both groups are after territory and cash but the Anarchs are outsiders moving in to carve their own turf as well as resources by overthrowing the existing.<br /> <br /> In simple terms:<br /> <br /> Cyberpunk:<br /> <br /> Camarilla=Megacorporations<br /> Anarchs=Crime Syndicates<br /> PCs=Mercenaries<br /> <br /> The big benefit of the Anarchs is the fact that the Anarchs can exist within a Camarilla city and the Camarilla can exist within a Anarch City. The Sabbat will always be their own sort of game and are antagonistic to the point of not being able to play local politics against one another since they're always in a state of direct overt war. The Anarchs and Camarilla can engage in Cold Wars, loose alliances, or outright conflict with a lot more &quot;under the table&quot; diplomacy as well as friendships/alliances/rivalries.<br /> <br /> Which is the irony that's on display here. Everyone is talking about how the Anarchs are lesser for the fact that they're not engaged in a militarized campaign of extermination when that is SHIT for street level roleplaying games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T13:34:28-07:00","id":1377791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377776#post1377776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Anarchs vs. Camarilla appeal</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, people try to attribute the Camarilla and Sabbat and Anarchs to real world philosophical groups and speaking as an academic that's....dumb. The vampire is a creature that requires at least 1000 to 10,000 humans for every single one of them and they exist as a parasite among them. They exist as an elite nobility (or predator) among the masses no matter what they are and they will never have numbers larger than a mid-sized high school in any city in the world. There's never going to be more than 200 vampires in a city as large as New York City which means that existing political models are RIDICULOUS to apply to them.<br /> <br /> Instead, the best model for the Anarchs vs. Camarilla are the fictional and very entertaining cyberpunk models as well as organized crime. Anarchs exist as competing organized gangs against the stiff and decaying institutions of the Camarilla mafia. In the end, both groups are after territory and cash but the Anarchs are outsiders moving in to carve their own turf as well as resources by overthrowing the existing.<br /> <br /> In simple terms:<br /> <br /> Cyberpunk:<br /> <br /> Camarilla=Megacorporations<br /> Anarchs=Crime Syndicates<br /> PCs=Mercenaries<br /> <br /> The big benefit of the Anarchs is the fact that the Anarchs can exist within a Camarilla city and the Camarilla can exist within a Anarch City. The Sabbat will always be their own sort of game and are antagonistic to the point of not being able to play local politics against one another since they're always in a state of direct overt war. The Anarchs and Camarilla can engage in Cold Wars, loose alliances, or outright conflict with a lot more &amp;quot;under the table&amp;quot; diplomacy as well as friendships/alliances/rivalries.<br /> <br /> Which is the irony that's on display here. Everyone is talking about how the Anarchs are lesser for the fact that they're not engaged in a militarized campaign of extermination when that is SHIT for street level roleplaying games.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet what you like about Anarchs is exactly what I do not like about them. Either the elders are the enemy, in which case fight them, or they aren't, so join them, come of the fence, or get splinters up the ass, seriously no Anarch group has been portrayed as smart and disciplined enough to survive a War Coterie or Crusade assault, and the plot armour that sees them never get smacked down breaks disbelief, I will buy ancient elders and inhuman monsters, please don't also ask me to buy them being monumentally incompetent as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> The blend of cyberpunk and supernatural horror really does not do anything for me, and certainly hasn't been expanded on enough for me to believe it was anything but a passing fancy in 1e(and even in cyberpunk I gravitate towards the adversarial end of the runner scale) I lived through enough of the Cold War IRL to not want a weird version of it in a game, set the sides, have the war, then lead, follow, or hide, that makes fun chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T15:13:33-07:00","id":1377806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377773#post1377773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is that I *LIKE* the Sabbat and think they have a very valuable role in the setting. I'm just saying they don't have shit on the Anarchs and it's nice they're finally getting the attention they deserve.<br /> <br /> I could go into length about what I like about the Sabbat and why I think V5 isn't fair to them but usually when I do, people start dumping on the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at your next statement I think V5 is more fair to them than you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can like 90% of V5 without agreeing with everything. The Sabbat have an important role as the inhuman irredeemable vampires that threaten the vampire status quo. The Satanic and mysterious undead wholly given to the Beast. </div> </div> </div>Seeing you did not mention this vision as your own I assume you present it as a default image of this sect in V5 which is both incorrect so far (we know too little to state it so overtly and have to wait for their book) and totally unfair to numerous players who like the concept(s) and themes of the sect and played it through previous editions. It was so much more in the books dedicated to or mentioning it in 2ed/Revised/V20 that I don't even know where to start. Again, I am confused by the necessity to pigeonhole them into such a category after all the texts written on it and the effort put into it both by authors and by players.<br /> <br /> I could go into great length why saying that some group in VtM or even WoD is irredeemable is going against the very spirit of the setting, but I thought it's obvious. I am also sure that nothing in V5 so far is pointing that such a blatant simplification is anywhere near in the coming books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T15:16:49-07:00","id":1377807,"title":"","content":"Anarchs are a combination of criminal elements, political dissidents, and an armed civil war faction in the Camarilla. While the difference between them is real, from an objective point of view that includes the Sabbat and Independent Clans, they actually agree on 80-90% of stuff. In fact, if you look at the political flanks of both sides (the Anarch sympathizing Camarilla loyalist, and the reform minded Anarch), there is so much overlap it's hard to tell why each one is included on the side they're on.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat though is ultimately anti-thetical to both of them. They're a combination of a religious apocalyptic sect, extremist totalitarian revolutionaries, and arch-reactionaries who've abandoned conservative monarchism for fascism. Their worldview is absolute and requires not just the defeat of their enemies - but their extermination. And if they ever won, they'd completely change how vampires interact with mortals (which is why in a metafictional capacity they can never be allowed to win, as if they did you wouldn't have a World of Darkness where vampires existed in secret along mortals, but a more explicitly fantasy version of the world where mortals actively warred on the undead.)<br /> <br /> I don't like CTPhipp's description of their struggle in reference to Cyberpunk tropes. I think it's really stretching things. But I do agree that trying to use the lens of real world philosophical groups doesn't work.<br /> <br /> What the distinction is really about - is what kind of vampires are we talking about?<br /> <br /> Camarilla - any vampire fiction which shows vampires and humans cooperating to some degree; an elegant society of monsters who are concerned about the Beast or Masquerade<ul><li>Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles</li> <li>Twilight and other Paranormal Romance</li> <li>Forever Knight</li> <li>Innocent Blood</li> </ul>Anarchs - vampire fiction which shows vampires as rebellious teenagers enjoying their power/freedom; or any struggle between a vampire master and a vampire's spawn<ul><li>Lost Boys</li> <li>Near Dark</li> </ul>Sabbat - classic vampires that spread like a plague and represent metaphysical evil<ul><li>Hammer Horror style Satanic vampires</li> <li>Count Yorga films</li> <li>Salem's Lot</li> <li>From Dusk to Dawn</li> <li>30 Days of Night</li> </ul>These distinctions aren't drawn with hard lines. Near Dark is often mentioned as both Anarchs and Nomad Sabbat for example. And the Camarilla and Anarch sources of inspiration can often switch back and forth. (That's because the difference is now between how they interact with mortals, but with each other). But each sect has themes that represent what kind of monster they are.<br /> <br /> The Independent Clans are harder to recognize, but their original function was to serve a very specific metaplot setting or narrative purpose. And the more the game strays from that, the greater the game stops treating them as independents and pushes them to one of the sects. Depending on how you like each of those clans, and why you like them, you'll have different opinions on whether that change was good or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T15:23:11-07:00","id":1377808,"title":"","content":"Playing Sabbat isn't about being &quot;irredeemable&quot;, it is about playing a creature who is not beholden to the morality system of a different species. Playing a Feral Heart character who tries to balance his path's eschewing of politics and need to protect his pack with the practical realities of unlife in a sect where a fair amount of politicking IS needed in order to actually protect one's pack. Trying to balance the tenets of Honorable Accord with the ruthless realities of actual warfare. I find these things interesting.<br /> <br /> I get very weary hearing things that just kind of assume that a system of social constructs created by predatory apes to deify themselves is The One True Way, as objective as thermodynamics and gravity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:19:40-07:00","id":1377812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377791#post1377791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet what you like about Anarchs is exactly what I do not like about them. Either the elders are the enemy, in which case fight them, or they aren't, so join them, come of the fence, or get splinters up the ass, seriously no Anarch group has been portrayed as smart and disciplined enough to survive a War Coterie or Crusade assault, and the plot armour that<br /> sees them never get smacked down breaks disbelief, I will buy ancient elders and inhuman monsters, please don't also ask me to buy them being monumentally incompetent as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a social game and not a war game. Also, repeatedly in every Crusade and military conflict, the Anarchs have been portrayed as the boots on the ground. Which makes sense because no one would actually fight for the Camarilla since it's a conspiracy of the super-rich to protect their wealth. They were also the first to die on the ground as well, which was detailed in the Clan Novels. They were stupid to try to protect the Camarilla against the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> However, whatare you going talking about &quot;smart&quot; or &quot;disciplined&quot;? Did you ever read the Clan Novels. They beat over the head the Sabbat is a disorganized, unity-less, infighting-ridden bunch of barely controlled Beasts. Only a handful of geniuses can direct the swarm of locusts that they tend to be and then they collapse back into infighting. There is an organized, inhuman, and alien mindset group...it's called the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> Or the Assamites or Web of Knives.<br /> <br /> They are NOT the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The blend of cyberpunk and supernatural horror really does not do anything for me, and certainly hasn't been expanded on enough for me to believe it was anything but a passing fancy in 1e(and even in cyberpunk I gravitate towards the adversarial end of the runner scale) I lived through enough of the Cold War IRL to not want a weird version of it in a game, set the sides, have the war, then lead, follow, or hide, that makes fun chronicles. </div> </div> </div>For me, it's a game of intrigue. Vampires shouldn't be fighting in the streets. They should be engaging with proxies, secret attacks, and covert missions like the kind in Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377806#post1377806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing you did not mention this vision as your own I assume you present it as a default image of this sect in V5 which is both incorrect so far (we know too little to state it so overtly and have to wait for their book) and totally unfair to numerous players who like the concept(s) and themes of the sect and played it through previous editions. It was so much more in the books dedicated to or mentioning it in 2ed/Revised/V20 that I don't even know where to start. Again, I am confused by the necessity to pigeonhole them into such a category after all the texts written on it and the effort put into it both by authors and by players.<br /> <br /> I could go into great length why saying that some group in VtM or even WoD is irredeemable is going against the very spirit of the setting, but I thought it's obvious. I am also sure that nothing in V5 so far is pointing that such a blatant simplification is anywhere near in the coming books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our clearest view of the Sabbat was given in both CHICAGO BY NIGHT with the idea that the organization is in the state of a Civil War with the Lasombra fighting over defections as well as CHICAGO FOLIO which states that the Sabbat in America have collapsed. The largest group in the Midwestern United States is described as a terrorist cult existing solely to destroy the Camarilla as well as Anarchs.<br /> <br /> My view of the Sabbat is they're a bunch of alien Satanic monsters, eldritch priests, and people like HOUSE OF 1000 CORPSES and THE TEXAS CHAINSAW MASSACRE. They're people who live in houses full of corpses, twisted altars to demons, and a wholesale embrace of the worst in themselves. They disdain humanity and indulge in their worst impulses to be the vampires that terrify the shit out of you. They're sort of the poor cousins to the Assamites and the Followers of Set who have much better knowledge of the Darkness. The Lasombra and Tzimicse, ironically, didn't pass laong their inner clan secrets that well to their sect brethren.<br /> <br /> They were right that human morality is incompatible with the Vampire LifestyleTM but failed to tame the Beast like the Assamites, Followers of Set, or True Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-01-2020, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:21:38-07:00","id":1377813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377776#post1377776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Anarchs vs. Camarilla appeal</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, people try to attribute the Camarilla and Sabbat and Anarchs to real world philosophical groups and speaking as an academic that's....dumb. The vampire is a creature that requires at least 1000 to 10,000 humans for every single one of them and they exist as a parasite among them. They exist as an elite nobility (or predator) among the masses no matter what they are and they will never have numbers larger than a mid-sized high school in any city in the world. There's never going to be more than 200 vampires in a city as large as New York City which means that existing political models are RIDICULOUS to apply to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you just called dumb was going on in the VtM/VtR books and in games for decades.<br /> <br /> I believe most of us know of the vampiric demographics and how it could vary from sect to sect. I am also not sure what is wrong with applying political models to vampires while one of the main Vampire themes, and I think, any other World of Darkness line, was taking a look at shadowy politics as a dark reflection of the human world one's. Both supernatural and real worlds affected each other, the latter affecting the former arguably more than vice versa.<br /> <br /> Sects were international, continent-spanning organizations not just some scattered domains who pay lip service to main cause and appearing more as semi-independent conclaves barely giving a heck about the cause of common protection of Masquarade or upholding Traditions, or waging war against some blood gods or demons.<br /> <br /> I get your idea about cyberpunk but that's totally not down my street even if talking solely Camarilla vs Anarchs. Boiling it down to turf wars and feeding ground rivalries is kind of GTA. What's interesting in it? If you do it as a not-so-sophisticated background for some interesting, complicated relations, I get it. The lone idea of a rivalry between an overtly criminal and a more subtly criminal supernatural organization sounds not like a Vampire game at all. Anyway, it is still something else I've never heard of or tried - blending in cyberpunk shtick is great. Just to me, it's too small of a part of the game itself and I can;t see how this is more entertaining than something more old-school.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead, the best model for the Anarchs vs. Camarilla are the fictional and very entertaining cyberpunk models as well as organized crime. Anarchs exist as competing organized gangs against the stiff and decaying institutions of the Camarilla mafia. In the end, both groups are after territory and cash but the Anarchs are outsiders moving in to carve their own turf as well as resources by overthrowing the existing.<br /> <br /> In simple terms:<br /> <br /> Cyberpunk:<br /> <br /> Camarilla=Megacorporations<br /> Anarchs=Crime Syndicates<br /> PCs=Mercenaries<br /> The big benefit of the Anarchs is the fact that the Anarchs can exist within a Camarilla city and the Camarilla can exist within a Anarch City. The Sabbat will always be their own sort of game and are antagonistic to the point of not being able to play local politics against one another since they're always in a state of direct overt war. The Anarchs and Camarilla can engage in Cold Wars, loose alliances, or outright conflict with a lot more &quot;under the table&quot; diplomacy as well as friendships/alliances/rivalries. </div> </div> </div>The part about the sword of caine is simply not true, but I believe that's your personal view on it. <br /> Frankly, to me, the idea of such game have little in common with Vampire, or rather represents a small facet of what a Vampire chronicle is. How can a story about two groups of supernatural predators rivalring for the city boil down to 'territory and cash'? Isn't it easier - and cheaper to your supernatural immortal ass - to go with two human &quot;Veils&quot;, speaking in KotE terms, to do it for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is the irony that's on display here. Everyone is talking about how the Anarchs are lesser </div> </div> </div>Everyone is talking about how Anarchs are lesser because 1) they were lesser before V5 and you can't erase 20 years of development which depicted them like that in one night - again, I am not one of those people and love to see Anarchs rejuvenated and redesigned in a more serious light, and playing a crime syndicate _only_ would not help that redesign, in my opinion; 2) some of those who dump on your favorite sect are probably fans of the sect you are dumping on (mostly by misinterpreting or simplifying it). That's not appropriate and I do not encourage dumping on anything<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> for the fact that they're not engaged in a militarized campaign of extermination when that is SHIT for street level roleplaying games </div> </div> </div>Whoa. We aren't in here to define 'the most appropriate and esteemed way to roleplay', aren't we? That sounds rude, and not just to a big chunk of street-level LARPers, Camarilla-Sabbat war had militarized campaigns of extermination only as one facet of the whole conflict. A culmination of sorts, with years, decades, sometimes centuries of schemes, shadowy treaties, occult research, shifting allegiances, undercover reconnaisance, political powerplay and even negotiations ACROSS continents preceding the 'combat campaigns'. Reminding you of whole books dedicated to conflict, we can safely assume it all was not just shit for street level roleplaying games. And most of the time extermination was not the one and only final goal - conversion and indoctrination possibly on the same level with extermination or simply driving 'the others' away. It WAS a turf war, indeed - but also much more than that.<br /> Anyway, why the elitism?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:49:40-07:00","id":1377817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377813#post1377813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you just called dumb was going on in the VtM/VtR books and in games for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the books are pretty good about establishing that the politics of the Anarchs vs. Camarilla vs. Sabbat vs. Kuei-Jin have always been best on a local street level. It's about taking over cities and not national-level conflicts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe most of us know of the vampiric demographics and how it could vary from sect to sect. I am also not sure what is wrong with applying political models to vampires while one of the main Vampire themes, and I think, any other World of Darkness line, was taking a look at shadowy politics as a dark reflection of the human world one's. Both supernatural and real worlds affected each other, the latter affecting the former arguably more than vice versa. </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, the games have always personified the politics they deal with. It doesn't matter what you believe ideology wise because in the end the politics are not going to be bigger than the nearest vampire who embodies them. Lodin, Sebastian La Croix, Marcus Vitel, and Hardestadt are the Camarilla big wigs you deal with and they are individuals who have the authority and position to embody the Camarilla. The Princes BARELY answer to anyone higher than themselves and have a massive amount of authority to deal with problems as they see fit. I feel that makes the games more interesting because every city is customizable in a way that a larger political struggle wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> The dictator of your personal revolution and revolutionary war leader are people you know personally. Be they Juggler or Modius.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sects were international, continent-spanning organizations not just some scattered domains who pay lip service to main cause and appearing more as semi-independent conclaves barely giving a heck about the cause of common protection of Masquarade or upholding Traditions, or waging war against some blood gods or demons. </div> </div> </div>It's hilarious that I literally just wrote the exact opposite above in my interpretation of them. The Camarilla and Movement will never be as important as the local representatives of such in your area. Most vampires will never leave within 30 miles of their Embrace, sort of like feudalism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get your idea about cyberpunk but that's totally not down my street even if talking solely Camarilla vs Anarchs. Boiling it down to turf wars and feeding ground rivalries is kind of GTA. What's interesting in it? If you do it as a not-so-sophisticated background for some interesting, complicated relations, I get it. The lone idea of a rivalry between an overtly criminal and a more subtly criminal supernatural organization sounds not like a Vampire game at all. Anyway, it is still something else I've never heard of or tried - blending in cyberpunk shtick is great. Just to me, it's too small of a part of the game itself and I can;t see how this is more entertaining than something more old-school. </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, Grand Theft Auto is a very good inspiration for games of vampire in my view. Because you always are going to have varying degrees of assholes to deal with and questions of who can you trust [answer: no one]. The first Camarilla and Anarch leaders you ever meet in V:TM are Modius and Juggler with both of them two sides of the same coin. Ideology is something that is exploited by Elder vampires to manipulate younger ones but you have to believe in something to get through your unlife. Still, 90% of all vampire conflicts is power, prestige, and Domain. Doesn't matter which sect is doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The part about the sword of caine is simply not true, but I believe that's your personal view on it. Frankly, to me, the idea of such game have little in common with Vampire, or rather represents a small facet of what a Vampire chronicle is. How can a story about two groups of supernatural predators rivalring for the city boil down to 'territory and cash'? Isn't it easier - and cheaper to your supernatural immortal ass - to go with two human &quot;Veils&quot;, speaking in KotE terms, to do it for you? </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall that the canonical end of the Kuei-Jin and Camarilla conflict in Revised was the Camarilla paid off the Kuei-Jin to leave them alone. It was in NIGHTS OF PROPHECY. Do you remember that?<br /> <br /> Summary: In &quot;Walking after Midnight&quot;, the New Promise Mandate and Camarilla reach an aggreement where the former will receive a massive cash payment in exchange for not expanding beyond the former Anarch Free States. The Anarchs have the opportunity to disrupt the peace treaty and steal the money for themselves.<br /> <br /> I love this adventure because it perfectly encapsulates what all of the sects are: crime syndicates dueling it out for territory. I always think Vampire works a lot like THE GODFATHER with fangs. You have the suit and tie mafisio as the Camarilla and the Anarchs as the street toughs on the ground with the independents being outside context problems. You can still have conflicts over humanity, persecution, trying to get out of the corrupt businesses, and trying to &quot;make it&quot; so you can protect yourself--you know, stuff like the Godfather, Yakuza games, and so on.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, a large part of it is the rivalry between the sides you pick to serve. Safety in numbers vs. being a lone operator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone is talking about how Anarchs are lesser because 1) they were lesser before V5 and you can't erase 20 years of development which depicted them like that in one night - again, I am not one of those people and love to see Anarchs rejuvenated and redesigned in a more serious light, and playing a crime syndicate _only_ would not help that redesign, in my opinion; 2) some of those who dump on your favorite sect are probably fans of the sect you are dumping on (mostly by misinterpreting or simplifying it). That's not appropriate and I do not encourage dumping on anything </div> </div> </div>They were shit on in Revised but were major sects in 1st, 2nd, and V20. Also, the Anarchs were revised for the NWoD as the Carthians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-19-2020, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:54:33-07:00","id":1377820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377812#post1377812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our clearest view of the Sabbat was given in both CHICAGO BY NIGHT with the idea that the organization is in the state of a Civil War with the Lasombra fighting over defections as well as CHICAGO FOLIO which states that the Sabbat in America have collapsed. The largest group in the Midwestern United States is described as a terrorist cult existing solely to destroy the Camarilla as well as Anarchs.<br /> <br /> My view of the Sabbat is they're a bunch of alien Satanic monsters, eldritch priests, and people like HOUSE OF 1000 CORPSES and THE TEXAS CHAINSAW MASSACRE. They're people who live in houses full of corpses, twisted altars to demons, and a wholesale embrace of the worst in themselves. They disdain humanity and indulge in their worst impulses to be the vampires that terrify the shit out of you. They're sort of the poor cousins to the Assamites and the Followers of Set who have much better knowledge of the Darkness. The Lasombra and Tzimicse, ironically, didn't pass laong their inner clan secrets that well to their sect brethren.<br /> <br /> They were right that human morality is incompatible with the Vampire LifestyleTM but failed to tame the Beast like the Assamites, Followers of Set, or True Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - that's certainly not fair but concerns US 'gaming theater' only so not a big loss. Are you one of the writers for V5?<br /> <br /> 2 - that's one huge simplification and an erasure of a huge chunk of fluff. First edition, basically. Hope it doesn't influence the future books. It's a nice concept of NPCs or a cannon fodder for the 'actual' Sabbat to hunt down in order to avoid exposure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're sort of the poor cousins to the Assamites and the Followers of Set who have much better knowledge of the Darkness. </div> </div> </div>Ironically, in the books dedicated to them, including the one on Paths, they are the best scholars of it. Again, just for comparison, check out the Road of Night and the ideas of Moncada behind Sabbat's role in God's plans, Montreal by Night, Path of Redemption etc.<br /> <br /> I really don't see the need of your favoritism - elevating one sect as a main protagonists (Anarchs) with two others being dealt a huge blow and boiled down/simplified into the ground, taking one of the most resentful (by human standards) aspects (a super rich 1% conspiracy/deathmetal nazi satanitsts) of each as the 'core' idea. If we are being pragmatic - Is it going to help the sales and overall success of the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-01-2020, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T17:30:17-07:00","id":1377828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377817#post1377817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the books are pretty good about establishing that the politics of the Anarchs vs. Camarilla vs. Sabbat vs. Kuei-Jin have always been best on a local street level. It's about taking over cities and not national-level conflicts.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the games have always personified the politics they deal with. It doesn't matter what you believe ideology wise because in the end the politics are not going to be bigger than the nearest vampire who embodies them. Lodin, Sebastian La Croix, Marcus Vitel, and Hardelstadt are the Camarilla big wigs you deal with and they are individuals who have the authority and position to embody the Camarilla. The Princes BARELY answer to anyone higher than themselves and have a massive amount of authority to deal with problems as they see fit. I feel that makes the games more interesting because every city is customizable in a way that a larger political struggle wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> The dictator of your personal revolution and revolutionary war leader are people you know personally. Be they Juggler or Modius.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's hilarious that I literally just wrote the exact opposite above in my interpretation of them. The Camarilla and Movement will never be as important as the local representatives of such in your area. Most vampires will never leave within 30 miles of their Embrace, sort of like feudalism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hilaroius indeed. It looks like we read and perceived the same books and stories in totally different ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I seem to recall that the canonical end of the Kuei-Jin and Camarilla conflict in Revised was the Camarilla paid off the Kuei-Jin to leave them alone. It was in NIGHTS OF PROPHECY. Do you remember that?<br /> <br /> Summary: In &quot;Walking after Midnight&quot;, the New Promise Mandate and Camarilla reach an aggreement where the former will receive a massive cash payment in exchange for not expanding beyond the former Anarch Free States. The Anarchs have the opportunity to disrupt the peace treaty and steal the money for themselves. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I remember it. I also remember that both the reason of Quincunx to start the whole thing was not just to 'get money and resources', like East Asia, or whole of Asia, lack financial opportunities, really.<br /> I also recall that there was a nice intrigue involving an impersonator from Sabbat, not sure if he was alone or working with someone else. I also recall that this whole adventure is a part of the bigger thing called NIGHTS OF PROPHECY. Does not sound very down-to-earth, concerning the name and the idea behind it?<br /> <br /> I would also like to recall another part of the NIGHT OF PROPHECY, what happened in Montreal. It's interesting how you recalled the less 'supernaturally-themed' adventure and forgot &quot;the more&quot;. this adventure is dedicated to Noddism, research, inner sectarian strife, shifting loyalties and much, much more personal horror than the previous one (e.g. a total loss of faith by Lionel after he finally translated the newfound exempt from the Book).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love this adventure because it perfectly encapsulates what all of the sects are: crime syndicates dueling it out for territory. I always think Vampire works a lot like THE GODFATHER with fangs. You have the suit and tie mafisio as the Camarilla and the Anarchs as the street toughs on the ground with the independents being outside context problems. You can still have conflicts over humanity, persecution, trying to get out of the corrupt businesses, and trying to &quot;make it&quot; so you can protect yourself--you know, stuff like the Godfather, Yakuza games, and so on. </div> </div> </div>Godfather with fangs was the most prevalent element across all sects and all of Revised, killing a lot of 'fantasy' and 'unknown' which we had in the second edition. Godfather with fangs is what Sabbat was, with 'satanic shovelheads' you love so much to describe in gory details being just one facet of the sect, limited to New World specifically (Old World Sabbat expressed open disdain towards that element of the sect overseas) and certainly not the most fun to play, with the mainstay being Cartels/Mafia/Evil CIA (Dastur's Black Hand) upped to eleven with vozhd, ritae and abyss mysticism. These spooky elements served to provide atmosphere not to be a centerpiece of the sect's identity. Seriously, GttS 1998 is an epitome of such a serious, grounded depiction. Again, we seem to have read those books in opposite ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were shit on in Revised but were major sects in 1st, 2nd, and V20. Also, the Anarchs were revised for the NWoD as the Carthians. </div> </div> </div>They were shit on 2ed (not so hard as in the next ed), Revised, V20 improved things especially with Anarch's blood magic (it's the best part of the BS book). V5 makes them shine like in 1ed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T17:48:03-07:00","id":1377831,"title":"","content":"By the way, while we are at it, TableGoth Twitch is now streaming a Sabbat game set in NY 2020. A pack tries to claw their way out of the city. Most importantly, you can donate to charity while watching it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:01:14-07:00","id":1377833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377817#post1377817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the books are pretty good about establishing that the politics of the Anarchs vs. Camarilla vs. Sabbat vs. Kuei-Jin have always been best on a local street level. It's about taking over cities and not national-level con,.................</div> </div> </div> </div>NWOD/VtR had no good ideas, no system, no setting, nothing, it was one of the worst RPGs I have ever read, and any ideas from it are a tumour to excise from VtM, not a selling point <br /> <br /> Yes I do remember how badly the new promise mandate was botched in Nights of Prophecy, but turning a war into a criminal operation, it lost all impact and interest. Luckily the Montreal section remained a philosophical and theological story, and was far better for it.<br /> <br /> The less the Anarchs were the core assumption, the better the writing of the edition was, it is a rock solid trend line.<br /> <br /> As to GTA with fangs? That is exactly the thing I loathe about Anarchs. If I want to play a criminal/Cyberpunk game, their are RPGs that do it far better, I want to play a game of of international supernatural conspiracy and cthonic horror, of ancient evil and posthuman blood drinkers, the Sabbat used to give us that, all we have for V5 for the Sabbat is the Devs screaming how much they hate is and how kewl the Anarchs are, if the setting books are to be believed. In short we played totally different games, and I do not recognize the one you describe, nor does it interest me, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:02:15-07:00","id":1377834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377831#post1377831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, while we are at it, TableGoth Twitch is now streaming a Sabbat game set in NY 2020. A pack tries to claw their way out of the city. Most importantly, you can donate to charity while watching it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are they doing the Paths ? Do they have official rules or are they home-brewing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:13:28-07:00","id":1377841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377833#post1377833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short we played totally different games, and I do not recognize the one you describe, nor does it interest me, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that means we like different things. I can't imagine that's ever happened before in a game before.<br /> <br /> But what the do you mean, &quot;you don't RECOGNIZE it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-01-2020, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:18:43-07:00","id":1377842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377834#post1377834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are they doing the Paths ? Do they have official rules or are they home-brewing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I see, they are not doing them at all.( It's just a start of it, but I bet they do either low Humanity, or homebrew.<br /> The game is centered about survival, escaping the city. Currently it;s about investigations/interrogations rather than discussions or combat/action. They had a Vaulderie at the very start of the sessoin, though. I love Sabbat games which minimize action and make violent scenes short and focused (therefore all the more terrifying).<br /> Contrary to what I saw here in that thread, no recurring themes of satanism and being EEEEVIL for evil's sake. So far so good!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:22:14-07:00","id":1377843,"title":"","content":"You could do paranormal teen romance (or just romance in general) with either the Anarchs or the Camarilla, but it would be really hard to do with the Sabbat. I think any sexual feelings they might still have are pretty much sublimated by the Vaulderie.<br /> <br /> Also, there\u2019s the false Black Hand, who are the elite warriors of the Sabbat, and the True Black Hand, the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra. The Sabbat hates the True Black Hand because they serve the Antediluvians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:23:00-07:00","id":1377844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377820#post1377820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 - that's certainly not fair but concerns US 'gaming theater' only so not a big loss. Are you one of the writers for V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it's the most we've heard about the Sabbat anyway. The Sabbat we've heard about in Mexico and Canada have lost their primary cities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - that's one huge simplification and an erasure of a huge chunk of fluff. First edition, basically. Hope it doesn't influence the future books. It's a nice concept of NPCs or a cannon fodder for the 'actual' Sabbat to hunt down in order to avoid exposure. </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's a weird bit of fanon going on here because the vast majority of Sabbat were not like the Sabbat of Montreal. The Sabbat of Montreal with their intellectual and scholarly side were explictly outliers and the majority of Sabbat were barely controlled punks that were either going to die horribly or be consumed by the Beast. Also, the Sabbat in Montreal were subject to a large amount of Infernalist infiltration and corruption.<br /> <br /> I feel like people ignore the &quot;Sabbat lost to the beast&quot; because it doesn't fit their philosopher kings ideal of them that was never more than a minority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ironically, in the books dedicated to them, including the one on Paths, they are the best scholars of it. Again, just for comparison, check out the Road of Night and the ideas of Moncada behind Sabbat's role in God's plans, Montreal by Night, Path of Redemption etc. </div> </div> </div>Moncada notably corrupted and twisted the Road of the Night into something utterly unrecognizable. Part of what I like about the Sabbat were its Fall from Grace in the Dark Ages chronicles. The Anarchs were the hope for Kindred society and were warped into something nightmarish. It's a very powerful and interesting story, though not the only one that could be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't see the need of your favoritism - elevating one sect as a main protagonists (Anarchs) with two others being dealt a huge blow and boiled down/simplified into the ground, taking one of the most resentful (by human standards) aspects (a super rich 1% conspiracy/deathmetal nazi satanitsts) of each as the 'core' idea. If we are being pragmatic - Is it going to help the sales and overall success of the game? </div> </div> </div>Actually, the weird thing is the Anarchs were pretty much half of the Camarilla in previous editions. Most Anarchs were part of the Camarilla so the Camarilla split in half rather than &quot;one sect being elevated over the other two.&quot; Its more like, &quot;One sect became more clearly two.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't like the handling of the Sabbat in V5 as they could have easily inserted the Sabbat as a playable option if they'd included less predator types and in-game fiction in the corebook. Mind you, I'm very glad that they've stopped the Sabbat ripping off the Anarchs and their themes but they went way way too far. I hope they eventually do release a Sabbat book and it's kind of weird they haven't.<br /> <br /> It should be a smaller, darker, more terrifying sect than Revised with the Anarchs being the Camarilla's primary rivals but its still one of the core groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:27:35-07:00","id":1377846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377841#post1377841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, that means we like different things. I can't imagine that's ever happened before in a game before.<br /> <br /> But what the do you mean, &quot;you don't RECOGNIZE it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean your interpretation of previous editions is so different from mine that I cannot see how you came to those conclusions, it is like you are describing a completely different book by a different company. And since all V5 sabbat Lore so far is the Devs spitting at us and screaming their hatred of players who like the Sabbat, and missing the point of anything that isn't the Anarchs completely, maybe stop using that steaming pile of excrement as a source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-01-2020, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:29:41-07:00","id":1377847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377841#post1377841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what the do you mean, &quot;you don't RECOGNIZE it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The same I did. Dozens of VtM books I read are telling a different story, provide a different atmosphere and set a different tone from those you must've read in regards to all sects, but most obviously in regards to the Sabbat. Or you intentionally omit the parts that don't suite your vision of the sect(s).<br /> <br /> Playing your own game and homebrewing is one thing. Twisting the vision set by decades of development to suit your own and try to set it as a mainstream going forward is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:30:29-07:00","id":1377848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377828#post1377828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hilaroius indeed. It looks like we read and perceived the same books and stories in totally different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had one argument in a Technocracy game that the player characters shouldn't know the Conventions existed. I was like, &quot;That may be the way you do it at your table but this is my table.&quot; Which is true, the Storyteller is who matters in the interpretation of these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I remember it. I also remember that both the reason of Quincunx to start the whole thing was not just to 'get money and resources', like East Asia, or whole of Asia, lack financial opportunities, really. I also recall that there was a nice intrigue involving an impersonator from Sabbat, not sure if he was alone or working with someone else. I also recall that this whole adventure is a part of the bigger thing called NIGHTS OF PROPHECY. Does not sound very down-to-earth, concerning the name and the idea behind it? </div> </div> </div>I think they actually retconned the Great Leap Outward as essentially a Henry the 5th-esque plot to get rid of their own versions of the Anarchs. They started beating the drum of war in order to get younger Kuei-jin to attack the Camarilla and Anarchs so they would get the hell out of the territories of older as well as more established Kuei-Jin. It's only when the two sides fought for a few years that they realized they'd both been had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ]I would also like to recall another part of the NIGHT OF PROPHECY, what happened in Montreal. It's interesting how you recalled the less 'supernaturally-themed' adventure and forgot &quot;the more&quot;. this adventure is dedicated to Noddism, research, inner sectarian strife, shifting loyalties and much, much more personal horror than the previous one (e.g. a total loss of faith by Lionel after he finally translated the newfound exempt from the Book). </div> </div> </div>Noddism is my favorite part of the game. I play a Priest of Caine Anarch Malkavian right now. I regularly have him say, &quot;The Church of Caine should be all Kindred's shared faith, the Sabbat are our version of ISIS.&quot; It's his dark secret he's a defector from the sect and he wants to exterminate every Sabbat he can get his hands on while stealing back artifacts from the fallen cities of the Black Hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Godfather with fangs was the most prevalent element across all sects and all of Revised, killing a lot of 'fantasy' and 'unknown' which we had in the second edition. Godfather with fangs is what Sabbat was, with 'satanic shovelheads' you love so much to describe in gory details being just one facet of the sect, limited to New World specifically (Old World Sabbat expressed open disdain towards that element of the sect overseas) and certainly not the most fun to play, with the mainstay being Cartels/Mafia/Evil CIA (Dastur's Black Hand) upped to eleven with vozhd, ritae and abyss mysticism. These spooky elements served to provide atmosphere not to be a centerpiece of the sect's identity. Seriously, GttS 1998 is an epitome of such a serious, grounded depiction. Again, we seem to have read those books in opposite ways. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel like V:TM occasionally went overboard with its expansion of materials. I admit to being a &quot;meat and potatoes&quot; kind of gamer. A typical vampire game for me is:<br /> <br /> * Neonates<br /> * One City<br /> * Local Politcs<br /> * 7 Clans<br /> * Prince as the Big Bad<br /> * Sheriff as his Henchman<br /> <br /> You can play many different kinds but that's just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were shit on 2ed (not so hard as in the next ed), Revised, V20 improved things especially with Anarch's blood magic (it's the best part of the BS book). V5 makes them shine like in 1ed. </div> </div> </div>Its kind of ironic too because the Anarchs of 1st Edition are kind of naff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:30:59-07:00","id":1377849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377842#post1377842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I see, they are not doing them at all.( It's just a start of it, but I bet they do either low Humanity, or homebrew.<br /> The game is centered about survival, escaping the city. Currently it;s about investigations/interrogations rather than discussions or combat/action. They had a Vaulderie at the very start of the sessoin, though. I love Sabbat games which minimize action and make violent scenes short and focused (therefore all the more terrifying).<br /> Contrary to what I saw here in that thread, no recurring themes of satanism and being EEEEVIL for evil's sake. So far so good!</div> </div> </div> </div>So they aren't actually playing a sabbat game then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:33:03-07:00","id":1377850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377846#post1377846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean your interpretation of previous editions is so different from mine that I cannot see how you came to those conclusions, it is like you are describing a completely different book by a different company. And since all V5 sabbat Lore so far is the Devs spitting at us and screaming their hatred of players who like the Sabbat, and missing the point of anything that isn't the Anarchs completely, maybe stop using that steaming pile of excrement as a source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to discuss where you disagree on points. The funny thing is I love the Sabbat and have run games on them all the time. I admit, I have a good fun of Sabbat games because I drew from my STAR WARS D6 experience. There's a lot of fun to be had with &quot;The Fall of an Empire&quot; games as I did some Imperial games in my college years as well.<br /> <br /> Whenever I do Sabbat and Technocrat games, I set the players as much against their superiors as I do their exterior enemies.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I've done more Technocrat games than I've ever done Traditionalist because I feel the Technocrats are better written for a Gothic Punk game while the Traditions are kind of bland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377847#post1377847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same I did. Dozens of VtM books I read are telling a different story, provide a different atmosphere and set a different tone from those you must've read in regards to all sects, but most obviously in regards to the Sabbat. Or you intentionally omit the parts that don't suite your vision of the sect(s).<br /> <br /> Playing your own game and homebrewing is one thing. Twisting the vision set by decades of development to suit your own and try to set it as a mainstream going forward is another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think you've judged a very different interpretation of how I view the Sabbat as a whole from how I view the Sabbat in an Anarch or Camarilla game. Obviously the view of the Sabbat you're going to get from a game where you're not a member is different from one where you are. If the Sabbat doesn't terrify you as a Cammie or Anarch then you're playing them wrong, IMHO.<br /> <br /> But I'm happy to talk to you about how I view them from all angles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:40:00-07:00","id":1377851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377850#post1377850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm happy to discuss where you disagree on points. The funny thing is I love the Sabbat and have run games on them all the time. I admit, I have a good fun of Sabbat games because I drew from my STAR WARS D6 experience. There's a lot of fun to be had with &quot;The Fall of an Empire&quot; games as I did some Imperial games in my college years as well.<br /> <br /> Whenever I do Sabbat and Technocrat games, I set the players as much against their superiors as I do their exterior enemies.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I've done more Technocrat games than I've ever done Traditionalist because I feel the Technocrats are better written for a Gothic Punk game while the Traditions are kind of bland.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) that VtM is a local game. It fundamentally isn't, your interests may, temporarily be local, but the Sect is always there, the international power ready to drop the hammer of you get to far out of line, and that global power is where the really interesting stories are told, global philosophical rivalries and wars, not gangsters with fangs. <br /> <br /> 2)Noddism is the militant wing of the Sabbat, and always was, the Church of Caine is a deliberate insult by paradox to anyone who liked the Sabbat, and yet another slap in the face by the Devs for that part of the player base, like the entire Gehenna crusade, it serves no purpose beyond letting the Anarchs steal more sabbat trappings and ruin them.<br /> <br /> Also your description of your Sabbat game doesn't sound interesting, just as an aside. Ideally a Sabbat game is about 60% external enemies, 20% Path Vs Path, and 20% Pack rivalries, Elder politics tends to be under the Path and Pack headings, with big names (Arch Bishops and Prisci, playing at the Sect 'external enemies' level. When Arch Bishops and Prisci war, regions tremble and packs fall as collateral, when the Paths fall out, (remember they tend to have their own internal priesthoods, and aspirants who want in, while still not being True Sabbat yet) sabbat cities fight each other, the Sects are international supernatural conspiracies, not local criminal gangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-01-2020, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:55:34-07:00","id":1377853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377851#post1377851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) that VtM is a local game. It fundamentally isn't, your interests may, temporarily be local, but the Sect is always there, the international power ready to drop the hammer of you get to far out of line, and that global power is where the really interesting stories are told, global philosophical rivalries and wars, not gangsters with fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of the Transylvania and Giovanni Chronicles, the vast majority of V:TM games I've played have been Chronicles like the Chicago Chronicles. The player characters are Embraced in a single city and they become affiliated with the local sects within a city before expanding their power base and building alliances. They will eventually either overthrow the Prince, get Blood Hunted, or form a power base in alliance with them. Basically, Bloodlines and Coteries of New York is how a typical chronicle goes for me.<br /> <br /> I admit, we have Vampire: The Masquerade: Redemption as a direct contrast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2)Noddism is the militant wing of the Sabbat, and always was, the Church of Caine is a deliberate insult by paradox to anyone who liked the Sabbat, and yet another slap in the face by the Devs for that part of the player base, like the entire Gehenna crusade, it serves no purpose beyond letting the Anarchs steal more sabbat trappings and ruin them. </div> </div> </div>One of the biggest mistakes of the game is denying the awesomeness of Noddism to non-Sabbat players. The Elysium supplement provided Elders with access to Gehenna Cults but I think Caine should be just as popular with the younger sect as people will search for answers after their Embrace. It's not just for Anarchs, though, but all Kindred as the Church of Caine was very popular among the Dark Ages players for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Kindred like Anatole would spread it among Cammies and Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also your description of your Sabbat game doesn't sound interesting, just as an aside. Ideally a Sabbat game is about 60% external enemies, 20% Path Vs Path, and 20% Pack rivalries, Elder politics tends to be under the Path and Pack headings, with big names (Arch Bishops and Prisci, playing at the Sect 'external enemies' level. </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, the blood of your superiors belongs to you if you're strong enough to take it. It's like the Sith. The Sabbat has no need for loyalty because it regularly culls the week. If you're strong enough to kill a superior and take his place, you should.<br /> <br /> Mind you, most infighting is a bit more good natured. The Bishops and Archbishops know to smack down fools who pull this shit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:55:49-07:00","id":1377854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377844#post1377844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like there's a weird bit of fanon going on here because the vast majority of Sabbat were not like the Sabbat of Montreal. The Sabbat of Montreal with their intellectual and scholarly side were explictly outliers and the majority of Sabbat were barely controlled punks that were either going to die horribly or be consumed by the Beast. Also, the Sabbat in Montreal were subject to a large amount of Infernalist infiltration and corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not talking specifically about Montreal, although I would like to stress out how important the city was to the Sabbat - exactly for the purpose of holding inner Darkness, binding it, reforging into weapon - whether social, mental or physical. It was the city of Paths. I am talking about the core of the sect - bishops, templars, inquisition, black hand, oldest covens, Path practicioners, Lasombra and Tzimisce. GttS 1998 sets them exactly as Cartels - extremely disciplined power structure which struggles to combine freedom with loyalty, which holds the ritae sacrosanct and never, ever spits on traditions, Archbishops whose orders are executed with more precision and effort than any Prince's. This is the backbone of the Sabbat, with rob zombie fans being a violent shock troops expendable and uninfiltratable facade whose numbers were never high simply due to war attrition. <br /> Of course the 1998 took a lot from 1997 but simply because 2ed bordered on outright vampiric D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like people ignore the &quot;Sabbat lost to the beast&quot; because it doesn't fit their philosopher kings ideal of them that was never more than a minority. </div> </div> </div>There is so much space between being lost to the beast and being a philosopher king. Montreal sabbat are certainly not kings in any meaningful ways, but they certainly are shepherds - both of the mortal sinners and of their unruly brethren who seek to break the chains of human' consciousness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't like the handling of the Sabbat in V5 as they could have easily inserted the Sabbat as a playable option if they'd included less predator types and in-game fiction in the corebook. Mind you, I'm very glad that they've stopped the Sabbat ripping off the Anarchs and their themes but they went way way too far. I hope they eventually do release a Sabbat book and it's kind of weird they haven't.<br /> <br /> It should be a smaller, darker, more terrifying sect than Revised with the Anarchs being the Camarilla's primary rivals but its still one of the core groups. </div> </div> </div>At least here we can partially agree. Hooray. I would like the sect to be less violent, less OVERTLY terrifying, more detached, more intellectual, more focused and certainly more disciplined - the most rigid of the three, even - organization aimed at forging a new society for the undead and reworking their relations with mortals in a more meaningful way of efficient parasytism. All of this in order to oppose the chthonic forces you would like them to become the slaves of. <br /> <br /> <br /> Going back to one of your arguments, I hope we can agree that there is nothing bad with vampires fighting in the streets. VtM, contrary to VtR, was never limited to social combat only, or didn't even attempt to chastise players for resorting to outright violence, like I felt VtR did. That combat theme was and always will be recurring in roleplay, especially in a game of bloodsucking unhumans. I hope V5 also does not throw it out of the window along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:10:53-07:00","id":1377856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377853#post1377853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the exception of the Transylvania and Giovanni Chronicles, the vast majority of V:TM games I've played have been Chronicles like the Chicago Chronicles. The player characters are Embraced in a single city and they become affiliated with the local sects within a city before expanding their power base and building alliances. They will eventually either overthrow the Prince, get Blood Hunted, or form a power base in alliance with them. Basically, Bloodlines and Coteries of New York is how a typical chronicle goes for me.<br /> <br /> I admit, we have Vampire: The Masquerade: Redemption as a direct contrast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One of the biggest mistakes of the game is denying the awesomeness of Noddism to non-Sabbat players. The Elysium supplement provided Elders with access to Gehenna Cults but I think Caine should be just as popular with the younger sect as people will search for answers after their Embrace. It's not just for Anarchs, though, but all Kindred as the Church of Caine was very popular among the Dark Ages players for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Certainly, Kindred like Anatole would spread it among Cammies and Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the blood of your superiors belongs to you if you're strong enough to take it. It's like the Sith. The Sabbat has no need for loyalty because it regularly culls the week. If you're strong enough to kill a superior and take his place, you should.<br /> <br /> Mind you, most infighting is a bit more good natured. The Bishops and Archbishops know to smack down fools who pull this shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)We disagree on Noddism, no one worthy of the title Noddist can be outside the Sabbat, or on the path of humanity, the core of the faith demands it, it's like a None Communist Bolshevik, an oxymoronic contradiction in terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) I would need a source to show what book turns the hyper disciplined ordo militant with the shovel head shock troops into the incompetent orcs you describe. GttS had them as far more disciplined and unified than the Cam or Anarchs, and that never changed, which is why the Gehenna crusade is such a slap in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-01-2020, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:14:01-07:00","id":1377858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377853#post1377853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the exception of the Transylvania and Giovanni Chronicles, the vast majority of V:TM games I've played have been Chronicles like the Chicago Chronicles. The player characters are Embraced in a single city and they become affiliated with the local sects within a city before expanding their power base and building alliances. They will eventually either overthrow the Prince, get Blood Hunted, or form a power base in alliance with them. Basically, Bloodlines and Coteries of New York is how a typical chronicle goes for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I would not be too far from the truth if I say the very reason VtM got expanded so far and wide in themes, characters and places as it did in 1992-2000 because this type of the 'meat and potato' game was not enough for a big number of players, and said expansion attracted so much more ppl to the setting and keeps them interested. Including me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the end of the day, the blood of your superiors belongs to you if you're strong enough to take it. It's like the Sith. The Sabbat has no need for loyalty because it regularly culls the week. If you're strong enough to kill a superior and take his place, you should.<br /> <br /> Mind you, most infighting is a bit more good natured. The Bishops and Archbishops know to smack down fools who pull this shit. </div> </div> </div>Tbh I never loved infighting and have seen monomacy and stuff more a liability than an asset. Countless killed leaders could've been used in other ways than becoming ash, and countless shattered vinculum bonds caused further bickering, infighting, bitterness and mistrust in otherwise successful packs and whole domains. Although I admit it's an awesome tool in ST's arsenal, one not available to other sects cause, again, other sects are meant to explore different reflections of human nature and society.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:26:41-07:00","id":1377861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377851#post1377851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) that VtM is a local game. It fundamentally isn't, your interests may, temporarily be local, but the Sect is always there, the international power ready to drop the hammer of you get to far out of line, and that global power is where the really interesting stories are told, global philosophical rivalries and wars, not gangsters with fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. Why would there be a need to describe sects across continents and regions in two consecutive editions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2)Noddism is the militant wing of the Sabbat, and always was, the Church of Caine is a deliberate insult by paradox to anyone who liked the Sabbat, and yet another slap in the face by the Devs for that part of the player base, like the entire Gehenna crusade, it serves no purpose beyond letting the Anarchs steal more sabbat trappings and ruin them. </div> </div> </div>I for one do not see the crusade as a failure - it's a chance to burn the fat off Sabbat soul, provide enough action and experience for surviving members and reforge Sabbat into something new, bigger and better, turning them into elite combat/occult monsters who operate like CIA and either abandon Humanity completely, or rework their attitude towards them into something new and more believable than just 'hah stupid cattle'. I think they will start deliberately embracing the most promising humans, being rid of luxury of hitting a random Joe with a shovel and hoping he becomes a worthy post-human monster of the night. They're kinda forced to become picky in order to get the cream of the crop of the most indoctrinated humans, and I can only imagine what new 'cadres' they can recruit in the war zones across the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:33:10-07:00","id":1377863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377849#post1377849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they aren't actually playing a sabbat game then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why not?<br /> <br /> They just finished it. The part with them being followed/surveilled/approached by Ministry for some tricky deal quickly ended, and the action started. Even though it was an action packed game, it was totally justified - they were the prey and almost every other big NY power were the hunters. Still they escaped with 'I'll be back!' feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:35:37-07:00","id":1377865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377861#post1377861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)So much this. Why would there be a need to describe sects across continents and regions in two consecutive editions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2)I for one do not see the crusade as a failure - it's a chance to burn the fat off Sabbat soul, provide enough action and experience for surviving members and reforge Sabbat into something new, bigger and better, turning them into elite combat/occult monsters who operate like CIA and either abandon Humanity completely, or rework their attitude towards them into something new and more believable than just 'hah stupid cattle'. I think they will start deliberately embracing the most promising humans, being rid of luxury of hitting a random Joe with a shovel and hoping he becomes a worthy post-human monster of the night. They're kinda forced to become picky in order to get the cream of the crop of the most indoctrinated humans, and I can only imagine what new 'cadres' they can recruit in the war zones across the world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) agreed.<br /> <br /> 2) hard disagree, we already have the picky, careful and subtle infiltration sect, they are called the Camirilla. While maybe the Sabbat needed to use up some shovel heads, the main enemy, on a daily basis is and should remain the Cam and Anarchs, those are the sword and shield of the Antes, and up until they fall, going after their masters is talking to Mr Stupidity Stone again, and making decisions while concussed and lobotomized. Mass Embrace shock troops work, why give up that tactic? 99% of them die or degenerate, so what? Let them earn their place as True Sabbat or die trying, while carefully selected embraces and ghoul families continue as the night to night peace time process of embrace, the crusade era mass Embrace adds that chaos in to refresh the clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-01-2020, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:51:39-07:00","id":1377867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377865#post1377865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) agreed.<br /> <br /> 2) hard disagree, we already have the picky, careful and subtle infiltration sect, they are called the Camirilla. While maybe the Sabbat needed to use up some shovel heads, the main enemy, on a daily basis is and should remain the Cam and Anarchs, those are the sword and shield of the Antes, and up until they fall, going after their masters is talking to Mr Stupidity Stone again, and making decisions while concussed and lobotomized.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2) We already had the sample of what Sabbat should become - Caine's Chosen, the Black Hand (not the TalmahRa) - while being NOT Camarilla and being NOT Anarchs. Freedom loving idiots can go join the latter, Lasombra schemers already jumped ship for the former. good riddance. with the remaining rest I believe there is no choice for Sabbat to stay overtly violent and shovelhead. Considering the age of smartphones and SI. I would gladly abandon the rob zombie element if they made the whole sabbat like Black Hand of Jalan and Dastur's vision. And I also guess subtlety, precision and competence are necessary when you take on an enemy like the ancients or second inquisition. I understand your mention of the rival sects, but, given the ancients, Caine and all Noddist mythos are now taken for granted, Sabbat would rather welcome converts from the other sects wanting to be red-pilled against the 'lies of the Patriarchs' rather than kill them outright. Kyle Strathcona, one of the most competent and faithful cardinals, was a Camarilla convert.<br /> <br /> I really don't see what's the problem with expanding the dichotomy of subtle careful Cam and unsubtle reckless Sabbat into trichotomy - subtle careful Cam, unsubtle witty Anarchs, zealous and reclusive Sabbat. Camarilla are Methuselahs' 1%, Anarchs are Carthians, Sabbat are Noddist CIA.<br /> Also, did you ever meet a howling, blood-crazed Noddist in the books?: ) I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-01-2020, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T20:12:11-07:00","id":1377869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377867#post1377867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2) We already had the sample of what Sabbat should become - Caine's Chosen, the Black Hand (not the TalmahRa) - while being NOT Camarilla and being NOT Anarchs. Freedom loving idiots can go join the latter, Lasombra schemers already jumped ship for the former. good riddance. with the remaining rest I believe there is no choice for Sabbat to stay overtly violent and shovelhead. Considering the age of smartphones and SI. I would gladly abandon the rob zombie element if they made the whole sabbat like Black Hand of Jalan and Dastur's vision. And I also guess subtlety, precision and competence are necessary when you take on an enemy like the ancients or second inquisition. I understand your mention of the rival sects, but, given the ancients, Caine and all Noddist mythos are now taken for granted, Sabbat would rather welcome converts from the other sects wanting to be red-pilled against the 'lies of the Patriarchs' rather than kill them outright. Kyle Strathcona, one of the most competent and faithful cardinals, was a Camarilla convert.<br /> <br /> I really don't see what's the problem with expanding the dichotomy of subtle careful Cam and unsubtle reckless Sabbat into trichotomy - subtle careful Cam, unsubtle witty Anarchs, zealous and reclusive Sabbat. Camarilla are Methuselahs' 1%, Anarchs are Carthians, Sabbat are Noddist CIA.<br /> Also, did you ever meet a howling, blood-crazed Noddist in the books?: ) I didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Howling and blood crazed? Nope, genocidal and sadistic, hell yes, can you even call yourself a Noddist if you aren't hand crafting holy texts out of the carefully flayed remains of an Archon?<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly sick of the Anarchs stealing the Sabbats thunder, they should go back to being the Cam brats they always were and let the adults in the room 'discuss' matters of importance. (Either that or get obliterated like their total tactical and strategic ineptitude demands). But no, both the proper sects had to go full concussed mode to hand the Anarchs unearned victory, so that the plot tumour they are could metastasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T20:55:14-07:00","id":1377871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377869#post1377869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Howling and blood crazed? Nope, genocidal and sadistic, hell yes, can you even call yourself a Noddist if you aren't hand crafting holy texts out of the carefully flayed remains of an Archon?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one's saying the second part of depiction should be omitted. It's just has to be focused, believable and motivated. I always said devil-tigers of KotE were what Sabbat should have been.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly sick of the Anarchs stealing the Sabbats thunder, they should go back to being the Cam brats they always were and let the adults in the room 'discuss' matters of importance. (Either that or get obliterated like their total tactical and strategic ineptitude demands). But no, both the proper sects had to go full concussed mode to hand the Anarchs unearned victory, so that the plot tumour they are could metastasis. </div> </div> </div>You say it like the Sabbat of Revised were not the strategical dumbasses themselves. Going to war with literally everything supernatural you encounter is a sound plan of winning a sectarian conflict? What good can a sect of reduced numbers (third of Camarilla size) do for their cause if the main question it is occupied with is whether to allow their young ones to roam everywhere unchecked or not? How effective is that in fighting Camarilla or their puppetmasters themselves? The only ones who achieved anything in EastCoast were exactly black hand packs or black hand-led operations, it is stated across GttS and CC books numerous times and it is what basic military principles explain. Inquisition and BH were the last competent parts of a sect falling apart: nomadic loyalists demanding freedom and disobeying orders; shovelhead berzerkers raising hell in Sabbat's own domains (and don;t tell me Sabbat didn;t hold up the silence of the blood or tried to - they always did, although to a lesser extent than other sects); cultured and learned freak shows obsessed with their own depravity; infernalists; those simply too dumb to accomplish anything but too tough to be questioned or removed via monomacy. With Galbraith's death, a new civil war was inevitable even without any gehenna or whatever.<br /> <br /> Side joke: Sabbat's portrayal in revised reminds me of Siege of Terra recent books from Warhammer40k. A coherent and unstoppable rebellion finally reached it's final goal aaaaand everyone of the leaders gone bonkers: torturing civilians for giggles, pursuing personal vendettas, falling into uncontrollable and infinite RAGE, and the leader being simply too high in the empyreans to care; with just one dude out of nine desperately trying to hold it all together.<br /> <br /> I understand your vision for the sect but can't see it as a coherent enitity even in V20 after everything which was described in Revised books. If I wanted to go full unapologetic 'thunder' I'd play 2ed New York or Detroit or Amsterdam.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:12:02-07:00","id":1377873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377871#post1377871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one's saying the second part of depiction should be omitted. It's just has to be focused, believable and motivated. I always said devil-tigers of KotE were what Sabbat should have been.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You say it like the Sabbat of Revised were not the strategical dumbasses themselves. Going to war with literally everything supernatural you encounter is a sound plan of winning a sectarian conflict? What good can a sect of reduced numbers (third of Camarilla size) do for their cause if the main question it is occupied with is whether to allow their young ones to roam everywhere unchecked or not? How effective is that in fighting Camarilla or their puppetmasters themselves? The only ones who achieved anything in EastCoast were exactly black hand packs or black hand-led operations, it is stated across GttS and CC books numerous times and it is what basic military principles explain. Inquisition and BH were the last competent parts of a sect falling apart: nomadic loyalists demanding freedom and disobeying orders; shovelhead berzerkers raising hell in Sabbat's own domains (and don;t tell me Sabbat didn;t hold up the silence of the blood or tried to - they always did, although to a lesser extent than other sects); cultured and learned freak shows obsessed with their own depravity; infernalists; those simply too dumb to accomplish anything but too tough to be questioned or removed via monomacy. With Galbraith's death, a new civil war was inevitable even without any gehenna or whatever.<br /> <br /> Side joke: Sabbat's portrayal in revised reminds me of Siege of Terra recent books from Warhammer40k. A coherent and unstoppable rebellion finally reached it's final goal aaaaand everyone of the leaders gone bonkers: torturing civilians for giggles, pursuing personal vendettas, falling into uncontrollable and infinite RAGE, and the leader being simply too high in the empyreans to care; with just one dude out of nine desperately trying to hold it all together.<br /> <br /> I understand your vision for the sect but can't see it as a coherent enitity even in V20 after everything which was described in Revised books. If I wanted to go full unapologetic 'thunder' I'd play 2ed New York or Detroit or Amsterdam.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not going to argue on Sabbat upholding a masquerade, they flat out do, then claim not to...<br /> <br /> On letting shovelheads roam: hell yes, drop them on a hostile or neutral city, they either win or die, either way is a bonus, maybe they even focus the SI on that city, if so bonus! Let the mortals kill main burn our supernatural.rivals for a while. As to going to war with every supernatural you encounter..yea that's actually accepting the other lines hatred of vampires into the main VtM line, the default setting of mages and changing breeds is 'killing leeches', actually acknowledging that is a nice touch, and should have been more widespread.<br /> <br /> I understood revised differently, and really like the monsters in love with depravity aspects of it, while the rabble on Humanity really spoiled the sect imho, if you aren't on a path, you aren't sabbat, if V5 cannot properly support Paths (and since it doesn't support Humanity I doubt it can). I'd rather they had just removed the Sabbat entirely, just flat retgone them. Then the sickening anarch pestilence would make more sense, and it would be clear only people who like Anarchs are welcome.<br /> <br /> The Black Hand are the exact opposite of what I like about the main Sabbat, I want hordes of shov heads lead by Templar fanatics, not vampire Isis. Give me posthuman monsters and death cultists not fanged ninjas, or vitae commando's, and above all get competent strategic thinkers to write your war plots, because as you admit, it takes beating the Sabbat and Cam with the cretinous club to explain current meta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:14:24-07:00","id":1377874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least here we can partially agree. Hooray. I would like the sect to be less violent, less OVERTLY terrifying, more detached, more intellectual, more focused and certainly more disciplined - the most rigid of the three, even - organization aimed at forging a new society for the undead and reworking their relations with mortals in a more meaningful way of efficient parasytism. All of this in order to oppose the chthonic forces you would like them to become the slaves of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to think of making sure most of the Clans and sects having their own themes as well as parts of the setting. For me, I tend to have the Followers of Set being the intellectual and detached cold blooded philosophers of the undead. It's their niche. I do have Sabbat who have that but I make them a very small inner circle of &quot;True Sabbat&quot; who are distinct from the sect as the whole. They're both the Black Hand and inner cults like the Amis Noctis as well as Metamorphistis. None of them have much loyalty to the sect as a whole. This is not justified in canon but is just how I prefer to do it. The Crazy Horrible Inhuman Monster Sawyer Clan Sabbat exist because they make for very easy to run games. Not because they're terribly fun to play.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle Sabbat are more for True Hand of False Hand games as well as Elder Games. Otherwise, if a player wants to be an inhuman intellectual monster then I recommend they play a Follower of Set or Assamite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to one of your arguments, I hope we can agree that there is nothing bad with vampires fighting in the streets. VtM, contrary to VtR, was never limited to social combat only, or didn't even attempt to chastise players for resorting to outright violence, like I felt VtR did. That combat theme was and always will be recurring in roleplay, especially in a game of bloodsucking unhumans. I hope V5 also does not throw it out of the window along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, I've done many a &quot;Sabbat lays siege to the city&quot; plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)We disagree on Noddism, no one worthy of the title Noddist can be outside the Sabbat, or on the path of humanity, the core of the faith demands it, it's like a None Communist Bolshevik, an oxymoronic contradiction in terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat are kind of embarrassing in canon regarding Noddism. Isn't it canonical that the Path of Caine was made by a bunch of Assamites who didn't want to teach the Path of Blood to their fellow Anarchs? It's just a dumbed down stupid and Book of Nod heretical version of the Path of Blood. Caine forbid diablerie for example.<br /> <br /> Anatole and the Church of Caine are the real Noddists. Hell, the Path of Heaven's followers were nicknamed &quot;Noddists&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) I would need a source to show what book turns the hyper disciplined ordo militant with the shovel head shock troops into the incompetent orcs you describe. GttS had them as far more disciplined and unified than the Cam or Anarchs, and that never changed, which is why the Gehenna crusade is such a slap in the face. </div> </div> </div>From Clan Novel: Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <i>The gathered Sabbat warlords, however, were an even greater uncertainty. Drawn from marauding bands that ravaged the length and breadth of the American countryside, these autonomous mercenary groups gave allegiance to none and respect only to a select few\u2014those who had earned such through trials of fire and sword.<br /> <br /> In less than an hour, Polonia realized, this conference room would be filled with a clamoring throng of the most ruthless tyrants, predators, fanatics, mafiosi, serial killers, highwaymen, ganglords, and anarchists that had been gathered in one place since\u2014well, probably since the onset of the First Crusade.</i><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe Nomad Coalition is here, gentlemen, because the word is out that Atlanta is spoiling for a fight, and you guys don\u2019t have the experience, the firepower, or the balls to carry that fight without us.\u201d A roar and a riot went up from the gathered Nomad war chiefs rose, and even Caldwell was on his feet. A man to Averros\u2019s left brandished a fist in which danced no fewer than three wicked and vitriolic-looking butterfly knives, each blade as long as the man\u2019s forearm.</i><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;This is the big time, tough guy. Whatcha gonna do? These bastards here,\u201d he gestured to the conference table where the rest of the assembly looked on with alternating distaste, detached curiosity, and ill-concealed blood hunger. \u201cYou think these guys are gonna stand with you when they see how you pay back the folks who put you where you are now? Come off it. These guys are the real deal. Hell, these guys are the Sabbat, I mean the real Sabbat. The folks that make things happen. You\u2019re not dealing with a bunch of low-life drifters and clansmen; fugitives and survivalists, weirdoes and cultists, anymore. You think these guys are sitting around waiting for someone to come along and tell them what to do and who to do it to?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I can't imagine where I got the view they were disorganized rabble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understood revised differently, and really like the monsters in love with depravity aspects of it, while the rabble on Humanity really spoiled the sect imho, if you aren't on a path, you aren't sabbat, if V5 cannot properly support Paths (and since it doesn't support Humanity I doubt it can). I'd rather they had just removed the Sabbat entirely, just flat retgone them. Then the sickening anarch pestilence would make more sense, and it would be clear only people who like Anarchs are welcome. </div> </div> </div>You act like Humanity wasn't drastically revised in, well, Revised. In Revised, you could torture a baby by lighting it on fire and playing football with it and still maintain a Humanity 2.<br /> <br /> Humanity 4 was an evil bastard with some sense of honor but treats human beings like cattle.<br /> <br /> Humanity 1 was beyond the most sickest twisted person you have ever met in your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-02-2020, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:30:10-07:00","id":1377875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377874#post1377874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to think of making sure most of the Clans and sects having their own themes as well as parts of the setting. For me, I tend to have the Followers of Set being the intellectual and detached cold blooded philosophers of the undead. It's their niche. I do have Sabbat who have that but I make them a very small inner circle of &quot;True Sabbat&quot; who are distinct from the sect as the whole. They're both the Black Hand and inner cults like the Amis Noctis as well as Metamorphistis. None of them have much loyalty to the sect as a whole. This is not justified in canon but is just how I prefer to do it. The Crazy Horrible Inhuman Monster Sawyer Clan Sabbat exist because they make for very easy to run games. Not because they're terribly fun to play.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle Sabbat are more for True Hand of False Hand games as well as Elder Games. Otherwise, if a player wants to be an inhuman intellectual monster then I recommend they play a Follower of Set or Assamite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, yes, I've done many a &quot;Sabbat lays siege to the city&quot; plot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Sabbat are kind of embarrassing in canon regarding Noddism. Isn't it canonical that the Path of Caine was made by a bunch of Assamites who didn't want to teach the Path of Blood to their fellow Anarchs? It's just a dumbed down stupid and Book of Nod heretical version of the Path of Blood. Caine forbid diablerie for example.<br /> <br /> Anatole and the Church of Caine are the real Noddists. Hell, the Path of Heaven's followers were nicknamed &quot;Noddists&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From Clan Novel: Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <i>The gathered Sabbat warlords, however, were an even greater uncertainty. Drawn from marauding bands that ravaged the length and breadth of the American countryside, these autonomous mercenary groups gave allegiance to none and respect only to a select few\u2014those who had earned such through trials of fire and sword.<br /> <br /> In less than an hour, Polonia realized, this conference room would be filled with a clamoring throng of the most ruthless tyrants, predators, fanatics, mafiosi, serial killers, highwaymen, ganglords, and anarchists that had been gathered in one place since\u2014well, probably since the onset of the First Crusade.</i><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe Nomad Coalition is here, gentlemen, because the word is out that Atlanta is spoiling for a fight, and you guys don\u2019t have the experience, the firepower, or the balls to carry that fight without us.\u201d A roar and a riot went up from the gathered Nomad war chiefs rose, and even Caldwell was on his feet. A man to Averros\u2019s left brandished a fist in which danced no fewer than three wicked and vitriolic-looking butterfly knives, each blade as long as the man\u2019s forearm.</i><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;This is the big time, tough guy. Whatcha gonna do? These bastards here,\u201d he gestured to the conference table where the rest of the assembly looked on with alternating distaste, detached curiosity, and ill-concealed blood hunger. \u201cYou think these guys are gonna stand with you when they see how you pay back the folks who put you where you are now? Come off it. These guys are the real deal. Hell, these guys are the Sabbat, I mean the real Sabbat. The folks that make things happen. You\u2019re not dealing with a bunch of low-life drifters and clansmen; fugitives and survivalists, weirdoes and cultists, anymore. You think these guys are sitting around waiting for someone to come along and tell them what to do and who to do it to?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I can't imagine where I got the view they were disorganized rabble.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You act like Humanity wasn't drastically revised in, well, Revised. In Revised, you could torture a baby by lighting it on fire and playing football with it and still maintain a Humanity 2.<br /> <br /> Humanity 4 was an evil bastard with some sense of honor but treats human beings like cattle.<br /> <br /> Humanity 1 was beyond the most sickest twisted person you have ever met in your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care how depraved you can be on Humanity (well actually I feel sorry for the people who wanted that Path to mean something) I do not want to play a character judged by that morality. Walking a Path should be a hard and very personal thing. Not a ' oh yea just do what you like and never drop below about 3' that is completely the opposite oh what I am asking for, and your constant rehashing of this point is getting old, paths are THE most important tool a vampire has to hold back the beast, and they need to be unwavering iron, not this goopy mess. Humanity is a Path, one of many, one I do not want to walk. The most interesting theme of VtM used to be 'beast I be lest Beast I become' with the new Humanity system (and yes, revised started this) that is totally removed.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat as described in those extracts sounds like a super organized bunch of paramilitary units, with clear command and structure of fealty, not a modern militia by any means, but certainly a medieval army, certainly earning the comparison with a crusader host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:36:27-07:00","id":1377878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377875#post1377875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care how depraved you can be on Humanity (well actually I feel sorry for the people who wanted that Path to mean something) I do not want to play a character judged by that morality. Walking a Path should be a hard and very personal thing. Not a ' oh yea just do what you like and never drop below about 3' that is completely the opposite oh what I am asking for, and your constant rehashing of this point is getting old, paths are THE most important tool a vampire has to hold back the beast, and they need to be unwavering iron, not this goopy mess. Humanity is a Path, one of many, one I do not want to walk. The most interesting theme of VtM used to be 'beast I be lest Beast I become' with the new Humanity system (and yes, revised started this) that is totally removed.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat as described in those extracts sounds like a super organized bunch of paramilitary units, with clear command and structure of fealty, not a modern militia by any means, but certainly a medieval army, certainly earning the comparison with a crusader host.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I'm just saying the vast majority of Sabbat don't stand for anything other than not caring about the judgement of humanity. Being a Path is something I feel should be hard and require a whole devotion of your being to. It's not something people just get by deciding they're not human anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:39:09-07:00","id":1377879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377863#post1377863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why not?<br /> <br /> They just finished it. The part with them being followed/surveilled/approached by Ministry for some tricky deal quickly ended, and the action started. Even though it was an action packed game, it was totally justified - they were the prey and almost every other big NY power were the hunters. Still they escaped with 'I'll be back!' feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Paths. You aren't True Sabbat without one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:41:14-07:00","id":1377880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377878#post1377878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, I'm just saying the vast majority of Sabbat don't stand for anything other than not caring about the judgement of humanity. Being a Path is something I feel should be hard and require a whole devotion of your being to. It's not something people just get by deciding they're not human anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why do you keep mentioning how devalued the Path of Humanity is? I know it get screwed over, doesn't actually make me want to use it....or that anyone on it is capable of becoming anything more than a shovel head. <br /> <br /> A Sabbat vamp who tries to stay on Humanity should wassail, you should not be able to decide you aren't human yet cling to Humanity, it should be just as hard and require just as much commitment as any other path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T21:52:59-07:00","id":1377881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377880#post1377880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why do you keep mentioning how devalued the Path of Humanity is? I know it get screwed over, doesn't actually make me want to use it....or that anyone on it is capable of becoming anything more than a shovel head.<br /> <br /> A Sabbat vamp who tries to stay on Humanity should wassail, you should not be able to decide you aren't human yet cling to Humanity, it should be just as hard and require just as much commitment as any other path.</div> </div> </div> </div>My view is they eventually will but wassail is a lot longer and harder process by Revised. Certainly, most Sabbat WOULD eventually hit it but it's a long and hard road.<br /> <br /> Smarter Sabbat do eventually find something to motivate themselevs or don't feel the need to become sadistic psychopaths reveling in the Beast.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just say no to head soccer.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:04:02-07:00","id":1377882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377881#post1377881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My view is they eventually will but wassail is a lot longer and harder process by Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was an issue with revised. Well for me, but then Paths and what they actually mean was my thing, which lead to loving the 2e Sabbat, revised started the rot, but also did somethings that made sense, Humanity should have stayed hard, but the alignment shovel did have to go, imho it should have been that PCs started as true Sabbat on Paths, and that shovelheads could not get accepted as Fu members until they had joined a Path (which would have neatly set up the alternate path hierarchies as obvious and competitive focuses of loyalty), then you could have that lovely medieval structure the clan novels you quoted adhere to, Lord Vs Liege Vs Church, not a disorganized rabble, but a feudal throwback to contrast with the despotism of the Cam ( seriously Cam Princes are soo 16-17th century royals in what they can do), having the Sabbat as paradoxically using the older organisation is an interesting juxtaposition, with Packs being warbands under the banners of lords, paying supposed fealty to the Regent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:20:27-07:00","id":1377885,"title":"","content":"I actually used to have a very low opinion of Revised's changing to the Sabbat. The Sabbat seemed to go from being a group that had a disdain for humanity to a group that actively cultivated a hatred for them.<br /> <br /> Basically going from, &quot;We're not human, why should we pretend to be human? We need our own morality&quot; to &quot;WE'RE MONSTERS, EVIL, AND BAD! ROARR!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think part of that was Justin Achilli who wanted to keep the central focus on Humanity vs. The Beast with the Sabbat basically being an easy way to opt out of the question. It's also reflected in how he handled the Giovanni as instead of them being alien in morality, they were just sick bastards and evil assholes. Disgusting and WRONG rather than a valid interpretation of an alternate morality system.<br /> <br /> I think he made Humanity more forgiving because he wanted the Elders to be like the Giovanni. Instead of vampires having to avoid murdering people lest they hit Wassail, the Humanity system let Elders and other older vampires be sick degenerates like the Giovanni with blood orgies and baby pies rather than immediately hitting wassail.<br /> <br /> Thus Revised had a lot more Black Dog-esque elements like the way ghouls were degenerate fuck ups as well.<br /> <br /> Revised take on Humanity and Paths contrasted strongly with the Dark Ages and the Roads as well. Dark Ages was more like 2nd Edition Sabbat where the Paths weren't NICE but weren't designed to be sick and wrong out of hand either.<br /> <br /> I always felt something was lost when the Path of Harmony was killed off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:35:00-07:00","id":1377887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377885#post1377885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually used to have a very low opinion of Revised's changing to the Sabbat. The Sabbat seemed to go from being a group that had a disdain for humanity to a group that actively cultivated a hatred for them.<br /> <br /> Basically going from, &quot;We're not human, why should we pretend to be human? We need our own morality&quot; to &quot;WE'RE MONSTERS, EVIL, AND BAD! ROARR!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think part of that was Justin Achilli who wanted to keep the central focus on Humanity vs. The Beast with the Sabbat basically being an easy way to opt out of the question. It's also reflected in how he handled the Giovanni as instead of them being alien in morality, they were just sick bastards and evil assholes. Disgusting and WRONG rather than a valid interpretation of an alternate morality system.<br /> <br /> I think he made Humanity more forgiving because he wanted the Elders to be like the Giovanni. Instead of vampires having to avoid murdering people lest they hit Wassail, the Humanity system let Elders and other older vampires be sick degenerates like the Giovanni with blood orgies and baby pies rather than immediately hitting wassail.<br /> <br /> Thus Revised had a lot more Black Dog-esque elements like the way ghouls were degenerate fuck ups as well.<br /> <br /> Revised take on Humanity and Paths contrasted strongly with the Dark Ages and the Roads as well. Dark Ages was more like 2nd Edition Sabbat where the Paths weren't NICE but weren't designed to be sick and wrong out of hand either.<br /> <br /> I always felt something was lost when the Path of Harmony was killed off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Roads do it better, and as they are based on 2e Paths, they did as well. Justin's approach to revised is what made the pedophile primogen and nazi brujah so easy to believe in the playtest, as they fit 100% for his style, and ironically his desire to re focus on beast Vs humanity, killed humanity as a thing you had to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:49:22-07:00","id":1377888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377887#post1377887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Roads do it better, and as they are based on 2e Paths, they did as well. Justin's approach to revised is what made the pedophile primogen and nazi brujah so easy to believe in the playtest, as they fit 100% for his style, and ironically his desire to re focus on beast Vs humanity, killed humanity as a thing you had to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to expect my players to be around Humanity 5-6 and state they are &quot;good&quot; vampires compared to Elders (1-4) but nowhere human enough to be 7-10 that are &quot;normal&quot; people. Only 12th and 13th generation vampires and Thin Bloods can be that high in humanity as their Beast is weak. If you're a vampire in my games, you probably have some blood on your hands and mortal laws don't apply to you.<br /> <br /> You should just try and not kill innocent people.<br /> <br /> (accent on try)<br /> <br /> <b>The Sabbat vs. Cammies/Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> Mind you, that's my view on Anarchs. Smiling Jack and Juggler alongside the idealist Maldavis and Anita Wainwright types. Mind you, my Anarchs have always been organized and dangerous with the vast majority of them being brutal hardasses and trained killers because you don't survive as an Anarch unless you're able to take down the Sheriff and his deputies as well as work in a group. I always stated in my games that the Anarchs and Camarilla had an uneasy alliance due to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla needed the Anarchs as boots on the ground and the Anarchs didn't have the mortal ties to hide from the mortal authorities or fund themselves. So they growled at each other but didn't exterminate one another but teamed up whenever the Sabbat came to town.<br /> <br /> So its easy for me to believe when the Sabbat vanished for a time that full-scale war erupted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-02-2020, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:56:51-07:00","id":1377889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377888#post1377888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to expect my players to be around Humanity 5-6 and state they are &quot;good&quot; vampires compared to Elders (1-4) but nowhere human enough to be 7-10 that are &quot;normal&quot; people. Only 12th and 13th generation vampires and Thin Bloods can be that high in humanity as their Beast is weak. If you're a vampire in my games, you probably have some blood on your hands and mortal laws don't apply to you.<br /> <br /> You should just try and not kill innocent people.<br /> <br /> (accent on try)<br /> <br /> <b>The Sabbat vs. Cammies/Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> Mind you, that's my view on Anarchs. Smiling Jack and Juggler alongside the idealist Maldavis and Anita Wainwright types. Mind you, my Anarchs have always been organized and dangerous with the vast majority of them being brutal hardasses and trained killers because you don't survive as an Anarch unless you're able to take down the Sheriff and his deputies as well as work in a group. I always stated in my games that the Anarchs and Camarilla had an uneasy alliance due to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla needed the Anarchs as boots on the ground and the Anarchs didn't have the mortal ties to hide from the mortal authorities or fund themselves. So they growled at each other but didn't exterminate one another but teamed up whenever the Sabbat came to town.<br /> <br /> So its easy for me to believe when the Sabbat vanished for a time that full-scale war erupted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where as I like 1/2e humanity. Killing is always a degeneration check, no matter the reason, serial killers wassail, soldiers wassail, find a path, find Golconda or die. That is the point I am trying and failing to make Beast Vs Reason is the absolute core of the setting for me, and Paths, done right , are the perfect expression of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T23:14:28-07:00","id":1377892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377889#post1377889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where as I like 1/2e humanity. Killing is always a degeneration check, no matter the reason, serial killers wassail, soldiers wassail, find a path, find Golconda or die. That is the point I am trying and failing to make Beast Vs Reason is the absolute core of the setting for me, and Paths, done right , are the perfect expression of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I just can't imagine most Camarilla elders being on a Path and that would be the only way they could be the cold blooded monsters they are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T23:27:54-07:00","id":1377893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377892#post1377892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I just can't imagine most Camarilla elders being on a Path and that would be the only way they could be the cold blooded monsters they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kings, Beast, Sin...ok Roads, but Elders being on Roads that they hide from the neonates and ancilla,to let the rabble degenerate, while the Elders live like they always have, and did before the Camarilla was founded. Either Humanity is hard, or why bother having it in gane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T23:30:45-07:00","id":1377894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377893#post1377893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kings, Beast, Sin...ok Roads, but Elders being on Roads that they hide from the neonates and ancilla,to let the rabble degenerate, while the Elders live like they always have, and did before the Camarilla was founded. Either Humanity is hard, or why bother having it in gane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind Humanity being a long road to fall on before you finally drop off but that's just a difference in styles. Both work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T23:35:18-07:00","id":1377895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377894#post1377894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't mind Humanity being a long road to fall on before you finally drop off but that's just a difference in styles. Both work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, but it is impossible to fall off revised or V5 (as you make plain by keeping pointing out sabbat can be on it, if they can it is worthless as a mechanism and should be removed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T23:55:51-07:00","id":1377897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377895#post1377895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, but it is impossible to fall off revised or V5 (as you make plain by keeping pointing out sabbat can be on it, if they can it is worthless as a mechanism and should be removed)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nu Humanity is basically a measure of how close you are to the Beast. So its about betraying your principles or what you believe your Principles are.<br /> <br /> So you only Fall to the Beast if your principles are, &quot;Never Eat Children&quot; then eat a bunch of kids.<br /> <br /> Or if you're Sabbat and, &quot;Never betray the Sabbat&quot;....well, betray the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I think it needs a HUGE amount of detail and revisions to Touchstones (make vampires able to be them or Places and Objects).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T01:47:18-07:00","id":1377902,"title":"","content":"Quick question: the Church of Caine is basically just a modern extension of the Cainite Heresy from Dark Ages, right? (I read that book and loved it.) At least, that was the impression I got from Cults of the Blood Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T02:18:45-07:00","id":1377905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377902#post1377902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question: the Church of Caine is basically just a modern extension of the Cainite Heresy from Dark Ages, right? (I read that book and loved it.) At least, that was the impression I got from Cults of the Blood Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more like Asatru in that it is a revival/recreation of the Cainite Heresy rather than a direct continuation of it. It's possible some vampires involved with it in ye olden times have woken from torpor or passed down the secrets but it seems like they implied, instead, that it's actually some Noddist scholars and Sabbat defectors remade the religion from studying its texts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T02:25:19-07:00","id":1377906,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> thanks. That clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T02:31:57-07:00","id":1377909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377897#post1377897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nu Humanity is basically a measure of how close you are to the Beast. So its about betraying your principles or what you believe your Principles are.<br /> <br /> So you only Fall to the Beast if your principles are, &amp;quot;Never Eat Children&amp;quot; then eat a bunch of kids.<br /> <br /> Or if you're Sabbat and, &amp;quot;Never betray the Sabbat&amp;quot;....well, betray the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I think it needs a HUGE amount of detail and revisions to Touchstones (make vampires able to be them or Places and Objects).</div> </div> </div> </div>That and hunger are my mechanical hang ups with the system, the Stupidity Stone being passed round for the meta being the hang up with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T03:05:59-07:00","id":1377918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377902#post1377902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question: the Church of Caine is basically just a modern extension of the Cainite Heresy from Dark Ages, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but instead of &quot;modern&quot; extension, I'd say &quot;fallen&quot; or &quot;broken&quot; extension,<br /> <br /> the Cainite heresy saw themselves as gods/angels on earth,<br /> the sabbat see themselves as damned creatures<br /> <br /> you could say the sabbat is the Cainite heresy admitting that they were wrong after their spectacular failure during the Inquisition<br /> <br /> at least, that's the big picture<br /> <br /> if we're going into details, the Path of Caine is supposed to have had influence from the Cainite heresy,<br /> the path supposedly was started by Assamite Noddists who allied with Cainite Heresy remnants,<br /> the path of Caine is the most influential in the sect, since sabbat aren't required to be on the path to heed the word of caine (you can be on humanity, and still follow your noddist priest's words)<br /> <br /> however, while the Heresy lives on in the sabbat (to some extent), so do their detractors,<br /> the path of Redemption is the broken legacy of the Road of Heaven (which was the main enemy of the Cainite Heresy during the Dark Ages),<br /> the path of Cathari is supposed to be born of a heretical sect of the Cainite Heresy (a heresy of a heresy), which has now become one of the main paths in the sabbat<br /> <br /> so, yeah...I'm not sure how much we can really say that sabbat is a true extension of the Cainite heresy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T05:01:59-07:00","id":1377928,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> thank you. That\u2019s really helpful. But I meant the Church of Caine, not the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T05:41:39-07:00","id":1377932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377928#post1377928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> thank you. That\u2019s really helpful. But I meant the Church of Caine, not the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh I see, my bad lol<br /> <br /> church of Caine used to be one of the sabbat's names, that's why I confused it with the sabbat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T08:22:45-07:00","id":1377949,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10998_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10998\" data-vbnamecard=\"10998\">Pleiades</a> Dw. It\u2019s cool \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T08:23:26-07:00","id":1377950,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:17:15-07:00","id":1377961,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra wiped out the Dark Ages Church of Caine and stole some of its rituals. Matthew Dawkins did an interview about i somewhere where he discussed that the Church of Caine/Cainite Heresy REALLY hates the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:13:32-07:00","id":1377980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377961#post1377961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra wiped out the Dark Ages Church of Caine and stole some of its rituals. Matthew Dawkins did an interview about i somewhere where he discussed that the Church of Caine/Cainite Heresy REALLY hates the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tho according to the same interview (iirc) originally they weren't going to, it was going to be the Path of Caine pretty much....but that got vetoed, with a 'no sabbat' ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:15:42-07:00","id":1377981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377980#post1377980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tho according to the same interview (iirc) originally they weren't going to, it was going to be the Path of Caine pretty much....but that got vetoed, with a 'no sabbat' ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Sabbat 2.0 wouldn't really be useful for the majority of Vampire players. The Sabbat's reintroduction should be in its own book or the Players Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:22:45-07:00","id":1377982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377981#post1377981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, Sabbat 2.0 wouldn't really be useful for the majority of Vampire players. The Sabbat's reintroduction should be in its own book or the Players Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> so far my hopes for them actually feeling anything like the Sabbat I like are very, very low. I expect them to be a gutted ruin of orcs with fangs tbh, especially if Justin gets to finish turning them into mindless cannon fodder as he keeps attempting. I do not trust ANY book that man works on to do the setting justice any more, good luck to you if you like his work...I no longer do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:49:23-07:00","id":1378009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1331805#post1331805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is where we strongly disagree. The Sabbat was continually taking away things from the Anarchs and Camarilla both. The Sabbat forced itself into their conflict and meant that the Anarchs couldn't be the number one enemy of the Ivory Tower that they were set up to be. The War of the Ages became deemphasized for Sect vs. Sect conflict. It also meant the conflict internally between the Prince and Neonates was dramatically undercut. The Sabbat were always throwing themselves into the storylines that it became very hard to run the other games as they thematically undermined a lot of the rest of the game as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why care about Humanity? Paths of Enlightenment show it's not important!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We're the only ones who care about Noddism and the Antediluvians!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sabbat just was everywhere and other parts of the game suffered for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For me, I feel like the Sabbat was great but they were just too big of a presence. If you want a game that focuses on:<br /> <br /> * Anarchs<br /> * Humanity<br /> * The evils of the Camarilla<br /> * Social interaction<br /> <br /> They just kind of pushed their way in and took up too much of the narrative space. I'm hoping the Sabbat will continue to exist but I hope in a dramatically reduced role--maybe like a 1/10th of its previous size.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat Remnant. People should be able to play the Classic Sabbat but as a faction rather than an all-consuming setting element.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm of the mind that Modiphus will probably include more Sabbat information. The Sabbat is still around in Chicago by Night 5E. They weren't exterminated as some people believed them to be. The Lasombra still have half of their clan staying with them.<br /> <br /> We're really mostly dealing with rumors here.<br /> <br /> It could well be the Sabbat as know them will be fine with the Eldritch Abomination Sabbat (I'm calling them &quot;The Brood&quot; in my game after a certain group in V:TR) just as an enemy they're fighting.<br /> <br /> We just have speculation now and some lost cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get to read the rest of this thread but I felt like I had to respond. You have it really twisted. Its the Anarchs that really get in the way of the central conflict. The main pull is the duality of the two factions- Sabbat and the Camarilla. One tries to masquerade its still human while also pretending the Antediluvians don't exist while all the way furthering their shadow masters plans, while Sabbat embraces its vampirc nature entirely and has their entire sect set to kill the Antediluvians. When I see Anarchs I just ask this question: What are they really in the game for? Why are they a thing? To me I never really saw the Anarchs as important at all to the grand scheme of VTM. They were always a third neutral faction to me. It just strikes me as odd- why are the Anarch even bothering fighting the Camarilla? They are so much alike: they follow humanity, the live in the same cities most of the time, their really squabbles are just political, etc. Sabbat and Camarilla are enemies for supernaturally purposes that fit into the theme of the game. They were an interesting sect. Anarchs are just.. meh. WW really dropped the ball by trying to pull a Ravnos on the entire sect. It just seems illogical to me they'd make the Anarchs one of the new central sects when that was never the case before. Anarchs were the less extreme portion of the Sabbat that split off. They were never meant to be one of the main sects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:53:08-07:00","id":1378011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377982#post1377982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so far my hopes for them actually feeling anything like the Sabbat I like are very, very low. I expect them to be a gutted ruin of orcs with fangs tbh, especially if Justin gets to finish turning them into mindless cannon fodder as he keeps attempting. I do not trust ANY book that man works on to do the setting justice any more, good luck to you if you like his work...I no longer do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect Bloodlines to be the guiding principle for basically how V:TM is going to be treated from now on. It's the most successful incarnation of the World of Darkness and much of the game's reboot seems designed to capture that feeling in every interaction. So the Sabbat of the 5th Edition World of Darkness are going to be patterned around Andrei, the Spider-Head Crabs, the Gang bangers wanting to be Sabbat, the shovelheads, and their fears of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/BAmKuVwxOfs/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> What we've seen of CHAPTERS shows the Sabbat showing up as a death-cult living in the sewers and performing horrific rituals while trying to take the city back from the Camarilla as well as Anarchs. Also, great news that they made an entire Anarch campaign as one of the Stretch Goals. I was going to be annoyed as hell if they were left out as an option in Montreal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:03:28-07:00","id":1378014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't get to read the rest of this thread but I felt like I had to respond. You have it really twisted. Its the Anarchs that really get in the way of the central conflict. </div> </div> </div>The central conflict is the old as shit inhumane vampires vs. the younger modern ones. The Antediluvians to the Methuselahs to the Elders to the Ancilla to the Neonates and the Thin Bloods. Every level being worse than the last until Caine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main pull is the duality of the two factions- Sabbat and the Camarilla. One tries to masquerade its still human while also pretending the Antediluvians don't exist while all the way furthering their shadow masters plans, while Sabbat embraces its vampirc nature entirely and has their entire sect set to kill the Antediluvians. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat are given over wholly to the Beast and wildness, which means they're good Anarch enemies as they show what could happen to them if they abandon their prinicples in the fight against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I see Anarchs I just ask this question: What are they really in the game for? Why are they a thing? </div> </div> </div>Because the game is about resisting being a slave to the Elders, to the people who want to control or destroy you. It's about freedom and slavery. Unless a PC is a toady or a kiss up, they're almost certainly Anarchs by default by resisting.<br /> <br /> To go back to Bloodlines, &quot;Does your character kiss La Croix's ring?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me I never really saw the Anarchs as important at all to the grand scheme of VTM. They were always a third neutral faction to me. It just strikes me as odd- why are the Anarch even bothering fighting the Camarilla? </div> </div> </div>My assumption is because the Camarilla wants to destroy them because they're competitors for blood and threats to the power. The Anarchs want to live their own lives but they can't because they're uncontrolled and Elders fear anything they don't want to control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sabbat and Camarilla are enemies for supernaturally purposes that fit into the theme of the game. </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem of Camarilla vs. Sabbat is that the Camarilla ends up looking like the good guys and that undermines them as a sect that's corrosive, evil, and all-consuming. You need to show the Camarilla isn't a necessary evil to show its true horrifying potential. The Anarchs also make the Sabbat's claims of freedom and liberty look like a joke, which also makes the Sabbat more interesting.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat and Camarilla also make you question if the Anarch cause is worth it since both the Cammies and Sabbat show there's more power in extrees.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They were an interesting sect. Anarchs are just.. meh. WW really dropped the ball by trying to pull a Ravnos on the entire sect. It just seems illogical to me they'd make the Anarchs one of the new central sects when that was never the case before. Anarchs were the less extreme portion of the Sabbat that split off. They were never meant to be one of the main sects. </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs were certainly a central sect in Bloodlines. Also, the Sabbat broke away from the Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:13:07-07:00","id":1378016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378011#post1378011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expect Bloodlines to be the guiding principle for basically how V:TM is going to be treated from now on. It's the most successful incarnation of the World of Darkness and much of the game's reboot seems designed to capture that feeling in every interaction. So the Sabbat of the 5th Edition World of Darkness are going to be patterned around Andrei, the Spider-Head Crabs, the Gang bangers wanting to be Sabbat, the shovelheads, and their fears of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What we've seen of CHAPTERS shows the Sabbat showing up as a death-cult living in the sewers and performing horrific rituals while trying to take the city back from the Camarilla as well as Anarchs. Also, great news that they made an entire Anarch campaign as one of the Stretch Goals. I was going to be annoyed as hell if they were left out as an option in Montreal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well crap, there goes everything actually interesting about the Sabbat into the dumpster. and as you may have guessed I flat hate the anarchs, (maybe due to the experience of the 'that guy' of LARP and TT ALWAYS being the anarch, dozens of 'that guy' over decades...always the anarch.) EDIT: Dozens is an over statement, maybe a dozen, but yea, never the Cam guy or the Sabbat guy, anecdotal, but it is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:21:22-07:00","id":1378018,"title":"","content":"The fight between the Sabbat and Camarilla were never about good vs evil. Its about supernatural ideological differences and the fact that the Sabbat want to destroy the backers of the Camarilla. Not only that it was the Anarchs that literally broke away from the Sabbat not the other way around. The Anarchs are focused on pretty human-like things and emotions, while the Sabbat were always about cracking down literal progenitors of ALL Vampire society. The dichotomy of the Anarchs vs Camarilla really doesn't make sense to me. What happens to an Anarch who is really old in age and starts siring childe on its own? Doesn't she become an Elder through that herself? Not only with this you also get the Sabbat really really wrong. They haven't &quot;given themselves&quot; wholly to the Beast. Its like you never even read any of the Paths of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> They have different curated ways of managing the Beast while not being tied down pretending to be still human. Your argument saying that they would be a good example for Anarchs of &quot;what would happen if they'd lose their principles fighting the Camarilla&quot; don't make sense because of that. Its as if you don't even know any of the lore regarding the Sabbat at all. Even with that mentioned, the Anarchs don't really have any principles to begin with. Their just a conglomeration of young Kindred apparently fighting against the Camarilla just 'cuz. At the end of things the Anarchs aren't really compelling at all. I don't know why WW would make them the new center faction. The Camarilla vs Sabbat paradigm was as good as you could get. Instead of removing the Sabbat they should've added new sects to spice up the Jyhad- I've always wondered why they've only stuck with only three. Like you said before though- the Anarchs were a third neutral faction to level off the two extremes of the Camarilla and the Sabbat. With this in mind though, they were never to be really taken seriously or have that much in the Jyhad other than being a mercenary faction that the other two were supposed to utilize in an opportunistic moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-02-2020, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:37:56-07:00","id":1378020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378018#post1378018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fight between the Sabbat and Camarilla were never about good vs evil. Its about supernatural ideological differences and the fact that the Sabbat want to destroy the backers of the Camarilla. Not only that it was the Anarchs that literally broke away from the Sabbat not the other way around. The Anarchs are focused on pretty human-like things and emotions, while the Sabbat were always about cracking down literal progenitors of ALL Vampire society. The dichotomy of the Anarchs vs Camarilla really doesn't make sense to me. What happens to an Anarch who is really old in age and starts siring childe on its own? Doesn't she become an Elder through that herself? Not only with this you also get the Sabbat really really wrong. They haven't &quot;given themselves&quot; wholly to the Beast. Its like you never even read any of the Paths of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> They have different curated ways of managing the Beast while not being tied down pretending to be still human. Your argument saying that they would be a good example for Anarchs of &quot;what would happen if they'd lose their principles fighting the Camarilla&quot; don't make sense because of that. Its as if you don't even know any of the lore regarding the Sabbat at all. Even with that mentioned, the Anarchs don't really have any principles to begin with. Their just a conglomeration of young Kindred apparently fighting against the Camarilla just 'cuz. At the end of things the Anarchs aren't really compelling at all. I don't know why WW would make them the new center faction. The Camarilla vs Sabbat paradigm was as good as you could get. Instead of removing the Sabbat they should've added new sects to spice up the Jyhad- I've always wondered why they've only stuck with only three. Like you said before though- the Anarchs were a third neutral faction to level off the two extremes of the Camarilla and the Sabbat. With this in mind though, they were never to be really taken seriously or have that much in the Jyhad other than being a mercenary faction that the other two were supposed to utilize in an opportunistic moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue is that I see the Sabbat as a massive number of hypocrites and that their quest is ultimately a failure. The statement here is that I don't &quot;understand&quot; the Sabbat or the Paths. No, I understand them just fine. It's just I go with the Revised view of them. Maybe 1% of the Sabbat successfully manage to get on a Path and become a high level practicioner of it and maybe 5% of Sabbat period are on a Path in my games. 10% if they're Tzimisce or Lasombra. The vast majority do not have the spiritual, mental, and social fortitude to divest themselves of humanity to get on a Path. This is compared to the Followers of Set where almost all of them do it.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of the Sabbat are simply Low Humanity and indulging in every possible vice and violence they can in the belief they're achieving spiritual perfection. They drink blood like junkies take heroin, except there's an unlimited amount of heroin walking around. They're all Blood Bound and intoxicated by the Black Hands religion as well as the Vaulderie, resulting in them having almost no freedom. They're an army claiming freedom but their every moment of unlife is dictated to them by their Packs, Priests, and Rituals.<br /> <br /> The irony is they're 100% correct about Gehenna, the Antediluvians, and the Jyhad but they're completely under their masters control just like the Camarilla. They're just pawns killing Camarilla Elders and Anarchs to prevent either group from getting strong enough to oppose the Antediluvians' will. The Sabbat could have been the salvation of the Kindred race but they're a failure and were well before V5 for me.<br /> <br /> The question is whether there is a group that can save them.<br /> <br /> In simpler terms, &quot;The False Hand, True Hand, Web of Knives, and Setites are the real deal. The majority of Sabbat are poseurs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I think makes them INTERESTING to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:52:33-07:00","id":1378022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378020#post1378020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the issue is that I see the Sabbat as a massive number of hypocrites and that their quest is ultimately a failure. The statement here is that I don't &quot;understand&quot; the Sabbat or the Paths. No, I understand them just fine. It's just I go with the Revised view of them. Maybe 1% of the Sabbat successfully manage to get on a Path and become a high level practicioner of it and maybe 5% of Sabbat period are on a Path in my games. 10% if they're Tzimisce or Lasombra. The vast majority do not have the spiritual, mental, and social fortitude to divest themselves of humanity to get on a Path. This is compared to the Followers of Set where almost all of them do it.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of the Sabbat are simply Low Humanity and indulging in every possible vice and violence they can in the belief they're achieving spiritual perfection. They drink blood like junkies take heroin, except there's an unlimited amount of heroin walking around. They're all Blood Bound and intoxicated by the Black Hands religion as well as the Vaulderie, resulting in them having almost no freedom. They're an army claiming freedom but their every moment of unlife is dictated to them by their Packs, Priests, and Rituals.<br /> <br /> The irony is they're 100% correct about Gehenna, the Antediluvians, and the Jyhad but they're completely under their masters control just like the Camarilla. They're just pawns killing Camarilla Elders and Anarchs to prevent either group from getting strong enough to oppose the Antediluvians' will. The Sabbat could have been the salvation of the Kindred race but they're a failure and were well before V5 for me.<br /> <br /> The question is whether there is a group that can save them.<br /> <br /> In simpler terms, &quot;The False Hand, True Hand, Web of Knives, and Setites are the real deal. The majority of Sabbat are poseurs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I think makes them INTERESTING to play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You liked the revised devastation of the Sabbat into mindless bogeymen, fair enough, V5 looks set to continue that pattern of making them muhahaha pointless evuuull ofr the lulz. That is never what I like about them, and was hoping for them to be made an actual playable faction again rather than cartoon villians, you quotes from the Novels showed what could be, warlords and high priests, crusaders worthy of the name, with the good and bad that come with that, that is not what Revised gave us, and not what V5 looks to be doing either, it really looks like Anarch or gtfo is the position of the devs, so gtfo it will have to be. I vastly prefered 2e, while the shovel of enlightenment was a hand wave, it made a vastly better and more interesting sect than what came after, as in fact did Humanity as it was in first and 2e, impossible for a killer to maintain, genuinely hard, and something you had to think about, all the time, like all Paths should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:37:35-07:00","id":1378037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378022#post1378022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You liked the revised devastation of the Sabbat into mindless bogeymen, fair enough, V5 looks set to continue that pattern of making them muhahaha pointless evuuull ofr the lulz. That is never what I like about them, and was hoping for them to be made an actual playable faction again rather than cartoon villians, you quotes from the Novels showed what could be, warlords and high priests, crusaders worthy of the name, with the good and bad that come with that, that is not what Revised gave us, and not what V5 looks to be doing either, it really looks like Anarch or gtfo is the position of the devs, so gtfo it will have to be. I vastly prefered 2e, while the shovel of enlightenment was a hand wave, it made a vastly better and more interesting sect than what came after, as in fact did Humanity as it was in first and 2e, impossible for a killer to maintain, genuinely hard, and something you had to think about, all the time, like all Paths should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify because I think there's some questions, I actually flat out hate how V5 has treated the Sabbat. It's weird because everyone looks at me as the guy who defends V5 and it's my 2nd favorite version of V:TM but that doesn't mean I don't have criticisms of it. It's just that when so many other people hate EVERYTHING about V5 there's nothing to discuss about criticisms in a largely positive experience.<br /> <br /> If you're at all interested, though, here's my opinion.<br /> <br /> <b>How I would have done V5 Sabbat</b><br /> <br /> The first thing I would have done would have been to have the Sabbat detailed in the main book. I would have removed some Predator types and fiction to make sure that both the Lasombra, Tzimisce, Obternation (Oblivion), and Vicissitude (Protean) were all detailed as powers. If you want to eliminate the Ravnos, fine, but the Lasombra and Tzimicse are groups that needed detailing. I would have also at least inserted rules for using the Sabbat as potential villains if not a player faction. THEN I would have made DAMN sure that the Sabbat would have gotten their own book. It would have been THE ANARCH, THE CAMARILLA, and then THE SABBAT.<br /> <br /> And what would I have changed?<br /> <br /> I love the Lasombra defection but I think that the Gehenna Crusade is kind of wasteful. Instead, I would have said that the Gehenna Crusade was a massive failure of the Sabbat and that a large number of its strategic reserve went out under Cardinal Polonia to destroy the Antediluvians, only to instead start returning as Low Generation servants of the Antediluvians. This would be like THREAT NULL from Mage Revised and they would give the Sabbat a new enemy to fight. They'd be the Satanic Belial's Brood irredeemable monster types and all of the demon worshiping types have joined them.<br /> <br /> I would also have the Sabbat currently broken up into feuding sub-sects and make a lot of interesting conflicts to be had here. The Loyalists to the Sabbat would defect to the Anarchs (ironic) and they would have made the Anarchs much more dangerous. The Black Hand would take over their own cities and have military dictatorships they directly controlled. The Inquisition would breakaway and become its own faction as well while a lot of Archbishops would fortify their cities while claiming to be loyal to the Sabbat yet only looking after themselves. The Sabbat would have lost cities to the Drowned, Anarchs, Second Inquisition, and Camarilla in its feuds.<br /> <br /> There is no Regent or there's 15 Regents, depending on who you ask.<br /> <br /> The theme of the Sabbat would be questioning whether the PCs can rebuild the Sword of Caine, reunite its factions, or whether it'd be better to reform it as a smaller and deadlier organization. The Sabbat Civil War would still be raging decades after it started in Beckett's Jyhad Diary and it would be the Sabbat vs. Anarchs vs. Camarilla vs. Drowned Legacies. It's a dark time for the Sabbat but may have forced them to cast aside a lot of their fat.<br /> <br /> <b>How this impacts the Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> The Sabbat defectors to the Anarchs cause the Movement to change and become much more militant. All the wild, unchained, psychopathic Kindred are now of the Anarch kind. They also are the reason the Anarch become more effective at holding territory. A lot of the Sabbats games and worst qualities get absorbed by the Anarchs. It causes a big rift the Anarchs as the Sabbat way infects their nastier members while repulsing others. It's also clear the Anarchs get things DONE. The Loyalists, the former Panders Clan, and others also find the Anarchs MUCH more to their tastes than the Sabbat ever was. There will be no law under them. Each Kindred is a Prince or Archbishop to himself.<br /> <br /> The Ministry, of course, welcomes the Sabbat and the two get along like firehoses.<br /> <br /> Ironically, it does also help that many of their leaders who defect ARE better at organizing Anarchs and its possible this will just lead to a Sabbat 2.0.<br /> <br /> <b>How this impacts the Camarilla</b><br /> <br /> The loss of the Sabbat allows some temporary gains for the Camarilla as they gain Mexico City, Montreal, and a bunch of other cities on the East Coast. They also immediately lose the Anarchs, the Gangrel, and the Brujah because without the Sabbat to justify their oppression--the Anarchs become the new biggest threat there is. Many Sabbat Elders, mostly Lasombra, defect to the Camarilla simply because it's the only game in town and it was never about sect vs. sect anyway. The vast wealth of the Sabbat disappears into Camarilla coffers and it grows stronger in its control over industries as well as groups that their ghoul families handled for them.<br /> <br /> But these Sabbat defectors are a poisonous vitae as the Camarilla starts tearing itself apart with the sudden introduction of so many schemers and murderers that are every bit as good, if not better than the Ventrue. The Tremere said not to let them in and were ignored, which means they watch from the sidelines as so many Princes fall to their new Scourges or Primogen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-02-2020, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T14:29:53-07:00","id":1378047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377853#post1377853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the biggest mistakes of the game is denying the awesomeness of Noddism to non-Sabbat players. The Elysium supplement provided Elders with access to Gehenna Cults but I think Caine should be just as popular with the younger sect as people will search for answers after their Embrace. It's not just for Anarchs, though, but all Kindred as the Church of Caine was very popular among the Dark Ages players for obvious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I would love to talk more about this, but it really deserves its own thread. I don't want to hijack this one, but I will say a few comments.<br /> <br /> I love Gehenna Cults and try to include them (or at least one of them) as a secret in any chronicle I run. And for those elders who are not actual members, they usually know (or think they know, or suspect) some level of ultra top level-Jyhad knowledge.<br /> <br /> Another element I try to include in the game is what I call &quot;knowledge of the Antedeluvian world&quot;. This includes, but is not the same as, Sabbat style Noddist lore. &quot;Noddism&quot; specifically interprets &quot;Cain&quot; and the Antedeluvians through the lens of Abrahamic mythology. Most of its tenets is based on earlier interpretations and secondary/tertiary/etc. sources that existed during the time of the Anarch Revolt, and thus were already steeped in interpretations in cultures dominated by the Christian and Muslim worldviews. &quot;Knowledge of the Antedeluvian world&quot; is a more open study that includes other interpretations of the &quot;Antedeluvian World&quot; (as well as traditional Noddism). That includes things like using the older Sumerian mythologies, Atlantis, REH or CAS style pre-Cataclysm setting, Theosophical theories, and more. Studies into the Antedeluvian World done outside the Sabbat is much more likely to include these alternative methodologies because the study isn't regulated by a religious cult. (Of course, the Followers of Set have their own interpretation of this as well influenced by Egyptian mythology and their own Typhonist interpretations).<br /> <br /> And there is any number of Kindred, Clans, secret societies, and individuals in the Camarilla and Anarchs who are interested in this by a variety of motives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T14:54:32-07:00","id":1378053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1377873#post1377873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not going to argue on Sabbat upholding a masquerade, they flat out do, then claim not to...<br /> <br /> On letting shovelheads roam: hell yes, drop them on a hostile or neutral city, they either win or die, either way is a bonus, maybe they even focus the SI on that city, if so bonus! Let the mortals kill main burn our supernatural.rivals for a while. As to going to war with every supernatural you encounter..yea that's actually accepting the other lines hatred of vampires into the main VtM line, the default setting of mages and changing breeds is 'killing leeches', actually acknowledging that is a nice touch, and should have been more widespread.<br /> <br /> I understood revised differently, and really like the monsters in love with depravity aspects of it, while the rabble on Humanity really spoiled the sect imho, if you aren't on a path, you aren't sabbat, if V5 cannot properly support Paths (and since it doesn't support Humanity I doubt it can). I'd rather they had just removed the Sabbat entirely, just flat retgone them. Then the sickening anarch pestilence would make more sense, and it would be clear only people who like Anarchs are welcome.<br /> <br /> The Black Hand are the exact opposite of what I like about the main Sabbat, I want hordes of shov heads lead by Templar fanatics, not vampire Isis. Give me posthuman monsters and death cultists not fanged ninjas, or vitae commando's, and above all get competent strategic thinkers to write your war plots, because as you admit, it takes beating the Sabbat and Cam with the cretinous club to explain current meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for providing awesome pack names for my future Sabbat chronicle. Vitae Commando sounds nice.<br /> Being serious though, Black Hand IS both. They ARE posthuman monsters who perform the role of vitae commandos because no one else in the whole VtM world would. It's their burden and duty, not a privilege. They follow Paths AND they think with their heads not their fangs.<br /> <br /> Competent strategic thinkers in Sabbat already are among BH dominions or cardinals only. Nomads and shovelheads are shock troops, and templars are the only adequate force keeping them focused, without them, the forefront of the sect will just degrade into hundreds of splinetered death cults with extremely low unlife expectancy.<br /> <br /> Shoevelheads led by Templars ARE vampire ISIS. Deranged, fully indoctrinated, succumbed to the Beast. If you are concerned with Paths, than no shovelhead mob can follow the Paths. Not in any of editions. They are either low Humanity or at low Path of Night (with the latter quickly ascending to position of leaders of the former). Again, you can check Montreal 1997 book. There are no shovelheads. Literally. Even the youngest Cainites (1992 embraced, like Sister Evelyn, or 1983 like Marie-Helene Dutoit) are adherents of Paths, albeit just starting on levels 2-3, and none - NONE - of Montreal cainites were mass-embraced.<br /> <br /> Being in love with your own depravity was a facet of specific Paths, not all of them - paths like Feral Heart, Scorched Heart, Death and the Soul or Honorable Accord simply abstein from anything regarding depravity, seeing it as hindrance rather than a bonus of undeath. And even those which fully embraced the vice (Cathari, Lilith, Caine, Metamorphosis, and, partially, Redemption) as core, actually encouraged or rather instructed their followers into exploring and scrutinizing their personal darkness, digging much deeper than just being a douchebag of the night like the pathetic path of night wants you to be (another vile creation of revised edition).<br /> <br /> OK I am being too rough to Metamorphosis. They were at the forefront of Tzimisce as the clan and as the concept, and represent a very important part of the Sabbat - the one which wants to go above and beyond. Probably the most vampiric thing in VtM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From Clan Novel: Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The gathered Sabbat warlords, however, were an even greater uncertainty. Drawn from marauding bands that ravaged the length and breadth of the American countryside, these autonomous mercenary groups gave allegiance to none and respect only to a select few\u2014those who had earned such through trials of fire and sword.<br /> <br /> In less than an hour, Polonia realized, this conference room would be filled with a clamoring throng of the most ruthless tyrants, predators, fanatics, mafiosi, serial killers, highwaymen, ganglords, and anarchists that had been gathered in one place since\u2014well, probably since the onset of the First Crusade.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Nomad Coalition is here, gentlemen, because the word is out that Atlanta is spoiling for a fight, and you guys don\u2019t have the experience, the firepower, or the balls to carry that fight without us.\u201d A roar and a riot went up from the gathered Nomad war chiefs rose, and even Caldwell was on his feet. A man to Averros\u2019s left brandished a fist in which danced no fewer than three wicked and vitriolic-looking butterfly knives, each blade as long as the man\u2019s forearm.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> &quot;This is the big time, tough guy. Whatcha gonna do? These bastards here,\u201d he gestured to the conference table where the rest of the assembly looked on with alternating distaste, detached curiosity, and ill-concealed blood hunger. \u201cYou think these guys are gonna stand with you when they see how you pay back the folks who put you where you are now? Come off it. These guys are the real deal. Hell, these guys are the Sabbat, I mean the real Sabbat. The folks that make things happen. You\u2019re not dealing with a bunch of low-life drifters and clansmen; fugitives and survivalists, weirdoes and cultists, anymore. You think these guys are sitting around waiting for someone to come along and tell them what to do and who to do it to?&quot;<br /> <br /> I can't imagine where I got the view they were disorganized rabble. </div> </div> </div>First of all, the text is quite on point. Emphasis is on *Nomad Coalition* - the Nomads, who were always the most unruly bunch of the sect; the ones who once waged war against the founded covens and started one of the the civil wars; the ones who comprise the most of the Loyalist faction; the Loyalists who are Anarchs in disguise. These dudes are going to join Anarchs as soon as the word spreads there are real Antediluvians out there and you have to fight them according to the Code of Milan; these dudes barely give two hecks about the Code, or Antediluvians or Paths or Caine (you mean the psycothic grocer from the Bible lol!) or whatever. Say hello not to the disorganized Sabbat &quot;core&quot; but to your future allies amongst Anarchs. <br /> You quoted a text on the most Anarch part of the sect. <br /> Nomads are not the core of the Sabbat.<br /> Second, there is nothing in the quotation which points to them being Satan worshipping mindless bodybags - yes, they are rabble, but rabble tough as nails, rabble which would not survive decades of unlife out of the city havens without wit and brain. Mostly like your Anarchs are. I see no difference between this Sabbat and the Anarchs you envision. Nomads were always a wild card, an efficient fighting force you can or cannot rely on to complete the sect's objectives, and only the tactical ones - they never gave a damn about strategic ones. Only Black Hand and Inquisition did.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you want to see the core of the Sabbat, please quote Archons &amp; Templars or MbN or Chaining the Beast books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T15:03:17-07:00","id":1378055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378020#post1378020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the issue is that I see the Sabbat as a massive number of hypocrites and that their quest is ultimately a failure. The statement here is that I don't &quot;understand&quot; the Sabbat or the Paths. No, I understand them just fine. It's just I go with the Revised view of them. Maybe 1% of the Sabbat successfully manage to get on a Path and become a high level practicioner of it and maybe 5% of Sabbat period are on a Path in my games. 10% if they're Tzimisce or Lasombra. The vast majority do not have the spiritual, mental, and social fortitude to divest themselves of humanity to get on a Path. This is compared to the Followers of Set where almost all of them do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>AGAIN, all books on Sabbat, especially - MbN. GttS 2 edition, Archons and Templars, Midnight Siege, Caine's Chosen - point to Sabbat being the SAME as Setites or rather tougher. Sabbat vampires were designed to be the only ones among vampires with enough social and mental fortitude to divest themselves of humanity, (for the hundred time, check Montreal by Night), with the number of the ones on that road being significantly reduced in revised/V20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The vast majority of the YOUNG Sabbat, IN REVISED, are simply Low Humanity </div> </div> </div>Fixed it for you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T15:05:36-07:00","id":1378056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378055#post1378055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixed it for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of vampires are young vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T15:15:14-07:00","id":1378057,"title":"","content":"It is interesting how three users arguing on the subject got their own three different versions of the same sect.<br /> <br /> Actually, I think, after all of this rambling over edition differences in regards to Sabbat vision, the ultimate question at the end of the night is this: Who the players would rather like to play?<br /> I am in no position of speaking for many, I would like to share my suggestions on the subject.<br /> <br /> Whether they would like to play<br /> - Sabbat thunder, depravity at it's core, second edition blood bath, Camarilla-Sabbat-Anarchs war, Paths at the core of the sect, military sectarian international conflict?<br /> - Sabbat depravity and satanism, no deep philosophical themes, Humanity 2, Revised bloodbaths, heavy occult, methuselah-possessed, shovelhead mob, vampire locust, vampire isis, boogeymen with fangs?<br /> - Sabbat secret service, indoctrination, subtlety, philosophy and psychology mixed with combat and occult, Paths as a nice addition, focus on the war with Ancients rather than sectarian conflict?<br /> <br /> is up to debate.<br /> <br /> With a deep sigh, I have to conclude - let's just wait for the V5 book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:22:29-07:00","id":1378077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378056#post1378056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vast majority of vampires are young vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed the vital part..in Revised aka the Justin Hates the Sabbat edition, aka the start of the rot edition, where all this edge lord bullcrap that infests V5 started,. I didn't realize how deep the infection was until this thread tb, or just how far the desire to destroy everything interesting about VtM went. Your description of what you want to do to the Sabbat sounds like a nightmare, a complete waste of their themes and stories, and simply another ploy to force the irrelevant, boring, flat disgusting Anarchs onto center stage, they aren't fun, they aren't cool, they aren't interesting, and they never have been, the game would be far better served destroying them rather than, as you demand, destroying the Sabbat. I have never had a positive experience with Anarchs, not in over two decades of various chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},