=1378113#post1378113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I like fanged superheroes. : (</div> </div> </div> </div>90% of my game is something supernatural is afoot and the PCs have to hit it with a fire ax until it's dead.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:00:57-07:00","id":1378124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378113#post1378113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I like fanged superheroes. : (</div> </div> </div> </div>As a playstyle , sure, as one of the sects..not so much. You can't have, as is currently the case the Anarchs as the no brainer auto pick with plot armour and auto victory, and expect to tell an interesting story.. currently the meta is 'why the Anarchs are the bestest and coolest' and that is not compelling at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:10:12-07:00","id":1378126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378123#post1378123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 90% of my game is something supernatural is afoot and the PCs have to hit it with a fire ax until it's dead.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fun sometimes, I way prefer exploring the Paths and Roads, and planning/execution of crusades, but I know that's pretty niche. Just like the dichotomy of philosophy Vs politics Vs logistics Vs 'screw it dragons breath and a broadsword ftw'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:15:38-07:00","id":1378128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378094#post1378094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When you're a Sabbat, you have no humanity. You're damned, you're evil, and you have no salvation--you revel in the Beast. It's what you've chosen. There's no horror because your story is over. Wassail or becoming a Cthulhu cultist (following a Path) with SAN 0 is your fate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's, like, your opinion, man. Many of us don't view Paths that way at all, whatsoever. It's frankly an insulting oversimplification of what Paths and playing characters on Paths is about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:30:09-07:00","id":1378132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378128#post1378128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's, like, your opinion, man. Many of us don't view Paths that way at all, whatsoever. It's frankly an insulting oversimplification of what Paths and playing characters on Paths is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you view Paths in terms of personal horror? I thought they'd be after you've abandoned humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:36:28-07:00","id":1378135,"title":"","content":"I view paths as exploring an alien mindset, with it's own complexity and complications, not as becoming a &quot;Chuthlu Cultist&quot;, or becoming &quot;SAN 0&quot; or anything so boring and simplistic. The horror is in trying to balance your beliefs with practical realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:03:32-07:00","id":1378140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378135#post1378135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I view paths as exploring an alien mindset, with it's own complexity and complications, not as becoming a &quot;Chuthlu Cultist&quot;, or becoming &quot;SAN 0&quot; or anything so boring and simplistic. The horror is in trying to balance your beliefs with practical realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh I write Cthulhu novels so I very much love Cthulhu religions and mindsets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:05:29-07:00","id":1378142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378132#post1378132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you view Paths in terms of personal horror? I thought they'd be after you've abandoned humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The horror is in trying to think in alien ways, to channel an inhuman and inhumane mindset in a convincing way, in fact you said it earlier, Paths aren't nice, but they used to at least make a twisted sense, that sense is where the horror lies, it is a different morality, and a different set of comprises with the beast, but it is still self Vs the beast. Personally I find that more difficult, and more horrific than humanity manages, humanity has the comfort of the familiar, of still being comfortable, Paths don't, they ask you to twist your base assumptions in ways that intrinsically aren't familiar.<br /> <br /> Earlier you used Bloodlines as an example...their is no personal horror in that game, the protagonist is just a fanged hero, being pulled out of the fire every so often by Nines the superawesome anarch ...yea....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:47:16-07:00","id":1378157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378123#post1378123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">90% of my game is something supernatural is afoot and the PCs have to hit it with a fire ax until it's dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that could be true in a lot of games, such as Call of Cthulhu, D&amp;D, Pathfinder, Teenagers from Outer Space...<br /> <br /> Anyway, all the vampires are bad, and the Sabbat are (or were as of V5) the most overt in their evil, while the Camarilla are all faceless corporate evil. The Anarchs are terrorists and rabble, but still inhuman killers for all of that. <br /> <br /> But wasn't this thread about the Montreal boardgame?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:51:44-07:00","id":1378159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378157#post1378157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that could be true in a lot of games, such as Call of Cthulhu, D&amp;D, Pathfinder, Teenagers from Outer Space...<br /> <br /> Anyway, all the vampires are bad, and the Sabbat are (or were as of V5) the most overt in their evil, while the Camarilla are all faceless corporate evil. The Anarchs are terrorists and rabble, but still inhuman killers for all of that.<br /> <br /> But wasn't this thread about the Montreal boardgame?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it was about how Montreal was treated in V5.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's now a Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> Because, AND SHOCK OF SHOCKS, the Montreal developers thought their city being Cammie made more sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378142#post1378142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier you used Bloodlines as an example...their is no personal horror in that game, the protagonist is just a fanged hero, being pulled out of the fire every so often by Nines the superawesome anarch ...yea....</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel there were some good bits for personal horror in the game based on how you wanted to play the morality of your character. Yes, you could play as a Friendly Neighborhood Vampire but you could also play as one who was giving into the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Horror in Bloodlines</b><br /> <br /> * Enslaving Heather and turning her into your sex toy as she loses all of her free will and gives up her life to serve you.<br /> * Killing the innocent (but annoying) ghoul in order to ingratiate yourself with the Anarchs. Nines may be a &quot;good&quot; guy but Skelter was evil.<br /> * Killing the Ghost Hunters crew member in order to protect the Masquerade, potentially feeding him to Pisha.<br /> * Potentially killing the script writer and the Thin Blood Vampire to protect the Masquerade.<br /> * Killing Chunk at the end of the game.<br /> * Potentially killing all manner of people with your Hunger.<br /> <br /> You don't have to be a bad guy but you can certainly roleplay yourself that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-02-2020, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:06:29-07:00","id":1378163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378159#post1378159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, it was about how Montreal was treated in V5.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's now a Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> Because, AND SHOCK OF SHOCKS, the Montreal developers thought their city being Cammie made more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel there were some good bits for personal horror in the game based on how you wanted to play the morality of your character. Yes, you could play as a Friendly Neighborhood Vampire but you could also play as one who was giving into the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Horror in Bloodlines</b><br /> <br /> * Enslaving Heather and turning her into your sex toy as she loses all of her free will and gives up her life to serve you.<br /> * Killing the innocent (but annoying) ghoul in order to ingratiate yourself with the Anarchs. Nines may be a &quot;good&quot; guy but Skelter was evil.<br /> * Killing the Ghost Hunters crew member in order to protect the Masquerade, potentially feeding him to Pisha.<br /> * Potentially killing the script writer and the Thin Blood Vampire to protect the Masquerade.<br /> * Killing Chunk at the end of the game.<br /> * Potentially killing all manner of people with your Hunger.<br /> <br /> You don't have to be a bad guy but you can certainly roleplay yourself that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was being an ahole character, not personal horror (at least imho) the horror comes from alien morality, from strange mindsets and terrible comprises with an invading instinct, those decisions are mostly being a dick,. ( I enjoy Bloodlines in spite of it being about Anarchs, at least I can go Autarkis at the end)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-02-2020, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T21:59:49-07:00","id":1378184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378095#post1378095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh huh. Well, bluntly, the chief purpose of any Storyteller is to make sure everyone should have fun at their games. Also, a good playstyle from players is to make sure you don't ruin the fun of your other gamers. So I think they sound very poor gamers.<br /> <br /> However, bluntly, your choice to state this is a reflection of a like of the fictional preference of sect faction is confusing with reality with gaming. It's also a bad gamer habit from you. At the end of the day, this is just our silly pretend world.<br /> <br /> Anarchs may not be your bag and I prefer EVIL Sabbat but it says nothing about you or me in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your arguments are giving that impression , it comes across as you liking parts of the Sabbat so wanting them torn off and given to the Anarchs, which frankly makes no sense and destroys the parts you claim to like, so stop trying to destroy the Sabbat while claiming to help. I know WW are trying to retgone them with the Gehenna war, and that at least some of the Devs utterly despise them and always have (the revised hatchet job proves that) but seriously, stop helping destroy them. Their is no horror in the Anarchs, at all, Humanity as presented removed all horror from that path, with zero risk of wassail, and human thought patterns, where is the horror? It's completely missing, you are a super powered person with a blood fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-03-2020, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T22:25:19-07:00","id":1378186,"title":"","content":"I agree. He says most Anarchs are on the path of Humanity but says &quot;They are on the Path of Humanity but are by and large a group of murderous marauders and misfits.&quot; Those are basically Sabbat shovelheads one of the lowest members of the Sect possible, not Anarchs. Almost all the Anarchs are idealists trying to take down the Camarilla network just 'cuz with no staple reason beside the sect leaders having a political ideological difference. Sure they may have rough character like you mentioned before, but they doesn't really account for most Anarchs. They aren't what you explained at all, but rather what you put on the Sabbat mostly. Putting Anarchs in their base as a sect without any addons makes it see how dull they are compared to the Sabbat as a story foil against the Camarilla. Their basically quasi-&quot;anarchists&quot; apparently, but not, with a mostly directionless ambiguous goal. I just can't see anything compelling about the Sect and I can't fathom why the V5 writers made them the new centerpiece over the Sabbat. I know their going for the whole &quot;lets do some soft rebooting so newcomers can get into game&quot; shtick, but the extremes they've pulled for the most part is too much. I'm not even an old school guy- I got interested in WW fairly recently (2018) and I grasped the lore very quickly through hours of reading. Maybe their trying to remove the Sabbat because they just can't write the Sect anymore at all. Also again- the Sabbat aren't really evil from the Kindred society of moral lens.<br /> <br /> They don't abide by human instincts or psychology anymore. They accept this vampiric nature while their main rival sect acknowledges their vampire self, while trying to suppress it by clinging to an ever degrading false sense of humanity. Thats what is the real fun drive between the Sabbat and the Camarilla. Dualistic extremes in a centuries long supernatural battle with eachother over the ages while the Methuselah and Antediluvians above those trife scrabbles utilize this in the eternal nocturnal Jyhad against one another. Anarchs don't come close to this. Their motivations for conflict with the Camarilla is basic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-03-2020, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T00:07:08-07:00","id":1378198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378184#post1378184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your arguments are giving that impression , it comes across as you liking parts of the Sabbat so wanting them torn off and given to the Anarchs, which frankly makes no sense and destroys the parts you claim to like, so stop trying to destroy the Sabbat while claiming to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat being broken up and having civil war is a good story in my mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know WW are trying to retgone them with the Gehenna war, and that at least some of the Devs utterly despise them and always have (the revised hatchet job proves that) but seriously, stop helping destroy them. Their is no horror in the Anarchs, at all, Humanity as presented removed all horror from that path, with zero risk of wassail, and human thought patterns, where is the horror? It's completely missing, you are a super powered person with a blood fetish. </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs are very much a horrifying group. They're the horrors of unlimited freedom and absolute lack of accountability. What will you sacrifice to never have to answer to a Prince or have the power to be a King yourself. Anarchs can offer you freedom, camraderie, and the ability to do whatever you want but do you NEED rules to survive? Just how much of a monster are you willing to become not to be a slave?<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs are my favorite part of vampire. Most of my love for the Sabbat is in their Anarch historical connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T02:29:13-07:00","id":1378217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378198#post1378198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) The Sabbat being broken up and having civil war is a good story in my mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2)<br /> The Anarchs are very much a horrifying group. They're the horrors of unlimited freedom and absolute lack of accountability. What will you sacrifice to never have to answer to a Prince or have the power to be a King yourself. Anarchs can offer you freedom, camraderie, and the ability to do whatever you want but do you NEED rules to survive? Just how much of a monster are you willing to become not to be a slave?<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs are my favorite part of vampire. Most of my love for the Sabbat is in their Anarch historical connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) hard disagree, it's a complete waste imo, them on Crusade claiming the rest of the third world, and a general realignment of who owns what where, and maybe unleashing the Sabbat inquisition, plus maybe hovering up the new more thuggish Anarchs and getting them on the way to the paths, so that Humanity can go back to being difficult to maintain.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) sounds like a no downsides power fantasy (which to be clear is fine, and fun sometimes, what it isn't is horrible)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-03-2020, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T02:47:47-07:00","id":1378219,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Taggie;n1378217<br /> <br /> 2) sounds like a no downsides power fantasy (which to be clear is fine, and fun sometimes, what it isn't is horrible)[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> How is it a power fantasy? When you give into the Beast you <i>lose.</i><br /> <br /> That's the game.<br /> <br /> Then again, I think we come at these things VERY differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:52:10-07:00","id":1378242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378219#post1378219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it a power fantasy? When you give into the Beast you <i>lose.</i><br /> <br /> That's the game.<br /> <br /> Then again, I think we come at these things VERY differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With Humanity as it was in V20 and is in V5, 'giving in' is a conscious decision, and really hard work as you have pointed out, repeatedly, you can do pretty much anything and maintain some humanity, so where is the downside? (Also this is in danger of rehashing the what the hells of Touchstones...so going to avoid that one). That is why it sounds like a power fantasy. Path should be central to how you act and why, like the most zealous religious practitioner or political activist, it (used to be) the center of your being, Humanity is a Path, and holding on to it should require constant, conscious effort to uphold it's Sins, with that you temper the beast, with that you actually have to fight it, every night, that is gone now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T07:26:30-07:00","id":1378260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378094#post1378094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bluntly, your interpretation of the story also is nonsensical. The Camarilla and the Sabbat have no horror. When you're a Sabbat, you have no humanity. You're damned, you're evil, and you have no salvation--you revel in the Beast. It's what you've chosen. There's no horror because your story is over. Wassail or becoming a Cthulhu cultist (following a Path) with SAN 0 is your fate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You rightly express discontent with someone who blatantly misinterprets your favorite part of the game and then you blatantly misinterpret someone else's favorite part of the game. How can you do it?)<br /> <br /> You're damned - guess what, all vampires are.<br /> <br /> You're evil - all vampires are. That's if we take the most common, the simpliest definition of 'evil' which comes to mind. There are no good vampires.<br /> <br /> You have no salvation - how many vampires seek it, as set in canon? 0.001% Golconda seekers? Do Anarch occupy themselves as a sect mainly with salvation seeking? Lol.<br /> <br /> Why did you ascribe all these sentences to depicting Sabbat? You can say the same about virtually any vampire in the game whatever sect or faction or cult they belong to.<br /> <br /> You revel in the Beast - if you degrade down below 1 Humanity/Path. Did you know Paths are not what happens to you when you reach 1-0 Humanity? Did you read Chaining the Beast? If not, I can only point to it - it's all written there. <br /> <br /> Who are Chtulhu cultists? If you say following a Path is being a Chthulhu culstist that's, to put it mildly, a comic book level interpretation. There are at least dozen of different Paths which combine elements of religious, spiritual and even scientifical mortal studies with elements of post-human, vampiric condition and further articulate in many ways what your existence means as a Damned creature of the night; why you should NOT succumb to the Beast or serve infernal overlords. Some Paths are being abandoned and have a couple of followers left in the whole world, some arise anew (Path of Orion) or evolve from half-forgotten ones (Path of Night). Some are more regional or clan like Paradox or Blood. The basics of some of the Paths were developed thousands of years before Sabbat or Camarilla were founded and have nothing to do with either sect let alone becoming a cultist. Only one - single one - of them resembles something close, and that's a Path of the Hive, and if Sabbat discovers someone following that Path, let alone said someone belongs to the sect, such a creature is destroyed in the most painful ways as soon as possible. <br /> <br /> All of this is from the books, not from my head. these are actually the parts of the canon I had never issue with and often made a centerpiece of my chronicles; they are so good they need no homebrew at all. That's why I am all the more offended by your misinterpretation. Not sure if Chaining the Beast is still around but I'd highly recommend it.<br /> <br /> Or basically what CajunKhan said. You misunderstand the Sabbat concept completely although I see what elements of the concept had helped your minsunderstanding. But taking those minor elements as central and turning the whole concept on it's head is pure fanon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T07:42:07-07:00","id":1378263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378159#post1378159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, it was about how Montreal was treated in V5.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's now a Camarilla city.<br /> <br /> Because, AND SHOCK OF SHOCKS, the Montreal developers thought their city being Cammie made more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still contested, not entirely Camarilla, not entirely Anarch and certainly no longer 100% Sabbat. One part of me longs for the familiar good old City of Black Miracles, but from the other hand, I always welcome a good shakeup. The emphasis is on good. Because, SHOCK OF SHOCKS, developers decided retconning hundreds of years of Sabbat domination into oblivion does not make much sense.<br /> <br /> The thread was about the state of things in Montreal in V5, developers of the board game joined with the new about it around page 6, iirc. Basically, it could not but lead to exploration of Sabbat themes in V5 because, as someone rightfully stated at the beginning of the thread, Montreal - not Mexico, not NY - was Sabbat dream city. It was a city where they could go and say, 'Yeah. We can do it, after all'. Montreal was the only city holding the answer to the main question every Sabbat asks herself sooner or later - rather sooner - 'Why? Why do I keep going?'. And the answers varied, but they were all valid. Now the 'soul' of the sect is gone/contested, and I, for one, would love the remaining Sabbat to forge their new soul somewhere in the Old World (MENA, Eastern Europe, India) and in Gehenna crusade. The desire of some people in the forums to turn that crusade into satanic locust festival saddens me all the more bc there is quite a possibility someone among the authors would love to do the same in the official book.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:28:11-07:00","id":1378326,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, Sabbat players have a lot of wonderful occult horror and personal horror elements. You're correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378263#post1378263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still contested, not entirely Camarilla, not entirely Anarch and certainly no longer 100% Sabbat. One part of me longs for the familiar good old City of Black Miracles, but from the other hand, I always welcome a good shakeup. The emphasis is on good. Because, SHOCK OF SHOCKS, developers decided retconning hundreds of years of Sabbat domination into oblivion does not make much sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not retconned, the city was taken by the Camarilla after the Second Inquisition defeated the Sabbat there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thread was about the state of things in Montreal in V5, developers of the board game joined with the new about it around page 6, iirc. Basically, it could not but lead to exploration of Sabbat themes in V5 because, as someone rightfully stated at the beginning of the thread, Montreal - not Mexico, not NY - was Sabbat dream city. It was a city where they could go and say, 'Yeah. We can do it, after all'. Montreal was the only city holding the answer to the main question every Sabbat asks herself sooner or later - rather sooner - 'Why? Why do I keep going?'. And the answers varied, but they were all valid. Now the 'soul' of the sect is gone/contested, and I, for one, would love the remaining Sabbat to forge their new soul somewhere in the Old World (MENA, Eastern Europe, India) and in Gehenna crusade. <b>The desire of some people in the forums to turn that crusade into satanic locust festival saddens me all the more bc there is quite a possibility someone among the authors would love to do the same in the official book.</b> </div> </div> </div>While I love our discussions, I kind of find it hilarious you bring this up since Montreal is a Sabbat city explictly corrupted and under the control of a Demon Lord who has warped a good quarter of the city as well as being presented as a place about to fall completely apart due to secretarianism a swell as infighting. It's bizarre because it's the MOST Satanic city, including Mexico, because all Sabbat Embraced there are put in demonically tainted Earth so they commune with the Lord of Disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-03-2020, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:39:02-07:00","id":1378331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378326#post1378326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, Sabbat players have a lot of wonderful occult horror and personal horror elements. You're correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While I love our discussions, I kind of find it hilarious you bring this up since Montreal is a Sabbat city explictly corrupted and under the control of a Demon Lord who has warped a good quarter of the city as well as being presented as a place about to fall completely apart due to secretarianism a swell as infighting. It's bizarre because it's the MOST Satanic city, including Mexico, because all Sabbat Embraced there are put in demonically tainted Earth so they commune with the Lord of Disease.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is bizaar, but as it was one of the few city books we had, and also went really deeply into Paths that actually made a twisted sense, and weren't for the evulz, it is beloved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:31:45-07:00","id":1378356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378326#post1378326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, Sabbat players have a lot of wonderful occult horror and personal horror elements. You're correct.<br /> <br /> It's not retconned, the city was taken by the Camarilla after the Second Inquisition defeated the Sabbat there.<br /> <br /> While I love our discussions, I kind of find it hilarious you bring this up since Montreal is a Sabbat city explictly corrupted and under the control of a Demon Lord who has warped a good quarter of the city as well as being presented as a place about to fall completely apart due to secretarianism a swell as infighting. It's bizarre because it's the MOST Satanic city, including Mexico, because all Sabbat Embraced there are put in demonically tainted Earth so they commune with the Lord of Disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>One huge facepalm. Sorry.<br /> <br /> If you've read more than a WW fandom wiki page e.g. the actual city book, it states explicitly that the reason city has not fell is the spiritual integrity of the most of Sabbat covens there.<br /> There are 2 (two) infernalists out of 26 vampires described in the city book. The main one, the only one who communicates with the demon, became an infernalist when he was a mortal - when his whole family was dying bc of smallpox, he prayed to anyone to save him, and he was heard, unfortunately. Everything he accomplished since then - Embrace, creation rite, amassing power, scheming, etc - is bc of the demon's assistance. The second one is an accidental embrace who gone mad afterwards and now wants to make the whole sect pay; he's only starting his journey on the path of evil revelations though and is used mostly as a yes man by the main baddy.<br /> <br /> That's it. The infernalist tries to use the more militant and headstrong faction covens to topple the power of the more learned ones who are the real threat to the demon BECAUSE they are path practicioners and founders of the Inquisition. The militant ones do not fall for it completely too, as they are high on respective paths and are black hand-trained.<br /> <br /> All the other direct influence of the demon is: 1) whispers and visions which disturb and can even shake the faith of particularly weak willed cainites and you bet there are not many - but those who are CAN pose a serious threat to internal security if you are a ST and are inclined towards this course of action; 2) some fomori in the sewers; 3) a lone black spiral dancer goofing around. There is no Demon Lord controlling the city, there is a powerful Bane imprisoned underneath the city who tries to use all means possible to corrupt the city which holds out for hundreds of years precisely because of highly spiritual cainites making it it's stronghold. Of course they are not 'grim vampire antiheros' - they are more aggressvie and ruthless than your regular camarilla or anarchs but the main idea is that they follow strict sets of rules dictating every ounce of their unlives and they not only follow those but help other Sabbat - both locals and newcomers - to become the same. The core of the city covens is basically Lancea Sanktum in the making, western Devil-Tigers, punishers of sinners, does this lot bow to some disease Bane?<br /> <br /> I hope now you get the book's idea - Sabbat's finest were intentionally confronted with the most scariest thing they strived against. The book emphasises the idea that despite all the violence and war parties, only the spiritual integrity of it's members is the backbone which holds the sect together and does it quite well even in the face of a demon/powerful Bane.<br /> Seriously, do I need to re-tell the whole book to prove you are plain wrong? I am in no intent to discuss fanon and see you are entrenched in your &quot;Sabbat=Satan/Cthulhu no no very bad&quot; position.<br /> Just read more books on the sect, please. maybe it'll change your mind, bc my retelling of them obviously cannot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:53:39-07:00","id":1378401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378331#post1378331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is bizaar, but as it was one of the few city books we had, and also went really deeply into Paths that actually made a twisted sense, and weren't for the evulz, it is beloved</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the conflict between the Sabbat and those corrupted by the infernal. I think the Infernalists help make the Sabbat all the more interesting.<br /> <br /> Is Loyalty to Caine truly different from loyalty to Demons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T20:00:15-07:00","id":1378454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378356#post1378356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One huge facepalm. Sorry.<br /> <br /> If you've read more than a WW fandom wiki page e.g. the actual city book, it states explicitly that the reason city has not fell is the spiritual integrity of the most of Sabbat covens there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of my favorite Sabbat books and I'm pretty sure it never says that. Hence why I pointed out the city is a demon infested hellhole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are 2 (two) infernalists out of 26 vampires described in the city book. </div> </div> </div>Plus one enormous demon lord who eats a sizeable chunk of the Mass Embraces.<br /> <br /> So, 10% of the population.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's it. The infernalist tries to use the more militant and headstrong faction covens to topple the power of the more learned ones who are the real threat to the demon BECAUSE they are path practicioners and founders of the Inquisition. The militant ones do not fall for it completely too, as they are high on respective paths and are black hand-trained. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Sabbat Inquisition are always trying to fight the demonic infestation in their ranks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All the other direct influence of the demon is: 1) whispers and visions which disturb and can even shake the faith of particularly weak willed cainites and you bet there are not many - but those who are CAN pose a serious threat to internal security if you are a ST and are inclined towards this course of action; 2) some fomori in the sewers; 3) a lone black spiral dancer goofing around. There is no Demon Lord controlling the city, there is a powerful Bane imprisoned underneath the city who tries to use all means possible to corrupt the city which holds out for hundreds of years precisely because of highly spiritual cainites making it it's stronghold. </div> </div> </div>Metathiax is under Mount Royale not the city itself, but it does have a Coven of worshipers called the Blood Circle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course they are not 'grim vampire antiheros' - they are more aggressvie and ruthless than your regular camarilla or anarchs but the main idea is that they follow strict sets of rules dictating every ounce of their unlives and they not only follow those but help other Sabbat - both locals and newcomers - to become the same. The core of the city covens is basically Lancea Sanktum in the making, western Devil-Tigers, punishers of sinners, does this lot bow to some disease Bane? </div> </div> </div>It's weird you think I don't like Montreal by Night. The demon infestation is the central conflict of the city, though, and why the PCs have to stop it before the city falls.<br /> <br /> That's my take on it, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T21:40:56-07:00","id":1378469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378401#post1378401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the conflict between the Sabbat and those corrupted by the infernal. I think the Infernalists help make the Sabbat all the more interesting.<br /> <br /> Is Loyalty to Caine truly different from loyalty to Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) So do I, I actually wish the 'infernal' had been better tied into the wider WOD, (as a general thing) so Nephandic Vampire cults and Maljean worship among Underlie Fae etc, but hey ho. <br /> <br /> 2) Yes, Caine does not want to unmake the universe for a start, and does not barter souls, it may be a subtle difference, but Noddism is a faith, a twisted one, a nasty one, but it is based on hope and faith, Infernalism is a surrender, it is the repudiation of freedom in exchange for temporal power, the inversion of hope into absolute nihilism, the rejection of discipline in exchange for servitude.<br /> <br /> The Paths and their ritae says embrace what you are, take your fate in your hands, eternity is yours if you have the will, and self discipline. Infernalism says give in, you are to weak to stave off the beast, to frail to endure, to pathetic to prosper, I will take that all away, for the low price of your will, your soul and your self.<br /> <br /> That is the difference, any faith is based on hope, maybe twisted, maybe flat insane, but hope for a better day to come. Infernalism is based on despair, the idea that you may as well destroy tomorrow for power today..<br /> <br /> In a fundamental way the Sabbats is about hope, faith,and self discipline, Infernalism inverts all of that, into. Despair, Nihilism and Servitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-04-2020, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:11:49-07:00","id":1378531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378454#post1378454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's one of my favorite Sabbat books and I'm pretty sure it never says that. Hence why I pointed out the city is a demon infested hellhole.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says that many times througout the book: the spiritual Cainites are the ones who can harm the demon. he's afraid of them and desperately strives to undermine not just specific vampires but the entire sect. his main weapon are not EVULLZ VAMPIRES but the infighting between the mentally tough ones. Your whole premise about evil sabbat being evil cause they are from montreal which is satans city is plain wrong. Sabbat's vampires are the only ones who prevent metathiax from plunging the city into chaos and ruin. The book provides enough tools to you as a story teller to either help Sabbat destroy the bane or help the bane to destroy Sabbat - and not through spiritual corruption as you try to convince us; but through intrigue only. <br /> <br /> It also exemplifies those cainites who fall to infernal are the weakest. They either were the weakest or gone mad and then corrupted. It is implied in characters part that only strong conciousness, either of human or post-human moral lense, can protect you from going to hell. That's why the old Sabbat are cool and that's why making them mere puppets of their own vice and cruelty is stupid as hell (pun intended).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus one enormous demon lord who eats a sizeable chunk of the Mass Embraces.<br /> <br /> So, 10% of the population. </div> </div> </div>There are no mass embraces. Only Embraces/creation rites done on the slopes on Mount Royal are messed up. read the book.<br /> What do you mean enormous? Did you measure him?<br /> It's a bane, powerful wyrm spirit who the local Garou imprisoned millenia ago under the mountain like in many other places across the world. Not some Fallen angel/Earthbound from DtF.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the Sabbat Inquisition are always trying to fight the demonic infestation in their ranks. </div> </div> </div>Not only them - Inquisitors work to locate and expose them; if infernalists are overt in their hellish powers, their fellow Sabbat will tear them apart without a second thought.<br /> <br /> And Montreal is the birthplace of it. Metathiax realises it is as much as the sabbat are locked with him as it's him being locked with the sabbat in Montreal. &quot;An unstoppable force meets an immovable object&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Metathiax is under Mount Royale not the city itself, but it does have a Coven of worshipers called the Blood Circle. </div> </div> </div>There is no blood circle coven among city cainites. Blood Circle is a location of worship where infernalists - two vampires and likely mortal cultists - perform their rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's weird you think I don't like Montreal by Night. The demon infestation is the central conflict of the city, though, and why the PCs have to stop it before the city falls. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you don't like it, I am pretty sure you misunderstood the main idea - the focus on enlightenment and the fact the sub-name of the book is Litany of Blood; you are focusing instead on the threat to the Sabbat rather then the sect itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's my take on it, though. </div> </div> </div>Which differs greatly from the very idea of the book. So going back to why we started it, why did you find it hilarious when I pointed out the invalidity of attempts to paint Sabbat as a satanists mob going forward?<br /> I presented the city and its book (not my personal take but as it is) as the prime example of the contrary - Montreal is the city of many cainites whose main occupation is hunting down satanists mobs. The Camarilla sieges or Anarch infiltrations are virtually no threat to the city - both the sect and their enemies know it. Even the Setites - probably the only vampire group capable to go toe to toe with Sabbat because they are equally ruthless - they also fell after a short-lived attempt to inflitrate the city in 1960s. (page 30-31 of the book. also page 5 of the Players GttS 1997)<br /> The only threat worthy of such a Sabbat city would be an otherworldly one, and quite a powerful one - even Garou could not destroy the Bane. Which means the capabilities of the Shepherds and Inquisitors of the city are on par or even better suited to harm demonic stuff than those of the very kids of Gaia.<br /> That's not my take on it though. That's the premise of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:50:20-07:00","id":1378542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378401#post1378401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Loyalty to Caine truly different from loyalty to Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's a question you would pose your Sabbat players with in your game, I doubt it's a Sabbat chronicle except a very very homebrewed one. It has nothing to do with the Sabbat so many people enjoyed playing since it was made playable.<br /> <br /> Taggie put it perfecty, but I'd like to add something very important. The infernals serve someone. The Sabbat serve only themselves. 'I am my own master, not God, not Satan, only I chose this fate, and I fully embrace what it means to be a vampire'. Loyalty to Caine is rather metaphorycal - it's a loyalty to a role model, not some specific God-Emperor of Vampirekind. It's a loyalty to predatory self vs loyalty to some otherworldly masters.<br /> <br /> The former obliges you to accept both freedom and the responsibility which comes with it. The latter is voluntarily handing your own fate into the hands of the ultimate oblivion, relieving yourself of the burden of self-reliance and the necessity to think and decide for yourself. You are an automaton in service of something hardly comprehensible even by a post-human mind. No true Sabbat can accept that. There are few exceptions, of course, designed exactly to provide additional contrast and a cautionary tale, but making them a core theme and playable characters is not what playing White Wolf's Sabbat is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-04-2020, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T09:05:36-07:00","id":1378554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378401#post1378401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the conflict between the Sabbat and those corrupted by the infernal. I think the Infernalists help make the Sabbat all the more interesting.<br /> <br /> Is Loyalty to Caine truly different from loyalty to Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know this is a strawman but, forget about Caine and noddists for a second, by your logic there is no difference between:<br /> <br /> - a lasombra on the path of night who worships satan, tries impersonating Satan's ideals, and works to break the celestial shackles and bring chaos to the world<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> - an infernalist on the path of screams (or whatever it's called) who worships satan, who has sold their blood for at least three investments with him, have replaced their beast with a hellbeast remotely controlled by their master, and their soul held hostage<br /> <br /> right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-04-2020, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T14:00:59-07:00","id":1378612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378554#post1378554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know this is a strawman but, forget about Caine and noddists for a second, by your logic there is no difference between:<br /> <br /> - a lasombra on the path of night who worships satan, tries impersonating Satan's ideals, and works to break the celestial shackles and bring chaos to the world<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> - an infernalist on the path of screams (or whatever it's called) who worships satan, who has sold their blood for at least three investments with him, have replaced their beast with a hellbeast remotely controlled by their master, and their soul held hostage<br /> <br /> right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's more the fact I'm a big Demon: The Fallen fan and am perfectly fine with Demons being an alien or honorable evil rather than just &quot;I WANT TO DESTROY THE UNIVERSE&quot; which I find boring. Evil can came in a rainbow of colors, motivations, and ideologies as well as have its own internal logic. Just because someone is irredeemable doesn't mean they're not interesting or complex.<br /> <br /> <u>Sabbat Infernalists</u><br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who believes he needs to kill God so his Devil patron can remake the universe as a paradise where no one ever has to suffer again.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who has sold his soul to a demon because it gives him control over his Beast after he was close to wassail.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships demons because it gives her pack a slight edge in keeping them alive and she thinks of them as her children.<br /> <br /> + A Tremere who carefully manages and records all of his deals with demons as to never lose their soul while noting that the demons usually are LESS violent than his fellow Sabbat.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships Kupala because believes they're a Slavic deity not a demon.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships the Devil because he interprets the Book fo Nod as saying Caine did.<br /> <br /> Back in the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat I always enjoyed a Sabbat Demon who accepted the murder of cats as a sacrifice. The Demon was horrified to find out Sabbat happily murdered people to him instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378542#post1378542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's a question you would pose your Sabbat players with in your game, I doubt it's a Sabbat chronicle except a very very homebrewed one. It has nothing to do with the Sabbat so many people enjoyed playing since it was made playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an argument that an Infernalist Sabbat would pose in-universe. If you can't separate that from the Storyteller's own opinions, you should find another one because they clearly suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-04-2020, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T15:23:44-07:00","id":1378622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378612#post1378612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it's more the fact I'm a big Demon: The Fallen fan and am perfectly fine with Demons being an alien or honorable evil rather than just &amp;quot;I WANT TO DESTROY THE UNIVERSE&amp;quot; which I find boring. Evil can came in a rainbow of colors, motivations, and ideologies as well as have its own internal logic. Just because someone is irredeemable doesn't mean they're not interesting or complex.<br /> <br /> <u>Sabbat Infernalists</u><br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who believes he needs to kill God so his Devil patron can remake the universe as a paradise where no one ever has to suffer again.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who has sold his soul to a demon because it gives him control over his Beast after he was close to wassail.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships demons because it gives her pack a slight edge in keeping them alive and she thinks of them as her children.<br /> <br /> + A Tremere who carefully manages and records all of his deals with demons as to never lose their soul while noting that the demons usually are LESS violent than his fellow Sabbat.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships Kupala because believes they're a Slavic deity not a demon.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships the Devil because he interprets the Book fo Nod as saying Caine did.<br /> <br /> Back in the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat I always enjoyed a Sabbat Demon who accepted the murder of cats as a sacrifice. The Demon was horrified to find out Sabbat happily murdered people to him instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That would be an argument that an Infernalist Sabbat would pose in-universe. If you can't separate that from the Storyteller's own opinions, you should find another one because they clearly suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you did not frame that as an in universe question, I certainly did not take it as such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:17:06-07:00","id":1378654,"title":"","content":"Aren't the Sabbat 100% against Infernalism of any sort? Actually yeah, I'm pretty sure the Sabbat actively hunt all Infernalists in their Sect. Only a minuscule of Sabbat even bother with the risk of Infernalism and most are indoctroned by their superiors from low rank to not practice that at all. Infernalism is met by a Sabbat Inquisition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyway my main gripe about this is basically some boardgame session apparently effected the canon of WoD out of freaking nowhere. Why is that even allowed in the first place? I think thats what everyone has been missing in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-04-2020, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:24:32-07:00","id":1378657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378654#post1378654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Sabbat 100% against Infernalism of any sort? Actually yeah, I'm pretty sure the Sabbat actively hunt all Infernalists in their Sect. Only a minuscule of Sabbat even bother with the risk of Infernalism and most are indoctroned by their superiors from low rank to not practice that at all. Infernalism is met by a Sabbat Inquisition.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: Anyway my main gripe about this is basically some boardgame session apparently effected the canon of WoD out of freaking nowhere. Why is that even allowed in the first place? I think thats what everyone has been missing in this thread</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they've said they want to do a completely integrated and canonical World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> As for why?<br /> <br /> Duh, so people will buy it who wouldn't normally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:29:58-07:00","id":1378658,"title":"","content":"That doesn't make sense at all. Whatever they did was a horrible move and needs to be retconned. A mere boardgame shouldn't change WoD lore. How many of us have down our own tabletop sessions- do the things we do ever change WoD lore? No? Then why should this? Thats not how canon should be maneuvered at all. It should be done booklet by booklet like last time. Even worse they've done this laughable garbage via boardgame, not even proper tabletop. So again, why in the world is this even allowed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T19:53:04-07:00","id":1378660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378658#post1378658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't make sense at all. Whatever they did was a horrible move and needs to be retconned. A mere boardgame shouldn't change WoD lore. How many of us have down our own tabletop sessions- do the things we do ever change WoD lore? No? Then why should this? Thats not how canon should be maneuvered at all. It should be done booklet by booklet like last time. Even worse they've done this laughable garbage via boardgame, not even proper tabletop. So again, why in the world is this even allowed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I support it because it's the same thing Star Wars Expanded Universe used to do. It canonized all the Tabletop RPG material that was incorporated into the novels and the video games. There's nothing abnormal about this. Certainly, the video games are going to reach a bigger audience than the RPG.<br /> <br /> Also, since when have miniature games NOT been the same thing as RPGs? Look at Warhammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T20:11:10-07:00","id":1378665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378658#post1378658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't make sense at all. Whatever they did was a horrible move and needs to be retconned. A mere boardgame shouldn't change WoD lore. How many of us have down our own tabletop sessions- do the things we do ever change WoD lore? No? Then why should this? Thats not how canon should be maneuvered at all. It should be done booklet by booklet like last time. Even worse they've done this laughable garbage via boardgame, not even proper tabletop. So again, why in the world is this even allowed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your tabletop sessions don't change lore because they aren't officially published materials. It's done because that encourages fans of all sorts to buy into the product. Lore people want it to see the impact to the world, board game fans may be tempted by the board game. And given that this is an official product with a story focus there isn't much of a better outlet for it. They did it with new york too. <br /> <br /> World of Darkness has an evolving lore, and given that board games and video games and any other materials they publish are going to tie into that. For example, Bloodlines 2 will define the current state of Seattle. Because unless there was a book that explained it, any material in any city will be defining the canon of that location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T20:54:34-07:00","id":1378671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378654#post1378654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't the Sabbat 100% against Infernalism of any sort? Actually yeah, I'm pretty sure the Sabbat actively hunt all Infernalists in their Sect. Only a minuscule of Sabbat even bother with the risk of Infernalism and most are indoctroned by their superiors from low rank to not practice that at all. Infernalism is met by a Sabbat Inquisition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyway my main gripe about this is basically some boardgame session apparently effected the canon of WoD out of freaking nowhere. Why is that even allowed in the first place? I think thats what everyone has been missing in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The board game is using Montreal lore as it's background, in effect becoming a source, playing the boardgame doesn't change canon, Legend of the Five Rings does something similar (in fact more so, with CCG tournaments deciding major plot conflicts and the meta going forward), it works fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T23:32:24-07:00","id":1378686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378671#post1378671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The board game is using Montreal lore as it's background, in