>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T05:06:49-07:00","id":1378728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378726#post1378726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you hate what I like.<br /> <br /> Is there more to say on that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Beyond that I hope that we both get enough as this edition goes forward to at least find something to enjoy, nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T08:20:36-07:00","id":1378765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378612#post1378612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it's more the fact I'm a big Demon: The Fallen fan and am perfectly fine with Demons being an alien or honorable evil rather than just &quot;I WANT TO DESTROY THE UNIVERSE&quot; which I find boring. Evil can came in a rainbow of colors, motivations, and ideologies as well as have its own internal logic. Just because someone is irredeemable doesn't mean they're not interesting or complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>except the Demon's motivations are unrelated to the conflict with infernalists,<br /> it's explicitly stated that sabbat are ok with demons and that some of them are willing to ally with them,<br /> infernalists, however, are not appreciated even by those who ally with demons, and that's regardless of the infernalist's master's motivations<br /> <br /> again, there's a difference between sharing a demon's motivations and selling out to that same demon,<br /> Infernalists are the latter (or both)<br /> anti-infernalists can be the former, but never the latter<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u>Sabbat Infernalists</u><br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who believes he needs to kill God so his Devil patron can remake the universe as a paradise where no one ever has to suffer again.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who has sold his soul to a demon because it gives him control over his Beast after he was close to wassail.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships demons because it gives her pack a slight edge in keeping them alive and she thinks of them as her children.<br /> <br /> + A Tremere who carefully manages and records all of his deals with demons as to never lose their soul while noting that the demons usually are LESS violent than his fellow Sabbat.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships Kupala because believes they're a Slavic deity not a demon.<br /> <br /> + A Sabbat who worships the Devil because he interprets the Book fo Nod as saying Caine did. </div> </div> </div>all of these are in Revised (except for the last one, cause it's dumb and you should drop it already),<br /> all of these except for the 4th one can be pardoned by the Inquisition provided the Infernalist has the necessary backing and proof of their motivations (although, a pardon only means that the Infernalist now is held by the Inquisition by the balls)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T11:33:30-07:00","id":1560714,"title":"","content":"So, the upcoming CRPG is set in...Montreal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/84DaW0W-F2o\" data-code=\"84DaW0W-F2o\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/84DaW0W-F2o/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T13:06:20-07:00","id":1560988,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, is this thread mostly a discussion of Fifth Edition or are there any posts talking about what Montreal might look like in Modern Nights?<br /> <br /> I took a look at the first page or two and became a little afraid to read further without confirming whether or not there was some worldbuilding in this thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T13:40:38-07:00","id":1560992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1560988#post1560988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, is this thread mostly a discussion of Fifth Edition or are there any posts talking about what Montreal might look like in Modern Nights?<br /> <br /> I took a look at the first page or two and became a little afraid to read further without confirming whether or not there was some worldbuilding in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some posts talking about the V5 boardgame that is set in Montreal. Then a load of arguing about what the Sabbat is or isn't, why the Anarchs should get all the Sabbat's cool stuff, and completely missing the point of <i>Montreal by Night</i>.<br /> <br /> Look for the stuff by the folks at Flyos Games and you'll get the important bits. Ignore most of the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:01:22-07:00","id":1560996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1378704#post1378704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bloodlines 2 is basically going to define the gameline for the next decade. I'm calling it right here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeaaaah... only 52% positive review scores in the last 30 days for Steam (since its release from 21 October 2025 by the time of this post, 25 June 2026), a mere 62 metascore average by critics as reported by Metacritic (in an era where Game Critics and Journalists are highly generous toward most &quot;AAA&quot; titles), and a 4.8 user rating as reported by Metacritic as well...<br /> <br /> Yeah.. I'm sure Bloodlines 2 will hold a definite definition for the gameline for years to come...<br /> <br /> Oh, and apparently there are rumors that V5 is being scrubbed for a 6th (but I highly doubt Parawolf has learned any of its lessons from V5. My expectations are already extraordinarily low).<br /> <br /> I still cannot believe a board game decided an important part of Masquerade lore... but given who the director of V5 was and what he revealed was the main design decisions going into it (not just the board game alone, but V5 as a whole) on his YouTube channel... it all makes sense now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:13:13-07:00","id":1560998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1560992#post1560992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are some posts talking about the V5 boardgame that is set in Montreal. Then a load of arguing about what the Sabbat is or isn't, why the Anarchs should get all the Sabbat's cool stuff, and completely missing the point of <i>Montreal by Night</i>.<br /> <br /> Look for the stuff by the folks at Flyos Games and you'll get the important bits. Ignore most of the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank You most kindly for the head\u2019s-up.\ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:35:05-07:00","id":1561002,"title":"","content":"I was trying to brush up on the original MONTREAL BY NIGHT sourcebook and stumbled onto the rather delightful fact that newly-minted Sabbat Archbishop Kyle Strathcona apparently sent a letter breathing fire and pure defiance to Mithras, Prince of London (His former master) \u2026 in AD 1838.<br /> <br /> By which point, according to later canon (from VICTORIAN AGE: VAMPIRE, I think?) Mithras hadn\u2019t actually been seen in London for over forty years (and wouldn\u2019t be seen again in London for another forty-odd years.<br /> <br /> One has to wonder (A) What the Regent Valerius made of this communication and (B) if Kyle Strathcona would ever, ever admit to this of he ever found out his mistake.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:39:41-07:00","id":1561003,"title":"","content":"Wait, Kyle Strathcona\u2019s Sire was named \u2018Collinsworth\u2019?<br /> <br /> That poor vampire is DOOMED if any moderns find out the fact: he will never, ever be able to avoid the inevitable Vampire Nerd jokes ever again.<br /> <br /> Or he\u2019ll have to murder the jester and everyone who hears and/or repeats the joke, but that\u2019s almost as expense of his time and patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T15:53:33-07:00","id":1561007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1560996#post1560996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeaaaah... only 52% positive review scores in the last 30 days for Steam (since its release from 21 October 2025 by the time of this post, 25 June 2026), a mere 62 metascore average by critics as reported by Metacritic (in an era where Game Critics and Journalists are highly generous toward most &quot;AAA&quot; titles), and a 4.8 user rating as reported by Metacritic as well...<br /> <br /> Yeah.. I'm sure Bloodlines 2 will hold a definite definition for the gameline for years to come...</div> </div> </div> </div>Phipps meant it in the sense that it bury the game with it for the time being if a flop.<br /> <br /> Also, it isn't an AAA, Paradox doesn't have this level of buck yet. They may be filthy rich by TTRPG standards, but they're just minor players in their industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T14:39:55-07:00","id":1561091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561002#post1561002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to brush up on the original MONTREAL BY NIGHT sourcebook and stumbled onto the rather delightful fact that newly-minted Sabbat Archbishop Kyle Strathcona apparently sent a letter breathing fire and pure defiance to Mithras, Prince of London (His former master) \u2026 in AD 1838.<br /> <br /> By which point, according to later canon (from VICTORIAN AGE: VAMPIRE, I think?) Mithras hadn\u2019t actually been seen in London for over forty years (and wouldn\u2019t be seen again in London for another forty-odd years.<br /> <br /> One has to wonder (A) What the Regent Valerius made of this communication and (B) if Kyle Strathcona would ever, ever admit to this of he ever found out his mistake.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just because he wrote it to Mithras, who was Prince-Regent of London <i>in absentia</i>, doesn't mean he wrote to him <i>in</i> London. More likely, he knew where Mithras was at the time and wrote to him there. Montreal by Night also has Mithras involved in the early years of Strathcona's regime (before he defected to the Sabbat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typos 06-30-2026, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T13:51:52-07:00","id":1561106,"title":"","content":"A fair and well-reasoned point that I\u2019m still tempted to overlook because it denies the opportunity imagine a vampire operating on one of those little misconceptions with which history abounds (and which is, in this case, highly amusing). (-;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T14:11:14-07:00","id":1561110,"title":"","content":"Yes, I feel Bloodlines 2 has buried V:TM with Paradox.<br /> <br /> And sadly if not for the Visual Novels, LA by Night, Paradox, and board game, I feel like we wouldn't have ANY continuity with Old World of Darknness.<br /> <br /> Paradox wanted a full reboot and were annoyed so many people...didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T14:16:05-07:00","id":1561112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561106#post1561106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fair and well-reasoned point that I\u2019m still tempted to overlook because it denies the opportunity imagine a vampire operating on one of those little misconceptions with which history abounds (and which is, in this case, highly amusing). (-;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't be anything weird or shameful. That's how communication worked before cellphones<br /> <br /> Mithras probably left instructions about what to do with correspondence, which would be an obvious and common detail when preparing to travel. If not, the letter would sit there until his return along with probably many others.<br /> <br /> The sender would also be used to the problem. No one sent letters expecting the receiver to be waiting for it, so instructions on what to do if they weren't home were also common.<br /> <br /> A letter is not a WhatsApp message, missing it is not like sending to another number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T14:20:52-07:00","id":1561113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561110#post1561110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I feel Bloodlines 2 has buried V:TM with Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>The next licensed WoD release by Hasbro/WotC will be way more relevant to the TTRPG game than Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> Also, new games keep trickling in, and the new Sabbat one is promising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T02:05:53-07:00","id":1561119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561110#post1561110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I feel Bloodlines 2 has buried V:TM with Paradox.<br /> <br /> And sadly if not for the Visual Novels, LA by Night, Paradox, and board game, I feel like we wouldn't have ANY continuity with Old World of Darknness.<br /> <br /> Paradox wanted a full reboot and were annoyed so many people...didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be why V6 is taking an explicitly more V20 approach to metaplot. Jess Lanzillo likely knows how to reach a broad range of people and will likely bring some much-needed pragmatism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T02:57:12-07:00","id":1561222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561112#post1561112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't be anything weird or shameful. That's how communication worked before cellphones<br /> <br /> Mithras probably left instructions about what to do with correspondence, which would be an obvious and common detail when preparing to travel. If not, the letter would sit there until his return along with probably many others.<br /> <br /> The sender would also be used to the problem. No one sent letters expecting the receiver to be waiting for it, so instructions on what to do if they weren't home were also common.<br /> <br /> A letter is not a WhatsApp message, missing it is not like sending to another number.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not so much the fact that Mithras wasn\u2019t there to receive the letter that\u2019s so funny - as you mention, this was a risk run by those posting messages back in the old days - it\u2019s the fact that Mithras disappeared as far back as the 1790s and Kyle Strathcona is sending this letter in the late 1830s.<br /> <br /> It gives the strong impression that Strathcona is trying to impress the Base without actually running the risk they think he\u2019s running (Which given the character\u2019s demonstrated tendencies toward weaselling deceitfulness* is entirely plausible).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Not going to lie, my strong impression is that the Edinburgh he stabbed in back were mostly his own childer (He having been Ventrue in residence/chief hostage for a goodly while).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T16:21:00-07:00","id":1561260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561113#post1561113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The next licensed WoD release by Hasbro/WotC will be way more relevant to the TTRPG game than Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> Also, new games keep trickling in, and the new Sabbat one is promising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we'll see. I hope you are right but I'm not fond of Hasbro's AI driven takes on RPGs either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T20:03:44-07:00","id":1561265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561260#post1561260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we'll see. I hope you are right but I'm not fond of Hasbro's AI driven takes on RPGs either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the labor issues and how Hasbro is almost pure evil, for VtM the quality of the result matters less than people reading and discussing it.<br /> <br /> If it sparks interest, we have new players. If it gets attention/views (in their new system), it shows profit is feasible. If people discuss it, then people make better adaptations, no big deal. In the end this is a humble adaptation with no big goals, not the future of the game.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it can open Paradox's eyes to the benefits of partnership and finally break the bubble into big media attention they dreamed from start. Curiously through the one media they didn't thought would do it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T11:27:06-07:00","id":1561391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561260#post1561260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well we'll see. I hope you are right but I'm not fond of Hasbro's AI driven takes on RPGs either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so out of the loop. What happened with Hasbro and AI?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T22:12:49-07:00","id":1561411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561391#post1561391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm so out of the loop. What happened with Hasbro and AI?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, using AI for art and writing, partly to reduce costs directly, but primarily to mine the workers and reduce their pay and benefits.<br /> <br /> Hasbro is going full Pentex on labor rights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T12:14:20-07:00","id":1561424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561411#post1561411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> AFAIK, using AI for art and writing, partly to reduce costs directly, but primarily to mine the workers and reduce their pay and benefits.<br /> <br /> Hasbro is going full Pentex on labor rights.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a mess!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T03:59:31-07:00","id":1561510,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Montreal, I would be interested in theorycrafting what it looks like today, but from a late-V20/BJD perspective. I think there's a lot of room to play around with stuff without just dropping a whammy on everyone and putting in exactly the same political system as in Chicago and everywhere else.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely tone down some of the gratuitous stuff from 2e, and lessen the impact of the infernal to be a background threat but not the overriding antagonist. But it's still possibly my favourite by Night book of all time. Nights of Prophecy provided a welcome update (making Mercy the primary antagonist instead of Metathiax), so we'd first need to figure out how much of that update has happened for V20 purposes.<br /> <br /> Per BJD, Benezri seems to be the archbishop, with Valez standing down due to a deal. This matches Nights of Prophecy. In earlier V20 books, Valez was still in charge per the metaplot-agnostic approach. Similarly, Mercy is apparently still there. Is she more or less fanatical than before? Is Kervos (Salubri antitribu Knight Inquisitor)? Are any of the other new characters there (Gharston Roland of the Ravnos antitribu, Agaitas the Harbinger, poor Rhania of the D'Habi)?<br /> <br /> What of old characters like Yasmin the Black? Last tome we saw her, she's written &quot;...and those who eat heart\u2019s blood will flourish&quot;. Is she dead now? Or did she commit diablerie to stave off the call to Mexico City, as her warning might suggest? Or maybe she's a crusader against diablerie now? Is Pierre Bellmare still missing in this version? Is Cairo captured?<br /> What of Strathcona's gambit to lure the Camarilla in? Will someone find out and end up replacing Strathcona as cardinal? I could see Ezekiel getting the job if the Camarilla is on their doorstep. He'd have to stand down from the Black Hand permanently, but his former martial expertise would help him lead the fight against the Ivory Tower. If the Camarilla is held back, Benezri would probably be the Status Quo's choice.<br /> <br /> How fares Dastur Anosh's war on the Tal'mahe'Ra? That would certainly keep 25:17 busy. I liked The Rose being one of Dastur Anosh's agents. It was a nice twist (since you'd expect him to pick one of the Black Hand members).<br /> <br /> What does everyone think? What would you like to see in a V20 Montreal by Night?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T07:45:33-07:00","id":1561515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561510#post1561510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does everyone think? What would you like to see in a V20 Montreal by Night?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have only surface reading of the by Nights, so take from that what you may, but:<br /> <br /> 1. We need new events, not only resolutions for old ones, so things may have changed however you want;<br /> <br /> 2. Also plot hooks. Each situation must be open for PCs to interact and change outcomes;<br /> <br /> 3. More specifically, there's legitimacy in player outcry from the area to have a Camarilla court there. I think V5 lore is bullshit, but a divided Montreal, either at war, siege or truce, is a good outcome;<br /> <br /> 4. Resolving Dastur Anosh requires deciding what to do with the Tal'Mare'Ha. Not necessarily it's whole canon, but the intersection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T10:38:49-07:00","id":1561526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561515#post1561515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only surface reading of the by Nights, so take from that what you may, but:<br /> <br /> 1. We need new events, not only resolutions for old ones, so things may have changed however you want;<br /> <br /> 2. Also plot hooks. Each situation must be open for PCs to interact and change outcomes;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on both counts. That's why I liked the chapters in NoP and BJD\u2014they definitely open things up for players to get involved. Mind you, Montreal by Night is a morass of plot hooks anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. More specifically, there's legitimacy in player outcry from the area to have a Camarilla court there. </div> </div> </div>I never really bought this argument. You could say the same about any city from the other perspective. Why isn't Chicago Sabbat? What about Sabbat players from there? Ergo, we must overthrow the Camarilla to give them something to play, too.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, someone is always going to be playing against the metaplot. The only place where it really matters is in large LARPs, where I'd just go for a more Requiem-style setup anyway, so anyone can play any sect and still mingle with each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think V5 lore is bullshit, but a divided Montreal, either at war, siege or truce, is a good outcome; </div> </div> </div>This, I am actually fine with. Again, it could apply to any city, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Resolving Dastur Anosh requires deciding what to do with the Tal'Mare'Ha. Not necessarily it's whole canon, but the intersection. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think a war between the TMR and Black Hand on the one hand, and a barely fought-off Camarilla on the other, shakes things up nicely. The Camarilla might have some domain, but I wouldn't give them much.<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to leave the cardinalcy still in the air, to give the players a chance to push it in either direction, while making it clear that Strathcona is definitely on the outs. Even if the Sabbat doesn't learn that he was feeding info to the Camarilla for decades, he was the one who failed to quash their arrival immediately.<br /> <br /> I'd probably have Ezekiel made dominion of the Black Hand's new war effort in the city. 25:17 would swell in numbers as they call on allies from the surrounding regions. They might even be temporarily merged with other packs to form their new kamut. This would give him the power to topple Archbishop Benezri once the war's over, but his ongoing fight against the Tal'mahe'Ra infiltrators on one side and the Camarilla on the other doesn't allow it. Ezekiel is hoping that after the war is over, he will either have proved himself, and get offered the role of cardinal, or can challenge Strathcona to Monomacy and simply take it for himself. Then it doesn't matter if Benezri holds onto the archbishopric.<br /> <br /> Ezekiel also has Blood Rot as of BJD. If so, he'd likely infect most of his kamut. But BJD also suggests the Sabbat might allow the Camarilla to temporarily claim the city so they could also get infected, before returning to rout them, so they take the disease back to Camarilla domains. The only problem is that Ezekiel needs the cure mentioned in BJD, and pronto. So he'd have to send agents into Vancouver to obtain it.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether Dastur Anosh would reveal himself to 25:17, or simply feed them info as needed. I think the latter feels more in-keeping with the lore. Dastur Anosh would be gathering his spies (including The Rose, as mentioned) even as the Tal'mahe'Ra gathers theirs. There are probably a bunch of new packs lurking in the wilderness around the city, left behind when they defeated the Camarilla's first wave. He can hide among those.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Sabbat Inquisition is, in a surprising turn, allying itself with the Hand in destroying the infiltrators (who are all Antediluvian worshippers, after all). But they fully intend to turn on the Hand at the end of it\u2014it's their fault that the sect was so thoroughly infiltrated with heretics in the first place. Every TMR agent slain is another nail in the Black Hand's coffin.<br /> <br /> There's also the Scholars: a pack that's looking to uncover as many thaumaturgical secrets they can from the abandoned chantries and havens of destroyed Tremere antitribu. They're apparently uncovering all kinds of blasphemies through their own experiments (per Chaining the Beast), so being right on the doorstep of the Inquisition puts them at risk. With the Tremere antitribu no longer destroyed in V20, I might have some Telyavs turning up to claim their clanmates' stuff and put the cat among the pigeons.<br /> <br /> There was also a rivalry brewing between the Old World Catharists and the ones in Montreal, which may lead to accusations of heresy against The Widows. Plus, the Librarians are nearly decimated. They would need to recruit more Cainites to survive. The leader of the Scholars, Father Juan Carlos, is disgusted with his pack's activities, so he might seek to join the Librarians. Other Noddist packs were apparently lining up to claim their status, according to Chaining the Beast, so maybe they have some new rivals.<br /> <br /> The packs on the outskirts of Montreal would likely be happy when they're fighting off a new incursion or mounting a counter-strike, but the longer they go without any target to fight, the more anxious they get. One of them would likely be the Disciples of the Black Brood, since Christafarious Black is Ezekiel's childe, but the rest could be any pack the ST wishes\u2014including the players'. This set up even allows Camarilla spies to infiltrate the city by pretending to be a nomadic pack that hung around on the borderlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typo 07-09-2026, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T23:55:01-07:00","id":1561556,"title":"","content":"I agree that both the sect problem and conflict &quot;solution&quot; apply to any city and both sides. In fact, I think a &quot;modern truce&quot; between the sects out of necessity would be the ideal situation, rather than this Warcraft scenario with the Camarilla Alliance and Sabat Horde eternally at full, &quot;kill on site&quot; war.<br /> <br /> As you said, something more Requiem style.<br /> <br /> Not because the plot isn't good, but because the one-note war is bad for setting building and play. It limits options for both ST and players with little payoff unless you want this specific plot.<br /> <br /> My ideal city has both presences to some degree and a <i>de facto</i> truce in some form, with a border region that's either mixed or empty, but work as a buffer.<br /> <br /> From there characters do their shenanigans, so you can have people on both sides trying to get the situation hotter or colder for their own reasons.<br /> <br /> Only LARP I played on was kind like that and I had a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T07:24:11-07:00","id":1561568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561556#post1561556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that both the sect problem and conflict &quot;solution&quot; apply to any city and both sides. In fact, I think a &quot;modern truce&quot; between the sects out of necessity would be the ideal situation, rather than this Warcraft scenario with the Camarilla Alliance and Sabat Horde eternally at full, &quot;kill on site&quot; war.<br /> <br /> As you said, something more Requiem style.<br /> <br /> Not because the plot isn't good, but because the one-note war is bad for setting building and play. It limits options for both ST and players with little payoff unless you want this specific plot.<br /> <br /> My ideal city has both presences to some degree and a <i>de facto</i> truce in some form, with a border region that's either mixed or empty, but work as a buffer.<br /> <br /> From there characters do their shenanigans, so you can have people on both sides trying to get the situation hotter or colder for their own reasons.<br /> <br /> Only LARP I played on was kind like that and I had a lot of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ages ago, I had the idea that if Lucita became Regent, she would facilitate just that. Called the Madrid Principle, it would allow Camarilla Kindred to coexist in Sabbat cities and maintain their own rules and Masquerade, so long as they didn't bother the Sabbat. The Sabbat were likewise told to leave the Camarilla alone.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat would maintain its own Silence of the Blood, with a Bishop of Silence for most major cities. The Bishop of Silence and probably the Sheriff would collaborate on keeping the peace across the city. The Rule of Silence would trump other concerns\u2014the Camarilla can't complain about how the Sabbat keeps things under wraps, so long as it does. Elysium and the Sabbat temple/communal haven would both be treated as sacrosanct with no entry without permission from the relevant side.<br /> <br /> Coteries can petition the Archbishop for formal recognition of domain in Sabbat territories, on the same basis as founded packs, on the understanding that a Sabbat pack gets an equivalent parcel of turf in a Camarilla domain. Usually, though, the Camarilla would just have its own enclave in a Sabbat city (and vice versa). I didn't really think about split cities, Berlin-wise, but I think that could work.<br /> <br /> I can see both sides embracing an uneasy truce worldwide. Especially given the rise of surveillance culture, making it easier for mortals to hunt them (but I'd put this down to the Technocracy more than the Second Inquisition). There might be sporadic acts of terrorism and maybe even guerilla warfare in remote areas when things boil over, but most of the time, each side would want to just get on with nightly existence. I suspect more vampires would turn independent in such a situation, since they no longer need to use one of the sects for protection or vengeance against the other.<br /> <br /> Per BJD, Lucita is supposed to be mostly Status Quo with a few concessions to the Loyalists, via Vasantasena, and greater support for the Sabbat Inquisition, via her &quot;sister&quot; Maria Sandoza. She favours preventing Gehenna at any cost rather than a protracted Gehenna Crusade (as in V5). I figured the reason for this is that she would realise that slaying the Antediluvians would result in another Week of Nightmares happening\u2014up to a dozen times, in fact, depending on how many Ancients are actually dead already\u2014and she would therefore seek other ways to stem the tide.<br /> <br /> In practice, this would be business as usual, since the sect hasn't attempted to slay any Antediluvians in 600 years, but the growing Crusader faction wouldn't be happy. To prevent a civil war, you'd need to either aim them at something or lop off their head (Polonia in this case). My vote's on the latter. There'd be no peace otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T21:28:23-07:00","id":1561583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561568#post1561568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ages ago, I had the idea that if Lucita became Regent, she would facilitate just that. Called the Madrid Principle, it would allow Camarilla Kindred to coexist in Sabbat cities and maintain their own rules and Masquerade, so long as they didn't bother the Sabbat. The Sabbat were likewise told to leave the Camarilla alone.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat would maintain its own Silence of the Blood, with a Bishop of Silence for most major cities. The Bishop of Silence and probably the Sheriff would collaborate on keeping the peace across the city. The Rule of Silence would trump other concerns\u2014the Camarilla can't complain about how the Sabbat keeps things under wraps, so long as it does. Elysium and the Sabbat temple/communal haven would both be treated as sacrosanct with no entry without permission from the relevant side.<br /> <br /> Coteries can petition the Archbishop for formal recognition of domain in Sabbat territories, on the same basis as founded packs, on the understanding that a Sabbat pack gets an equivalent parcel of turf in a Camarilla domain. Usually, though, the Camarilla would just have its own enclave in a Sabbat city (and vice versa). I didn't really think about split cities, Berlin-wise, but I think that could work.<br /> <br /> I can see both sides embracing an uneasy truce worldwide. Especially given the rise of surveillance culture, making it easier for mortals to hunt them (but I'd put this down to the Technocracy more than the Second Inquisition). There might be sporadic acts of terrorism and maybe even guerilla warfare in remote areas when things boil over, but most of the time, each side would want to just get on with nightly existence. I suspect more vampires would turn independent in such a situation, since they no longer need to use one of the sects for protection or vengeance against the other.<br /> <br /> Per BJD, Lucita is supposed to be mostly Status Quo with a few concessions to the Loyalists, via Vasantasena, and greater support for the Sabbat Inquisition, via her &quot;sister&quot; Maria Sandoza. She favours preventing Gehenna at any cost rather than a protracted Gehenna Crusade (as in V5). I figured the reason for this is that she would realise that slaying the Antediluvians would result in another Week of Nightmares happening\u2014up to a dozen times, in fact, depending on how many Ancients are actually dead already\u2014and she would therefore seek other ways to stem the tide.<br /> <br /> In practice, this would be business as usual, since the sect hasn't attempted to slay any Antediluvians in 600 years, but the growing Crusader faction wouldn't be happy. To prevent a civil war, you'd need to either aim them at something or lop off their head (Polonia in this case). My vote's on the latter. There'd be no peace otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of something similar, but with some differences based on my reading of the sects, because I really like the idea they're not just clubs with memberships, or formal institutions, but rather strong philosophies arranged around loose alliances and a claim over all vampires (and yes, that includes Kuei-Jin, some Fomors, Ananasi, anything, though those are unknown).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla isn't a group that enforces the Traditions. It is the <i>idea</i> of the Traditions. The city is Camarilla if it enforces the Traditions in some formal way, has Elysia and a top-down government.<br /> <br /> But I really like how for a time in Bloodlines LaCroix pretends to have absolute power while he actually knows how far he can push, and the Barons know they have power, but he's danger enough that they have to give some credit. Part theater, part reality, part the Little Prince's King.<br /> <br /> So in a Camarilla city, the Prince or Primogen (I don't use both in a city) claims domain over all vampires and establishes the Traditions as the ultimate law, but lives with the practical limits of power, probably bargaining with other power brokers.<br /> <br /> A Sabat city is one with a temple to the Church of the Sword of Caine and a Bishop. The same teachings of always are told, including rallying against the Traditions. Not against intelligence, though. If you're caught by the Sheriff being an idiot that's not anyone else's problem.<br /> <br /> Followers of the Church are pretty much the Sabbat we know, but &quot;tamed&quot; to live in society (tamed as in capable of doing so, neither just punk Cam, nor juvenile, unsustainable idiotic violence. Be a monster, but a smart monster. So tamed in comparison to some depictions). They don't like the Traditions, but neither is the Church requiring they tear them down openly, nor the Prince cares about crimes as long as they don't bring problems.<br /> <br /> It's a church and a state. The difference to the Invictus/L&amp;S relationship is that they're at odds openly, even if not at war. The Bishop has a lot of political power, but won't ever claim secular command. The Prince enacts and enforces law but never claimed authority over spirituality.<br /> <br /> As for the other Kindred, they're whatever they want. The Prince requires obedience to law or hierarchy (curiously not both), the Bishop want you to believe and participate in mass and the ritae. Both keep tabs of likely loyalties, but as long as you're ok with one and not a problem to the other, you're perfectly safe. They don't want you to stay so neutral, do they?<br /> <br /> While this arrangement could be a new version of the setting, I do imagine this being the result of the last 20 years. They have areas of greater influence in the city, and sone very well defined domains, but the limits are fuzzy and unofficial, both draw territorial claim ignoring the other.<br /> <br /> Lucita I agree, would try to prevent Gehenna in its entirety as a pragmatic compromise. It may be the whole reason she's there. It's apparently working, but through continuous effort. Becket thinks it'll be a complete success since the end of time, since there will be no Gehenna anyway, but whatever floats your boat.<br /> <br /> Polonia may die to ease things, but the best thing from a global strategy standpoint to do with the Crusaders is to let them find targets. The Antes are such a vague goal that the most eager Crusaders are manipulated around to do war on whatever, while the smarter ones grow more frustrated with their own lack of clues than with the Church. Lucita won't ever have to deny them their quarry if they never find it.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'd shake up some other factions the game always implied they could have diverse membership, but just ignored:<br /> <br /> Giovanni - even before the Hecata, the Family is a family. Their mortal blood has always been of utmost importance to the Giovanni. But then, what happens when a Giovanni embraces out of family without consent? And when a family member is Embraced by another clan? I say the only answer is family. An outsider they don't accept will be forfeited the right to exist, flee or die, a Giovanni in Curse only. A family member will be rescued, and if they're still loyal to the family as they usually are, that's that, though it is unlikely that they'll get the right to Embrace.<br /> <br /> Ministry - the Followers of Set have been for so long dedicated to corrupt minds and hearts to the teachings of Set. They seem to be the most disastrously incompetent missionaries in the history of religion, since they never appear with an actual convert. They're one of the greatest rivals to the Sabbat, and have many Vampires of every clan among them. Those of Setite line also appear here and there fleeing after falling out with the religion, and while some are spies, some are not.<br /> <br /> Tremere - while rare, sorcerers of other clans are accepted if they show enough promise as students and loyal followers, while students of the blood that don't make the cut, are cut. The odd Sorcerer who truly escape is under Blood Hunt from their POV, and while Giovanni and Setites may have some leniency with those who accept their dregs, the Tremere are willing to declare war on a whole Domain for the crime of housing a liability.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim complete the set. Their influence is more felt through their weight in the Ashirra, but individuals that show interest and really do believe in their cause are sometimes accepted as Residents of Alamut. Which is just a title as only the Web of Crazy Fuckers reside there now and all. The Sorcerers run a deep screen on the individual, then the Viziers and they're assigned a caste in the end. Those of the Blood who are not found sufficiently devoted after Embrace are also screened. If they're found at least just as good as other acceptable Vampires, they're graciously let go, though never with secrets of the clan in their minds.<br /> <br /> Case by case, similar situations should repeat all around: not everyone in a Gangrel gathering is a Gangrel by blood, not every Warren resident look like Max Schreck in expressionist makeup, and so on. Those aren't common, but they highlight the distinction between bloodline and culture, how far clans will go to hide their secrets by contrasting defectors, and how far they'll go to get their hands in such secrets by accepting those defectors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T02:03:06-07:00","id":1561595,"title":"","content":"How do you imagine the development of this model to arise? Did it require a treaty originally, or did it evolve naturally? I can totally see the state/church duality of the Camarilla/Sabbat, though it would take some shrewd politics to get there. The impending threat of hunters obviously helps.<br /> <br /> If the Crusaders went off to fight a war, the remaining factions would be more exposed to Camarilla takeover, so I can see scholarly packs like the Shepherds of Caine being clever enough to strike an accord over fighting to the death or getting involved in sieges. Most of those Cainites are more interested in their spiritual explorations than fighting the Antediluvians anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T08:43:53-07:00","id":1561605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1331574-v5-montreal?p=1561595#post1561595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you imagine the development of this model to arise? Did it require a treaty originally, or did it evolve naturally? I can totally see the state/church duality of the Camarilla/Sabbat, though it would take some shrewd politics to get there. The impending threat of hunters obviously helps.<br /> <br /> If the Crusaders went off to fight a war, the remaining factions would be more exposed to Camarilla takeover, so I can see scholarly packs like the Shepherds of Caine being clever enough to strike an accord over fighting to the death or getting involved in sieges. Most of those Cainites are more interested in their spiritual explorations than fighting the Antediluvians anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it developing naturally. Gradually but fast in the sense of being &quot;just&quot; 20 years.<br /> <br /> A lot of cross-sect contacts already exist in the lore. That would increase during the years after the last news of Revised. The Crusaders have a lot in their hands with the Red Star and all that stuff. They can't waste time and resources with the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Lucita is not a Cam hater. She welcomes any opportunity to focus on actual problems. She's smart enough to find the &quot;traitorous contacts&quot; and to shrug it off and see what they bring of useful. At the highest levels both sects find a common cause in pragmatic survival.<br /> <br /> No higher institution reinforces the Cam war policy anymore. Packs are indeed independent, and without this direction they lose interest at first and explore contact after. Princes are still not happy with the idea of close contact with anti-elder extremists, but under pressure of the same problems, mystical and mundane, they find something they like: Sabbat mercenaries.<br /> <br /> Eventually things calm down in the Signs of The End front. Not completely, though, and the Crusaders still have a hot track to follow. But enough. Hunters are getting more dangerous. If the developments of the early 2000s greatly increase the power of institutional hunters, at least some, the technologies of the 2010s start to give any hunter more access to information.<br /> <br /> Semiofficial accords start to happen. It isn't a big event, but several small arrangements here and there. First between minor packs and low hierarchy Guardians of Elysium, but sooner or later the higher ups see that they can't resist the tide. Most don't have any big reason to want to.<br /> <br /> The sects are also &quot;stabilizing&quot; in institutional nature with the leadership more focused on the big threats than night-to-night micromanaging. Princes and Bishops just want to take care of their interests, their personal turf and political style. As individuals their power grows, while the sects are more and more ideas rather than global hierarchies. The higher ups don't care of the important resources keep coming, and they do,more actually.<br /> <br /> When the big truces are openly signed between parties all over the world, the leaderships don't pretend to be responsible for this anymore. Its not a big global truce, but hundreds of regional or big cities truces. They're not equal, and here and there some open conflicts remain, but they are indeed more local grudges than anything.<br /> <br /> This is not a more tranquil world, just a less top-down sect structure. Leadership is strong, enough to not <i>care</i>. Don't cause problems, keep important resources flowing, and when they do come and ask something, you obey. As far as you can say, they're powerful enough to stop a primordial prophecy in its tracks and hold.<br /> <br /> Elders focus less on distractions forced upon them and more on their actual ambitions and rivalries. On many places, Princes and Bishops find out that bickering through influence rather than destruction makes for more wealth, of all kinds, reaching them.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are more fucked than ever. No more Anarch Free States, not because they fell, but because they had to organize for real to resist. They're proper attempts at administration, but not Cam enemies. To be an Anarch is again to be the rebel in your city trying to change what you think is wrong, now against both legal and spiritual oppression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T22:44:52-07:00","id":1561957,"title":"","content":"Random Lucita aside: I wish we could find out the true fate of Lucita. If it doesn't happen this edition, it'll probably never happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T23:00:48-07:00","id":1561958,"title":"","content":"That would be nice CTPhipps, but I wouldn't be shocked if they don't address that subplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T11:02:03-07:00","id":1561973,"title":"","content":"I have no doubt she's still unalive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}